// Multilevel Master Listening — Part 3
window.LISTENING_L3=[{"n":1,"q":"You will hear people speaking about habits they find difficult to control.","qu":"Odamlar nazorat qilish qiyin bo'lgan odatlari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"speaking about habits they find difficult to control.","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"arriving late for everything","u":"hamma joyga kechikish"},{"l":"B","t":"doing too much exercise","u":"haddan tashqari ko'p sport bilan shug'ullanish"},{"l":"C","t":"buying unnecessary items","u":"keraksiz narsalar sotib olish"},{"l":"D","t":"watching too much television","u":"juda ko'p televizor ko'rish"},{"l":"E","t":"spending too much time online","u":"internetda juda ko'p vaqt o'tkazish"},{"l":"F","t":"oversleeping","u":"ko'p uxlash (uxlab qolish)"}],"dur":222.3,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":13.69,"en":49.47,"ev":"I log on to one of my favourite sites… soon I've filled up my basket with all kinds of things (whether I actually need any of them is irrelevant)… it ends up in the bin.","uz":"Sevimli saytlarimdan biriga kiraman… tezda savatchamni har xil narsalar bilan to'ldiraman (ularning menga kerakmi-yo'qligi muhim emas)… oxiri axlat qutisiga tushadi.","why":"\"Whether I need them is irrelevant\" — keraksiz narsalar sotib olish (C). Internet ham tilga olinadi, lekin muammo — xarid.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":54.39,"en":93.79,"ev":"Getting up around 7 isn't easy when you've been up till 2 the night before, but somehow I never managed to log off until then. There are just so many great sites…","uz":"Kechasi soat 2 gacha o'tirsangiz, 7 da turish oson emas, lekin men hech qachon undan oldin internetdan chiqa olmasdim. Ajoyib saytlar juda ko'p…","why":"\"Never managed to log off\" — internetda ko'p vaqt (E). Shopping — kamdan-kam sotib oladi; ishga kechikmaydi (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":98.74,"en":137.66,"ev":"I don't feel right if I'm not working on my fitness level and the possible long-term effects of that are beginning to concern me.","uz":"Jismoniy tayyorgarligim ustida ishlamasam, o'zimni yaxshi his qilmayman va buning uzoq muddatli oqibatlari meni xavotirga sola boshladi.","why":"Doim mashq qilish va bundan xavotir — B (too much exercise). Kech yotish — oqibat, asosiy odat emas.","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":142.55,"en":178.14,"ev":"It was on all the time in my parents' home, and it's like that here in my own flat… I'm totally hooked on the same kinds of series.","uz":"Ota-onamning uyida u doim yoniq edi, o'z kvartiramda ham shunday… bir xil seriallarga butunlay mukkasidan ketganman.","why":"\"On all the time… hooked on series\" — televizor (D). Internet va sport — tengdoshlari haqida (tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":183.06,"en":222.27,"ev":"Then I end up literally running to wherever I'm going, always the last to turn up, and also often the most stressed one too.","uz":"Keyin borishim kerak bo'lgan joyga yugurib boraman, doim eng oxirgi yetib kelaman va ko'pincha eng asabiylashgan ham men bo'laman.","why":"\"Always the last to turn up\" — doim kechikish (A). Erta turishga urinishi — uxlab qolish emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.26,"e":8.54,"t":"will hear five short extracts in which people talk about habits they find difficult to control."},{"k":"h","s":13.69,"e":13.69,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":16.34,"e":24.03,"t":"It starts as soon as I get home in the early evening. I have a quick snack and then log on to one of my favourite sites."},{"s":24.5,"e":32.7,"t":"soon I filled up my basket with all kinds of things (whether I actually need any of them is irrelevant) and then head for the checkout."},{"s":33.3,"e":35.26,"t":"It's also quick and easy."},{"s":35.86,"e":49.47,"t":"Sometimes I'm watching TV and there's an ad for a tasty looking ready meal and I'll log back on for a minute and order that too. Though when it's actually delivered it usually turns out to be just junk food and it ends up in the bin."},{"k":"h","s":54.39,"e":54.39,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":57.14,"e":62.17,"t":"I first realized something wasn't quite right when I kept falling asleep at all hours of the day."},{"s":62.78,"e":70.11,"t":"Getting up around 7 isn't easy when you've been up till 2 the night before, but somehow I never managed to log off until then."},{"s":70.65,"e":78.43,"t":"There are just so many great sites, particularly news and sports, and also shopping, though I rarely end up buying anything."},{"s":79.03,"e":87.61,"t":"According to a quiz I did, I do seem to have an addiction. Though, compared to things like overeating, I don't think it's a particularly harmful one."},{"s":88.15,"e":93.79,"t":"I mean, I'm quite fit and unlike some of my colleagues, I always get to the office on time."},{"k":"h","s":98.74,"e":98.74,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":101.53,"e":104.35,"t":"I always feel I have to be doing something."},{"s":105.27,"e":112.57,"t":"don't feel right if I'm not working on my fitness level and the possible long-term effects of that are beginning to concern me."},{"s":113.24,"e":120.19,"t":"It also affects my life right now in various ways. For instance, I always go to bed late and get up early."},{"s":120.92,"e":130.72,"t":"also need bigger meals than less active people. And although I always choose food that's good for me, it can be rather expensive and hard to find in the shops."},{"s":131.42,"e":137.66,"t":"At least so, the fact that I go everywhere around town on foot means that I'm never held up by traffic."},{"k":"h","s":142.55,"e":142.55,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":145.3,"e":156.41,"t":"It was on all the time in my parents' home, and it's like that here in my own flat. Usually the same channel too, because to tell the truth I'm totally hooked on the same kinds of series."},{"s":156.95,"e":166.91,"t":"It's odd in a way because most people of my generation spend all their time on the internet or, in the case of the fitter ones, doing sport every evening and weekend."},{"s":167.45,"e":178.14,"t":"I know my own lifestyle isn't particularly healthy, though at least nowadays I'm up reasonably early, unlike back in my student days when I often had trouble getting out of bed before noon."},{"k":"h","s":183.06,"e":183.06,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":185.98,"e":193.18,"t":"It's always my intention to set off in plenty of time, but somehow there always seems to be something that holds me up."},{"s":193.62,"e":201.12,"t":"It may be a job that needs finishing off, an email that has to be answered, or even a TV programme that hasn't quite ended."},{"s":201.82,"e":210.24,"t":"Then I end up literally running to wherever I'm going, always the last to turn up, and also often the most stressed one too."},{"s":211.06,"e":216.83,"t":"I tried getting up earlier in the morning so that I have more hours in the day to get everything done."},{"s":217.37,"e":222.27,"t":"But the lack of sleep just makes me feel tired later on and doesn't help at all."}]},{"n":2,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people talk about deciding to take up new interests. What is the reason each speaker gives?","qu":"Odamlar yangi qiziqish (mashg'ulot) boshlash haqida gapiradi. Har birining sababi nima?","topic":"short extracts in which people talk about deciding to take up new interests","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"to help other people","u":"boshqalarga yordam berish uchun"},{"l":"B","t":"to make some money","u":"biroz pul topish uchun"},{"l":"C","t":"to make a change from their work","u":"ishdan chalg'ish (o'zgarish) uchun"},{"l":"D","t":"to meet new people","u":"yangi odamlar bilan tanishish uchun"},{"l":"E","t":"to try to win a prize","u":"sovrin yutishga urinish uchun"},{"l":"F","t":"to overcome a fear","u":"qo'rquvni yengish uchun"}],"dur":228.7,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":14.36,"en":51.23,"ev":"When I made my mind up to do badminton, it was far more about socialising than exercising, especially as I'd only recently moved to this part of town and I hardly knew anyone.","uz":"Badmintonga qaror qilganimda, gap mashqdan ko'ra ko'proq odamlar bilan muloqotda edi, ayniqsa shaharning bu qismiga yaqinda ko'chib kelganim va deyarli hech kimni tanimasligim uchun.","why":"\"Socialising… hardly knew anyone\" — yangi odamlar bilan tanishish (D). Chempionat — \"no chance of winning\", demak E emas.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":56.15,"en":99.52,"ev":"Last year I found that I was increasingly getting into financial difficulties, so I began to study the way electronic devices work and how to repair them… I've now paid off nearly all my debts.","uz":"O'tgan yili moliyaviy qiyinchiliklarga tobora ko'proq duch kela boshladim, shuning uchun elektron qurilmalarni ta'mirlashni o'rgana boshladim… endi qarzlarimning deyarli hammasini to'ladim.","why":"\"Financial difficulties… paid off my debts\" — pul topish (B). Yangi odamlar — benzin shoxobchasidagi ish haqida.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":104.73,"en":145.5,"ev":"For years I'd been so scared of heights that some people used to make fun of me. So one day I decided to do something about it.","uz":"Yillar davomida balandlikdan shunchalik qo'rqardimki, ba'zilar ustimdan kulishardi. Shuning uchun bir kuni bu bilan nimadir qilishga qaror qildim.","why":"\"Scared of heights… do something about it\" — qo'rquvni yengish (F). Do'stlar orttirgani — natija, sabab emas.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":150.42,"en":183.13,"ev":"What had initially attracted me to it was that it offered a contrast in every respect to my day job as a cab driver in a noisy, polluted city centre.","uz":"Meni bunga dastlab jalb qilgan narsa — u shovqinli, ifloslangan shahar markazidagi taksi haydovchiligi ishimdan har jihatdan farq qilishi edi.","why":"\"A contrast to my day job\" — ishdan o'zgarish (C). Yaxshi mashq ekani — \"bonus\".","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":188.12,"en":228.25,"ev":"The old lady next door asked me to look after her garden while she was away… I felt I'd done something really worthwhile. So I then offered to garden for other neighbours in their 80s and 90s… I always refused to accept it.","uz":"Qo'shni kampir yo'qligida bog'iga qarab turishimni so'radi… o'zimni haqiqatan foydali ish qilgandek his qildim. Keyin 80–90 yoshli boshqa qo'shnilarga ham bog'ida yordam berishni taklif qildim… pul taklif qilishsa ham, doim rad etardim.","why":"Keksalarga bepul yordam — boshqalarga yordam (A). Pul — rad etgan (B emas), sovrin — boshqalar haqida (E emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.74,"e":9.98,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people talk about deciding to take up new interests."},{"k":"h","s":14.36,"e":14.36,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.21,"e":32.22,"t":"I've always been a keen swimmer and that keeps me in good shape. So when I made my mind up to do badminton, it was far more about socialising than exercising, especially as I'd only recently moved to this part of town and I hardly knew anyone."},{"s":32.86,"e":42.05,"t":"I hadn't realised though just how competitive badminton can be so much so that I've now been invited to take part in a local championship"},{"s":42.55,"e":48.51,"t":"I've got no chance of winning it, or even coming close. And to be honest, I'm not really bothered about that."},{"s":48.98,"e":51.23,"t":"But it might be fun so I think I'll give it a"},{"k":"h","s":56.15,"e":56.15,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":58.87,"e":76.16,"t":"I work part-time in a petrol station, which in some ways is quite a pleasant job, but last year I found that I was increasingly getting into financial difficulties, so I began to study the way electronic devices work and how to repair them."},{"s":77.14,"e":84.22,"t":"Sound that fascinating? And eventually I felt confident enough to place an online ad offering my services."},{"s":84.76,"e":89.47,"t":"I've got loads of replies and I've now paid off nearly all my debts."},{"s":90.23,"e":99.52,"t":"I've thought of giving up my job at the petrol station, but I think I'd miss meeting different people every day if I worked entirely from home."},{"k":"h","s":104.73,"e":104.73,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":107.64,"e":117.12,"t":"For years I'd been so scared of heights that some people used to make fun of me. So one day I decided to do something about it."},{"s":117.59,"e":119.1,"t":"Go rock climbing!"},{"s":119.77,"e":125.12,"t":"Feeling that if I could do that, I'd be able to do anything. I joined a local club."},{"s":125.82,"e":131.61,"t":"On my first day I was surprised to find there were two other people who joined for the same reason."},{"s":132.06,"e":133.89,"t":"and we soon became friends."},{"s":134.49,"e":145.5,"t":"Together we got fitter and stronger and encouraged each other to keep going until by the end of the year we felt unconcerned about tackling the most challenging of climbs."},{"k":"h","s":150.42,"e":150.42,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":153.18,"e":161.53,"t":"I never imagined that going horse riding could be such good exercise until I'd spent a weekend trekking in the mountains with friends."},{"s":162.17,"e":174.62,"t":"That was something of a bonus, really, because what had initially attracted me to it was that it offered a contrast in every respect to my day job as a cab driver in a noisy, polluted city centre."},{"s":175.51,"e":183.13,"t":"And although it's certainly not the cheapest of activities, I find it so relaxing that I always feel it's worth every penny."},{"k":"h","s":188.12,"e":188.12,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":191.16,"e":197.95,"t":"Gardening had always seemed to me as just a way of passing the time of doing something completely different from office work."},{"s":198.46,"e":204.09,"t":"or perhaps even for the really keen of winning a prize for the largest home-grown vegetable."},{"s":204.79,"e":212.06,"t":"So it was only by chance that I became interested in it when the old lady next door asked me to look after her garden while she was away."},{"s":212.82,"e":219.07,"t":"On her return, she was so delighted by my efforts that I felt I'd done something really worthwhile."},{"s":219.67,"e":225.85,"t":"So I then offered to garden for other neighbours in their 80s and 90s. They sometimes offered me money."},{"s":226.33,"e":228.25,"t":"but I always refused to accept it."}]},{"n":3,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about difficult situations they have been in. What did each speaker do?","qu":"Odamlar boshidan kechirgan qiyin vaziyatlar haqida gapiradi. Har biri nima qilgan?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about difficult situations they have ","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I contacted the emergency services.","u":"Favqulodda xizmatlarga qo'ng'iroq qildim."},{"l":"B","t":"I was tempted to ignore what had happened.","u":"Bo'lgan voqeaga e'tibor bermaslik xohishi paydo bo'ldi."},{"l":"C","t":"I did what I had been trained to do.","u":"O'rgatilganimdek harakat qildim."},{"l":"D","t":"I followed someone else's advice.","u":"Boshqa birovning maslahatiga amal qildim."},{"l":"E","t":"I made a decision I later regretted.","u":"Keyin afsuslanganim qarorni qabul qildim."},{"l":"F","t":"I helped people reach safety.","u":"Odamlarga xavfsiz joyga yetib olishga yordam berdim."}],"dur":236.0,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":14.14,"en":52.13,"ev":"I took out my phone to call the rescue services or the police, but there was no signal… I ran back and shouted to the crew to row towards it as hard as they could… the waves pushed their boat into the bay where they were able to take shelter.","uz":"Qutqaruv xizmati yoki politsiyaga qo'ng'iroq qilish uchun telefonimni oldim, lekin aloqa yo'q edi… Ortga yugurib, ekipajga u tomonga bor kuchi bilan eshkak eshishni qichqirdim… to'lqinlar qayiqni ko'rfazga surdi va ular panoh topishdi.","why":"Odamlarni xavfsiz joyga olib chiqishga yordam berdi (F). Favqulodda xizmatga qo'ng'iroq qila olmadi — A tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":57.05,"en":94.4,"ev":"I didn't want to bother my host family by asking them to pick me up. So I set off on foot… When I eventually reached the house, the family said how worried they'd been and asked why I hadn't phoned. By then I wished I had.","uz":"Mezbon oilani bezovta qilib, meni olib ketishlarini so'ragim kelmadi. Shuning uchun piyoda yo'lga chiqdim… Nihoyat uyga yetganimda, oila qanchalik xavotirlanganini aytib, nega qo'ng'iroq qilmaganimni so'rashdi. O'shanda qo'ng'iroq qilmaganimdan afsuslandim.","why":"\"By then I wished I had\" — keyin afsuslangan qaror (E).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":99.38,"en":139.87,"ev":"I realised straight away I'd been overcharged, but it was only by a small amount, and my first thought was to forget about it as I was in a hurry.","uz":"Darhol ortiqcha pul olinganini angladim, lekin miqdori kichik edi va shoshayotganim uchun birinchi fikrim buni unutib yuborish edi.","why":"\"My first thought was to forget about it\" — e'tibor bermaslik xohishi (B).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":144.76,"en":190.24,"ev":"I asked him which way we should go, and he said we'd taken a wrong turning at the bridge. So, we headed back the way we'd come, turned left by the river instead of right…","uz":"Undan qaysi tomonga borishimiz kerakligini so'radim, u ko'prikda noto'g'ri burilganimizni aytdi. Shunda kelgan yo'limizdan qaytib, daryo yonida o'ngga emas, chapga burildik…","why":"Cho'ponning maslahatiga amal qilishdi (D). Mountain Rescue'ga qo'ng'iroq qilinmadi — A tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":195.16,"en":233.82,"ev":"I remembered what I'd been taught as a nurse, so I kept it still, checking to see if it was broken… I decided against calling an ambulance.","uz":"Hamshira sifatida o'rgatilganlarimni esladim: oyog'imni qimirlatmay, singan-sinmaganini tekshirdim… tez yordam chaqirmaslikka qaror qildim.","why":"\"What I'd been taught as a nurse\" — o'rgatilganidek (C). Tez yordam chaqirilmadi (A emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.12,"e":10.11,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about difficult situations they have been in."},{"k":"h","s":14.14,"e":14.14,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":16.79,"e":25.92,"t":"There was a storm blowing as I walked along the cliffs and down below I noticed a rowing boat being thrown about by the huge waves."},{"s":26.58,"e":31.97,"t":"took out my phone to call the rescue services or the police, but there was no signal."},{"s":32.63,"e":46.91,"t":"If the boat had hit the rocks, it would have been smashed to pieces. So I ran along the cliff top until I came to a small bay. I ran back and shouted to the crew to row towards it as hard as they could, and eventually they managed it."},{"s":47.48,"e":52.13,"t":"There the waves pushed their boat into the bay where they were able to take shelter."},{"k":"h","s":57.05,"e":57.05,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":59.77,"e":67.26,"t":"It was my first night out in that city and when I saw the last bus home disappearing round the corner I knew I had a problem."},{"s":67.86,"e":70.05,"t":"It was cold and I couldn't afford a taxi."},{"s":70.55,"e":78.91,"t":"but I didn't want to bother my host family by asking them to pick me up. So I set off on foot, telling myself it'd only take me an hour or so."},{"s":79.64,"e":82.37,"t":"Four hours later I was still walking."},{"s":82.94,"e":85.53,"t":"I was soaked through and my hands were frozen."},{"s":86.36,"e":92.45,"t":"When I eventually reached the house, the family said how worried they'd been and asked why I hadn't phoned."},{"s":93.14,"e":94.4,"t":"By then I wished I had."},{"k":"h","s":99.38,"e":99.38,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":102.23,"e":111.01,"t":"I realised straight away I'd been overcharged, but it was only by a small amount, and my first thought was to forget about it as I was in a hurry."},{"s":111.67,"e":117.02,"t":"Then I noticed the assistant glance at me, and somehow I knew it had been deliberate."},{"s":117.62,"e":121.34,"t":"I gently pointed out the error but he became quite aggressive."},{"s":121.98,"e":130.85,"t":"Not wanting to get into a row about it, I asked to speak to the manager and when she came over I explained that I hadn't been given the correct change."},{"s":131.32,"e":137.63,"t":"the assistant angrily denied this, but the manager pointed to a security camera right above us."},{"s":138.1,"e":139.87,"t":"He immediately gave me my money."},{"k":"h","s":144.76,"e":144.76,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":147.54,"e":159.33,"t":"Carlos, Alfonso and I had been camping in the mountains, and it was time to leave. Just then, a dense mist descended and soon we realised we were completely lost."},{"s":159.8,"e":165.98,"t":"I was in favour of keeping going along the path, while Carlos suggested heading downhill."},{"s":166.52,"e":169.95,"t":"Alfonso, though, wanted to phone Mountain Rescue for help."},{"s":170.62,"e":174.43,"t":"Two of them had just started arguing when a shepherd appeared."},{"s":174.97,"e":190.24,"t":"I asked him which way we should go, and he said we'd taken a wrong turning at the bridge. So, we headed back the way we'd come, turned left by the river instead of right, and within twenty minutes we'd reached the village."},{"k":"h","s":195.16,"e":195.16,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":198.04,"e":204.51,"t":"I was doing a cross-country run when suddenly I tripped and fell, feeling a sharp pain in my ankle."},{"s":205.08,"e":210.56,"t":"As I lay there, I wondered whether I'd be able to stand on it, maybe even carry on running."},{"s":211.1,"e":217.31,"t":"but I remembered what I'd been taught as a nurse, so I kept it still, checking to see if it was broken."},{"s":217.85,"e":226.3,"t":"It didn't seem to be, so I decided against calling an ambulance, but I didn't want to take any chances, so I phoned my sister."},{"s":226.81,"e":233.82,"t":"She immediately offered to come and collect me. And within 15 minutes, she was able to help me to the car and take me home."}]},{"n":4,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about cities they have visited. What opinion does each person give about the city?","qu":"Besh kishi borgan shaharlari haqida gapiradi. Har biri shahar haqida qanday fikr bildiradi?","topic":"different people talking about cities they have visited","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"It was exactly as I had imagined.","u":"U men tasavvur qilgandek edi."},{"l":"B","t":"It is not as good as it used to be.","u":"Avvalgidek yaxshi emas."},{"l":"C","t":"It is hard to find your way around it.","u":"Unda yo'l topish qiyin."},{"l":"D","t":"It is overrated.","u":"Uni haddan tashqari maqtashadi."},{"l":"E","t":"It can get too crowded.","u":"U juda gavjum bo'lib ketishi mumkin."},{"l":"F","t":"It was even better than I expected.","u":"Kutganimdan ham yaxshiroq edi."}],"dur":231.5,"items":[{"a":"A","ps":12.34,"en":49.95,"ev":"You have this image of skyscrapers everywhere… And guess what? It was just like that. Everything I'd expected to find was there.","uz":"Hamma joyda osmono'par binolar bor deb tasavvur qilasiz… Va bilasizmi? Aynan shunday ekan. Kutgan hamma narsam o'sha yerda edi.","why":"\"It was just like that\" — tasavvur qilgandek (A).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":53.53,"en":97.5,"ev":"The place was packed and of course with the narrow streets it is famed for that makes movement difficult. I just shuffled along with everyone else…","uz":"Joy odamga liq to'la edi, mashhur tor ko'chalari tufayli yurish qiyin edi. Hamma bilan birga sudralib yurdim…","why":"\"Packed… busy times\" — gavjum bo'lishi mumkin (E).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":101.3,"en":143.2,"ev":"In fact, it not only lived up to my expectations, it exceeded them.","uz":"Aslida u nafaqat kutganlarimni oqladi, balki ulardan ham oshib ketdi.","why":"\"Exceeded them\" — kutganidan ham yaxshi (F).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":146.87,"en":185.37,"ev":"People had told me that it wasn't the same as it used to be… but I didn't see any evidence of that. What did strike me was how confusing it is… I was always getting lost there.","uz":"Odamlar u avvalgidek emasligini aytishgan edi… lekin men bunga dalil ko'rmadim. Meni hayratga solgani — qanchalik chalkashligi edi… doim adashib qolardim.","why":"\"Not as good as it used to be\" — rad etilgan (B tuzoq). Asosiy fikr — yo'l topish qiyin (C).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":189.14,"en":228.61,"ev":"You can't see what all the fuss is about… But I don't think it really deserves all the praise people give it.","uz":"Bu shov-shuv nimaga ekanini tushunmaysiz… Menimcha, u odamlar beradigan barcha maqtovlarga loyiq emas.","why":"\"Doesn't deserve all the praise\" — haddan tashqari maqtalgan (D).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.45,"e":7.45,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about cities they have visited."},{"k":"h","s":12.34,"e":12.34,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.48,"e":24.19,"t":"The place is always on TV and in films and in magazines and so you get a mental picture of what it's like even if you haven't been there."},{"s":24.82,"e":39.71,"t":"You have this image of skyscrapers everywhere. Streets full of traffic and people. Everyone rushing around, talking fast and leading busy lives. You think of it as having a real buzz. And guess what?"},{"s":40.22,"e":49.95,"t":"It was just like that. Everything I'd expected to find was there. In fact, it all seemed so familiar that it was as if I'd actually been there before."},{"k":"h","s":53.53,"e":53.53,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.6,"e":63.04,"t":"I discovered, after I'd been there, that you need to be really careful about when you choose to visit the place."},{"s":63.58,"e":66.56,"t":"There are very busy times and quieter times."},{"s":67.22,"e":72.77,"t":"Without realising it, I chose one of the busy times and wow was it busy!"},{"s":73.37,"e":80.03,"t":"The place was packed and of course with the narrow streets it is famed for that makes movement difficult."},{"s":80.63,"e":86.65,"t":"I just shuffled along with everyone else, going at their pace, so I didn't manage to see much."},{"s":87.22,"e":91.29,"t":"There's a great atmosphere there. And of course it looks wonderful."},{"s":92.38,"e":94.43,"t":"Done with a bit more room to move."},{"s":95.03,"e":97.5,"t":"so I guess I didn't see it at its best."},{"k":"h","s":101.3,"e":101.3,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":104.54,"e":111.81,"t":"Everyone I've met who's been there says what a fantastic place it is, and I was expecting something really special."},{"s":112.38,"e":113.69,"t":"and I wasn't disappointed."},{"s":114.2,"e":119.29,"t":"Although I must say the picture I'd had of it in my mind didn't turn out to be totally accurate."},{"s":119.8,"e":125.09,"t":"In fact, it not only lived up to my expectations, it exceeded them."},{"s":125.94,"e":132.19,"t":"People always associate it with its famous buildings, but it was the less well-known places that struck me."},{"s":132.98,"e":139.13,"t":"Every little street, especially away from the tourist areas, there was something fascinating to see."},{"s":139.77,"e":143.2,"t":"It's those little streets that were really memorable for me."},{"k":"h","s":146.87,"e":146.87,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":149.91,"e":154.62,"t":"I'd been looking forward to going there for a long time and I finally managed it."},{"s":155.06,"e":160.77,"t":"I wasn't quite sure what to expect because people had told me that it wasn't the same as it used to be."},{"s":161.37,"e":166.81,"t":"Apparently, it's become much more touristy recently, but I didn't see any evidence of that."},{"s":167.38,"e":170.37,"t":"What did strike me was how confusing it is."},{"s":170.87,"e":176.41,"t":"Half the time I didn't know where I was and getting from A to B was always problematic."},{"s":177.05,"e":185.37,"t":"I normally have a good sense of direction, but I was always getting lost there. Once I did get to where I was trying to go, it was worth it though."},{"k":"h","s":189.14,"e":189.14,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":192.22,"e":199.33,"t":"People always talk about what a marvellous place it is and so eventually I decided to go and see for myself."},{"s":200.09,"e":206.05,"t":"It has the reputation of being a place you never forget and lots of people say it's their favourite city."},{"s":207.13,"e":208.13,"t":"Having been there..."},{"s":208.73,"e":210.53,"t":"You can't see what all the fuss is about"},{"s":211.26,"e":217.18,"t":"Sure, the places that you see pictures of all the time or that you see in films are impressive enough."},{"s":217.75,"e":218.85,"t":"but I've seen better."},{"s":219.61,"e":228.61,"t":"It's a pleasant enough place and it's certainly popular with tourists. There were plenty of them there. But I don't think it really deserves all the praise people give it."}]},{"n":5,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about the reasons why they became very successful. What reason does each person give for their success?","qu":"Besh kishi muvaffaqiyatga erishgani sabablari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about the reasons why they became very successful","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"natural ability","u":"tug'ma qobiliyat"},{"l":"B","t":"constant good luck","u":"doimiy omad"},{"l":"C","t":"careful planning","u":"puxta rejalashtirish"},{"l":"D","t":"peer pressure","u":"tengdoshlar bosimi"},{"l":"E","t":"determination to improve","u":"yaxshilanishga qat'iyat"},{"l":"F","t":"lack of competition","u":"raqobat yo'qligi"}],"dur":201.7,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":14.49,"en":49.02,"ev":"I guess it was all a case of simply being in the right place at the right time. I got my first job by pure chance and then one job offer followed another.","uz":"O'ylashimcha, hammasi shunchaki kerakli vaqtda kerakli joyda bo'lganim tufayli edi. Birinchi ishimni tasodifan topdim, keyin ish takliflari ketma-ket kela boshladi.","why":"\"By pure chance… one offer followed another\" — doimiy omad (B). \"No grand scheme\" — rejalashtirmagan (C emas).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":52.7,"en":89.21,"ev":"When I started the company, the market was wide open really and hardly anyone was doing what I was doing… There wasn't much to compare it with, so it did okay.","uz":"Kompaniyani ochganimda bozor deyarli bo'sh edi, men qilayotgan ishni deyarli hech kim qilmasdi… Solishtiradigan narsa kam edi, shuning uchun yaxshi ketdi.","why":"\"Hardly anyone was doing what I was doing\" — raqobat yo'qligi (F). U o'zini \"brilliant\" demaydi (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":93.24,"en":123.74,"ev":"I've never really had to work at it. It just seems to be something I was born with.","uz":"Bu ustida hech qachon ter to'kishim kerak bo'lmagan. Bu menda tug'ma bor narsa shekilli.","why":"\"Something I was born with\" — tug'ma qobiliyat (A).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":127.58,"en":163.26,"ev":"I had it all worked out from the very beginning, every detail of what I was going to do and how I was going to do it.","uz":"Boshidanoq hammasini — nima qilishim va qanday qilishimning har bir tafsilotini rejalashtirib qo'ygandim.","why":"\"Had it all worked out… every detail\" — puxta reja (C). Maslahatlarni rad etgan — D (peer pressure) emas.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":167.26,"en":198.37,"ev":"I may not be the most talented player there's ever been, but I've put a tremendous amount of effort in to be as good as I can be… That's just made me try even harder.","uz":"Balki men eng iqtidorli o'yinchi emasdirman, lekin imkon qadar yaxshi bo'lish uchun juda katta kuch sarfladim… Bu meni yanada ko'proq harakat qilishga undadi.","why":"\"Tremendous effort… try even harder\" — yaxshilanishga qat'iyat (E). Tanqidchilar — bosim emas, turtki.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.38,"e":9.63,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about the reasons why they became very successful."},{"k":"h","s":14.49,"e":14.49,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.62,"e":22.14,"t":"I just fell into my television career really. There was no grand scheme."},{"s":22.97,"e":27.33,"t":"I guess it was all a case of simply being in the right place at the right time."},{"s":28.02,"e":32.83,"t":"I got my first job by pure chance and then one job offer followed another."},{"s":33.53,"e":35.9,"t":"I didn't set out to get where I am today."},{"s":36.34,"e":41.47,"t":"And I'm sure there are plenty of people who could do the job as well as, if not better than me."},{"s":42.26,"e":49.02,"t":"People tell me they like what I do, and that's great. But I'd probably be just as happy if the whole thing hadn't happened."},{"k":"h","s":52.7,"e":52.7,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":55.83,"e":61.41,"t":"When I started the company, the market was wide open really and hardly anyone was doing what I was doing."},{"s":62.39,"e":66.14,"t":"Actually, the product I was offering in the early days wasn't all that good."},{"s":66.94,"e":69.5,"t":"There wasn't much to compare it with, so it did okay."},{"s":70.46,"e":72.61,"t":"The fact is, it was a good idea."},{"s":73.08,"e":76.32,"t":"and in business there's no substitute for a good idea."},{"s":77.14,"e":81.98,"t":"I'm not necessarily a brilliant businessman in terms of strategy and things like that."},{"s":82.46,"e":84.48,"t":"and sometimes I'm not sure what to do next."},{"s":85.21,"e":87.45,"t":"but I did have that great idea."},{"s":87.96,"e":89.21,"t":"so I've made my own look"},{"k":"h","s":93.24,"e":93.24,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":96.6,"e":101.34,"t":"The personal feeling is that in show business, talent will always get its reward."},{"s":102.04,"e":108.86,"t":"Even if you have to struggle on for years, which thankfully I didn't have to do, if you've got what it takes, you'll make it."},{"s":109.4,"e":114.24,"t":"Someone will spot you and give you a part if you're good enough. And that's exactly what happened to me."},{"s":115.0,"e":119.17,"t":"I've never really had to work at it. It just seems to be something I was born with."},{"s":119.83,"e":123.74,"t":"I've never thought of doing anything else, and fortunately I've never had to."},{"k":"h","s":127.58,"e":127.58,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":130.65,"e":139.01,"t":"There was no shortage of advice when I started my career as a singer. People told me how I should look, what sort of songs I should sing, all sorts of things."},{"s":139.58,"e":143.77,"t":"but I ignored them all and I'm glad I did because I've been proved right."},{"s":144.57,"e":151.45,"t":"I had it all worked out from the very beginning, every detail of what I was going to do and how I was going to do it."},{"s":151.93,"e":154.01,"t":"And it's all gone very smoothly."},{"s":154.68,"e":159.29,"t":"I knew what suited me and what would be popular and I followed my instincts on that."},{"s":159.9,"e":163.26,"t":"I haven't had to struggle at all. Everything's gone very well."},{"k":"h","s":167.26,"e":167.26,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":170.58,"e":174.27,"t":"To get to the top in my sport, I've had to make the most of what I've got."},{"s":175.13,"e":181.31,"t":"I may not be the most talented player there's ever been, but I've put a tremendous amount of effort in to be as good as I can be."},{"s":182.52,"e":185.28,"t":"And all along there have been people making comments about"},{"s":185.75,"e":186.88,"t":"How I'm not good enough"},{"s":187.7,"e":189.37,"t":"That's just made me try even harder."},{"s":190.3,"e":192.86,"t":"And I've exceeded my ambitions, really."},{"s":193.4,"e":198.37,"t":"I only wanted to be a good club player and I never imagined I'd make it into the national side."}]},{"n":6,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about what they discovered when they read autobiographies by famous people. What did each person discover?","qu":"Besh kishi mashhur odamlarning tarjimai hollarini o'qib nimani bilib olgani haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about what they discovered when they read autobiographi","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"He had a terrible life before becoming famous.","u":"Mashhur bo'lishidan oldin hayoti juda og'ir bo'lgan."},{"l":"B","t":"He is a nicer person than he appears to be.","u":"U ko'rinishidan ko'ra yoqimliroq odam."},{"l":"C","t":"He is exactly the same in private as he is in public.","u":"Shaxsiy hayotida ham omma oldidagidek."},{"l":"D","t":"He would have preferred a different career.","u":"U boshqa kasbni afzal ko'rgan bo'lardi."},{"l":"E","t":"He has a sad personal life.","u":"Uning shaxsiy hayoti g'amgin."},{"l":"F","t":"He feels that he is a very important person.","u":"U o'zini juda muhim odam deb hisoblaydi."},{"l":"G","t":"He believes family to be the most important thing.","u":"U oilani eng muhim narsa deb biladi."},{"l":"H","t":"He was very unkind to other people after he became famous.","u":"Mashhur bo'lgach, boshqalarga juda qo'pol bo'lgan."}],"dur":247.6,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":16.92,"en":63.42,"ev":"What struck me most was just how arrogant the man is… He seems to think they do, and that because he's been in a few successful films, people should listen to his views on everything.","uz":"Meni eng ko'p hayratga solgani — bu odamning qanchalik takabburligi… U bir nechta muvaffaqiyatli filmda o'ynagani uchun hamma uning har qanday masaladagi fikrini tinglashi kerak deb o'ylaydi.","why":"\"Arrogant… people should listen to his views\" — o'zini juda muhim deb biladi (F).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":67.29,"en":111.39,"ev":"From his public image on TV, I thought he was a ghastly person… So I was very surprised to find that he isn't actually like that at all… In reality, he's a decent person.","uz":"Televizordagi obraziga qarab, uni dahshatli odam deb o'ylardim… Aslida unaqa emasligini bilib, juda hayron qoldim… Haqiqatda u yaxshi inson.","why":"Ko'rinishidan yomon, aslida yaxshi — B. Oilani birinchi o'ringa qo'yishi ham aytiladi, lekin asosiy kashfiyot — u yoqimliroq odam (G tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":115.1,"en":156.29,"ev":"But he admits that after he made it to the top, he didn't treat them at all well… he says that he was really horrible to the people who were closest to him.","uz":"Lekin u cho'qqiga chiqqanidan keyin ularga umuman yaxshi munosabatda bo'lmaganini tan oladi… eng yaqin odamlariga juda yomon bo'lganini aytadi.","why":"\"After he made it to the top… horrible to people\" — mashhur bo'lgach qo'pol bo'lgan (H).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":160.76,"en":200.03,"ev":"With him it seems to be very much, what you see is what you get… there is no difference between his personality on stage and on screen and what he's like when he's not performing.","uz":"U bilan \"nimani ko'rsangiz, shu\": sahnadagi va ekrandagi shaxsiyati bilan chiqish qilmayotgandagi holati o'rtasida farq yo'q.","why":"\"No difference… on stage and… not performing\" — C. \"Comedians are sad people\" — bu yerda to'g'ri emas (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":203.58,"en":245.95,"ev":"He seems to have grown up in poverty with a family who didn't really care about him at all… It's hard to imagine how it could have been any worse.","uz":"U qashshoqlikda, unga umuman e'tibor bermaydigan oilada o'sgan ko'rinadi… Bundan yomonroq bo'lishini tasavvur qilish qiyin.","why":"\"Rags to riches… poverty\" — mashhur bo'lishidan oldin og'ir hayot (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.79,"e":11.2,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about what they discovered when they read autobiographies by famous people."},{"k":"h","s":16.92,"e":16.92,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":20.7,"e":24.29,"t":"me most was just how arrogant the man is."},{"s":24.89,"e":30.27,"t":"I mean he's a fine actor and I really like everything he's been in. That's why I bought the book."},{"s":31.03,"e":35.45,"t":"But that doesn't mean that his opinions on politics and the world really matter."},{"s":36.12,"e":45.21,"t":"He seems to think they do, and that because he's been in a few successful films, people should listen to his views on everything and take them seriously."},{"s":46.23,"e":51.23,"t":"Actually, he talks a lot of rubbish about all that, and that really irritated me."},{"s":52.18,"e":57.09,"t":"wanted to read about his early life and struggles, how he got to the top and all that."},{"s":57.66,"e":63.42,"t":"he hardly mentions that, or anything about his private life. It's really put me off him.\""},{"k":"h","s":67.29,"e":67.29,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":70.68,"e":76.7,"t":"I got the book because a friend recommended it, not because I was particularly interested in the man."},{"s":77.18,"e":82.69,"t":"In fact, from his public image on TV, I thought he was a ghastly person."},{"s":83.16,"e":88.89,"t":"self-important, fiercely ambitious and not at all likeable as Harry appears to me."},{"s":89.43,"e":94.59,"t":"So I was very surprised to find that he isn't actually like that at all."},{"s":95.29,"e":97.44,"t":"It's just for public consumption."},{"s":98.04,"e":103.74,"t":"In reality, he's a decent person who puts family and friendship first."},{"s":104.34,"e":108.45,"t":"and he comes across as the sort of person you could have a pleasant chat with."},{"s":109.02,"e":111.39,"t":"He's certainly gone up in my estimation."},{"k":"h","s":115.1,"e":115.1,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":118.26,"e":129.12,"t":"His family seemed to have played a very important part in his career, and he talks about how much help they gave him in the early days, paying for coaches and taking him to tournaments all over the place."},{"s":129.66,"e":135.17,"t":"But he admits that after he made it to the top, he didn't treat them at all well."},{"s":135.96,"e":144.7,"t":"He talks about how much pressure he was under once he became a champion and how he struggled to deal with all the attention from the media and fans."},{"s":145.62,"e":148.06,"t":"We always saw him smiling in victory."},{"s":148.5,"e":152.7,"t":"But he says that he was really horrible to the people who were closest to him."},{"s":153.56,"e":156.29,"t":"It just shows that appearances can be deceptive."},{"k":"h","s":160.76,"e":160.76,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":164.06,"e":164.67,"t":"Of course."},{"s":165.11,"e":168.7,"t":"People always say that comedians are actually very sad people."},{"s":169.14,"e":171.1,"t":"But that doesn't seem to be the case here."},{"s":171.61,"e":175.26,"t":"With him it seems to be very much, what you see is what you get."},{"s":175.96,"e":179.71,"t":"the books full of really funny stories and he makes fun of everything."},{"s":180.31,"e":185.12,"t":"from some of the things that happened during his childhood to the big issues in the world today."},{"s":186.04,"e":191.81,"t":"He seems to have come from a very peculiar family and his descriptions of them are really amusing."},{"s":192.57,"e":200.03,"t":"You get the impression that there is no difference between his personality on stage and on screen and what he's like when he's not performing."},{"k":"h","s":203.58,"e":203.58,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":206.84,"e":217.76,"t":"It's quite an uplifting story really, a real rags to riches one. Of course I knew all about his enormous success as a businessman, but I didn't know anything about his background."},{"s":218.26,"e":225.95,"t":"It certainly wasn't a privileged one, and he seems to have grown up in poverty with a family who didn't really care about him at all."},{"s":226.55,"e":231.87,"t":"the way he describes his childhood. It's hard to imagine how it could have been any worse."},{"s":232.44,"e":240.19,"t":"So the fact that he managed to go from that to such incredible success and wealth makes for a really interesting story."},{"s":240.76,"e":245.95,"t":"You don't get much of an idea of the real person, but the story is great."}]},{"n":7,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about how they felt when they received an award. How did each person feel?","qu":"Besh kishi mukofot olganda o'zini qanday his qilgani haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about how they felt when they received an award","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"relieved","u":"yengil tortgan"},{"l":"B","t":"surprised","u":"hayron qolgan"},{"l":"C","t":"proud","u":"faxrlangan"},{"l":"D","t":"exhausted","u":"juda charchagan"},{"l":"E","t":"grateful","u":"minnatdor"},{"l":"F","t":"confused","u":"dovdiragan, tushunmagan"},{"l":"G","t":"worried","u":"xavotirda"},{"l":"H","t":"indifferent","u":"befarq"}],"dur":227.2,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":14.68,"en":55.42,"ev":"The main thing in my mind was all the people who had helped me along the way… I knew that without them I would never have won it.","uz":"Xayolimdagi asosiy narsa — yo'lda menga yordam bergan barcha odamlar edi… Ularsiz hech qachon yuta olmasligimni bilardim.","why":"Yordam berganlarni o'ylagan — minnatdor (E). \"Thrilled\" ham bor, lekin asosiysi — minnatdorlik.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":59.06,"en":95.77,"ev":"All I could think about was how well I'd done. Me, the best… it was all thanks to my own efforts… I just felt so good about myself and what I'd managed to achieve.","uz":"Faqat qanchalik yaxshi natija ko'rsatganim haqida o'ylardim. Men — eng zo'r… hammasi o'z mehnatim tufayli edi… o'zimdan va erishganlarimdan juda mamnun edim.","why":"\"Felt so good about myself… big-headed\" — faxr (C).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":99.48,"en":135.07,"ev":"So when my name was announced, I was just glad that it was over… All the pressure came off me in a moment.","uz":"Ismim e'lon qilinganda, shunchaki hammasi tugaganidan xursand bo'ldim… Bir zumda butun bosim ustimdan tushdi.","why":"\"Glad that it was over… pressure came off\" — yengil tortish (A).","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":138.71,"en":179.93,"ev":"As I accepted the award, I was wondering if it would be all downhill from there. Would I be able to keep it up and stay at the top?","uz":"Mukofotni olayotganda, bundan keyin hammasi pastga ketmasmikan deb o'ylardim. Cho'qqida qola olarmikanman?","why":"Kelajakdan xavotir — G. \"Overcome with joy\" — aksincha bo'lgan.","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":183.58,"en":222.46,"ev":"I put in so much effort to win it… that I was completely worn out… I'd used up all my energy… and was totally drained.","uz":"Uni yutish uchun shunchalik ko'p kuch sarfladimki… butunlay holdan toydim… bor kuchimni sarflab, mutlaqo charchagan edim.","why":"\"Worn out… totally drained\" — juda charchagan (D). \"Wasn't totally surprised\" — B emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.5,"e":6.33,"t":"You will hear five different people"},{"s":6.81,"e":9.69,"t":"talking about how they felt when they received an award."},{"k":"h","s":14.68,"e":14.68,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.66,"e":21.5,"t":"When I won the Best Actor Award, it was an extraordinary moment."},{"s":22.23,"e":28.7,"t":"There had been so many occasions when I thought I might win an award, only to find that someone else got it instead."},{"s":29.34,"e":31.65,"t":"So when I finally got it, I was thrilled."},{"s":32.57,"e":37.63,"t":"It was a fantastic personal achievement, but in fact the main thing in my mind..."},{"s":38.36,"e":41.47,"t":"all the people who had helped me along the way."},{"s":42.23,"e":46.43,"t":"I thought about all of them and all the help they'd given me."},{"s":47.03,"e":48.64,"t":"I knew that without them."},{"s":49.08,"e":50.37,"t":"I would never have won it."},{"s":51.19,"e":55.42,"t":"and I mentioned as many of them as I could in the time available."},{"k":"h","s":59.06,"e":59.06,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":62.49,"e":66.24,"t":"I guess that being voted Footballer of the Year went to my head."},{"s":67.0,"e":70.97,"t":"All I could think about was how well I'd done. Me, the best."},{"s":71.8,"e":77.12,"t":"I thought back to the early years of my career, which weren't so great, and I felt fantastic."},{"s":77.72,"e":82.91,"t":"and it was all thanks to my own efforts, not because anyone had handed me anything on a plate."},{"s":83.51,"e":87.81,"t":"It had been a long, hard journey, but I'd finally made it to the very top."},{"s":88.82,"e":91.29,"t":"I suppose it made me a bit big headed for a while."},{"s":91.8,"e":95.77,"t":"but I just felt so good about myself and what I'd managed to achieve."},{"k":"h","s":99.48,"e":99.48,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":102.62,"e":110.43,"t":"Everybody was expecting me to win the Writer of the Year award. I don't know why. There were plenty of other good contenders on the shortlist."},{"s":110.87,"e":118.11,"t":"Because everyone was predicting I'd win, I felt under pressure, as if it would be some kind of failure if I didn't win."},{"s":118.58,"e":135.07,"t":"It was a silly way to feel, I know, but I couldn't help it. So when my name was announced, I was just glad that it was over and I had in fact won it. All the pressure came off me in a moment and I just felt like sitting down quietly rather than celebrating."},{"k":"h","s":138.71,"e":138.71,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":141.82,"e":148.19,"t":"These awards mean a lot in the music business, and so winning the Best Singer Award was a great honor."},{"s":148.66,"e":156.48,"t":"I'd worked so hard over the years and I'd spent so long getting nowhere that it was amazing to have achieved this recognition."},{"s":157.27,"e":162.53,"t":"I thought I'd be absolutely overcome with joy, but in fact, the reverse happened."},{"s":163.51,"e":168.57,"t":"As I accepted the award, I was wondering if it would be all downhill from there."},{"s":169.11,"e":176.29,"t":"Would I be able to keep it up and stay at the top? Or would this be the high point, followed by a lot of low points?"},{"s":177.11,"e":179.93,"t":"couldn't put those thoughts out of my mind."},{"k":"h","s":183.58,"e":183.58,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":186.87,"e":193.09,"t":"I wasn't totally surprised when I got the Best Student Award because to be honest I felt that I deserved it."},{"s":193.62,"e":200.77,"t":"In fact, I put in so much effort to win it, doing far more work than anyone else, that I was completely worn out."},{"s":201.66,"e":207.65,"t":"been so important to me to win it that I dedicated myself completely to the task of winning it."},{"s":208.38,"e":209.85,"t":"so when I went up to collect it"},{"s":210.36,"e":215.1,"t":"I'd used up all my energy over the previous couple of weeks and was totally drained."},{"s":216.12,"e":222.46,"t":"barely put a few sentences together for my acceptance speech, though I managed to remember to thank a few people for their help."}]},{"n":8,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about their visit to a city. What did each speaker like most about the city they visited?","qu":"Odamlar borgan shaharlari haqida gapiradi. Har biriga shaharda eng ko'p nima yoqqan?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about their visit to a city","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"the efficiency of the public transport system","u":"jamoat transportining samaradorligi"},{"l":"B","t":"the natural beauty of the scenery","u":"manzaralarning tabiiy go'zalligi"},{"l":"C","t":"the variety of goods in the markets","u":"bozorlardagi mollarning xilma-xilligi"},{"l":"D","t":"the style of the architecture","u":"me'morchilik uslubi"},{"l":"E","t":"the well-designed plan of the city","u":"shaharning yaxshi rejalashtirilgani"},{"l":"F","t":"the helpfulness of the people","u":"odamlarning yordamga tayyorligi"},{"l":"G","t":"the range of leisure opportunities","u":"hordiq imkoniyatlarining xilma-xilligi"},{"l":"H","t":"the standard of the accommodation","u":"turar joy sifati"}],"dur":413.9,"items":[{"a":"G","ps":16.6,"en":52.77,"ev":"Anyway, we weren't short of things to do in the city. We were spoilt for choice.","uz":"Har holda, shaharda qiladigan ishimiz kam emas edi. Tanlash uchun imkoniyat juda ko'p edi.","why":"\"Spoilt for choice\" — hordiq imkoniyatlari xilma-xil (G). Tog'larga bormagan (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":56.44,"en":89.28,"ev":"We had a view of the lake which was a real treat. We were really impressed by the forests and mountains around the city.","uz":"Ko'l manzarasi bor edi — haqiqiy rohat. Shahar atrofidagi o'rmonlar va tog'lar bizni juda hayratga soldi.","why":"Tabiat manzarasi (B). Xona yaxshi emas edi (H emas), bozorlarga bormagan (C emas).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":92.98,"en":128.83,"ev":"The best bit was the ferries. I was really impressed that they were always on time… The trams were good too.","uz":"Eng yaxshisi — paromlar edi. Ular doim o'z vaqtida yurishi meni juda hayratga soldi… Tramvaylar ham yaxshi edi.","why":"\"Always on time\" — transport samaradorligi (A). Shahar rejasini tushunishmagan (E emas).","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":132.54,"en":169.05,"ev":"We decided to move around and try something different every couple of nights. That worked out really well and they were all excellent.","uz":"Har ikki kechada boshqa joyda turib ko'rishga qaror qildik. Bu juda yaxshi bo'ldi — hammasi a'lo edi.","why":"Turar joylar a'lo — H. Avtobuslar haqida faqat eshitgan, mashina ijaraga olgan (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":172.79,"en":206.97,"ev":"We got lost several times… We were never short of help though. Some people were even prepared to walk with us to show us the way. And that was something I'll always remember.","uz":"Bir necha marta adashdik… Lekin yordam hech qachon kam bo'lmadi. Ba'zilar hatto yo'l ko'rsatish uchun biz bilan birga yurishga tayyor edi. Buni doim eslayman.","why":"Odamlarning yordamga tayyorligi (F). Mehmonxona oddiy edi (H emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.77,"e":9.82,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about their visit to a city."},{"k":"h","s":16.6,"e":16.6,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":19.96,"e":24.22,"t":"Spent a day exploring the shops and markets in the city and bought some souvenirs."},{"s":24.79,"e":34.85,"t":"Then we wanted to see some of the area outside the city and discovered it was easy to get to loads of places by train, including the mountains, where we were told there were great hostels."},{"s":35.38,"e":39.33,"t":"You can do bushwalks out there, and apparently the scenery is stunning."},{"s":40.34,"e":41.41,"t":"It can be dangerous."},{"s":42.17,"e":45.89,"t":"We were warned to have the right gear and tell other people where we were going."},{"s":46.39,"e":47.84,"t":"so we decided to give it a miss"},{"s":48.44,"e":50.97,"t":"Anyway, we weren't short of things to do in the city."},{"s":51.42,"e":52.77,"t":"We were spoilt for choice."},{"k":"h","s":56.44,"e":56.44,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":59.9,"e":63.55,"t":"pretty tired when we first arrived so we were glad just to relax."},{"s":64.28,"e":74.69,"t":"book late and I have to say that the room wasn't the best I've stayed in but we had a view of the lake which was a real treat. We were really impressed by the forests and mountains around the city."},{"s":75.19,"e":79.9,"t":"We made good use of the swimming pool, though we were too lazy to go to the famous markets."},{"s":80.34,"e":89.28,"t":"We didn't take advantage of all the shows either. Lots of people told us how good they were, so that was a pity. And the theatres themselves were supposed to be impressive."},{"k":"h","s":92.98,"e":92.98,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":96.25,"e":103.36,"t":"One of my main ambitions was to see inside the big concert hall, and in fact we managed to get into a concert there, which was pretty special."},{"s":103.86,"e":105.25,"t":"The acoustics were amazing."},{"s":105.69,"e":111.97,"t":"The city was divided by a river and getting round had its problems, especially as we didn't really understand the city plan."},{"s":112.66,"e":119.07,"t":"The best we eat was the ferries. I was really impressed that they were always on time and provided good views in the city."},{"s":119.8,"e":126.49,"t":"The trams were good too, and the local commuters seemed happy to chat to us and give us ideas for the best things to do and see."},{"s":127.19,"e":128.83,"t":"We didn't have time to do everything though"},{"k":"h","s":132.54,"e":132.54,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":135.8,"e":148.51,"t":"Before we went, we couldn't decide where to stay. So many people recommended different places. And there seemed to be loads of different and unusual possibilities, like old traditional farms converted into guest houses."},{"s":149.08,"e":153.53,"t":"So we decided to move around and try something different every couple of nights."},{"s":153.98,"e":156.96,"t":"That worked out really well and they were all excellent."},{"s":157.56,"e":165.53,"t":"Although we'd been told that getting round on the buses was easy and cheap in the city, we decided to rent a car so that we could get out into the countryside."},{"s":165.98,"e":169.05,"t":"we didn't want to miss out on the views driving along by the ocean."},{"k":"h","s":172.79,"e":172.79,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":176.28,"e":182.08,"t":"Even though we had a city plan, we got lost several times, especially in the old town where the buildings were quite similar."},{"s":182.81,"e":186.11,"t":"I know some people say getting lost is the best way to get a Noah City."},{"s":186.68,"e":188.29,"t":"We were never shown of help though."},{"s":188.79,"e":194.33,"t":"Some people were even prepared to walk with us to show us the way. And that was something I'll always remember."},{"s":194.87,"e":202.49,"t":"Our hotel was alright without being spectacular and it was a long walk into the evening shows. We took a taxi most times."},{"s":203.0,"e":206.97,"t":"There was loads to do every day though, and we certainly weren't bored."}]},{"n":9,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about happiness. What does each person say happiness means to them?","qu":"Odamlar baxt haqida gapiradi. Har biri uchun baxt nima?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about happiness","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"Having a happy personality allows you to cope effectively with problems.","u":"Quvnoq tabiat muammolarni yengishga yordam beradi."},{"l":"B","t":"Happiness comes from having someone special to share your thoughts with.","u":"Baxt fikrlaringizni bo'lishadigan alohida insonga ega bo'lishdan keladi."},{"l":"C","t":"Happiness is all about the experience of overcoming problems.","u":"Baxt — muammolarni yengish tajribasi."},{"l":"D","t":"Happiness is a short escape from everyday routine.","u":"Baxt — kundalik tartibdan qisqa qochish."},{"l":"E","t":"True happiness lies in making others happy.","u":"Haqiqiy baxt boshqalarni baxtli qilishda."},{"l":"F","t":"Older people are less happy than younger ones.","u":"Keksalar yoshlardan kamroq baxtli."},{"l":"G","t":"Happiness is being thankful for what you have.","u":"Baxt — bor narsangga shukr qilish."},{"l":"H","t":"Happiness comes from achieving your goals.","u":"Baxt maqsadlarga erishishdan keladi."}],"dur":433.6,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":14.39,"en":50.46,"ev":"All alone, just me and my thoughts. No stress, get away from it all for an hour or so… Then when it's all over, it's back to normal life and problems.","uz":"Yolg'iz, faqat men va fikrlarim. Stress yo'q, bir soatcha hamma narsadan uzoqlashasan… Tugagach esa, yana oddiy hayot va muammolarga qaytasan.","why":"\"Get away from it all for an hour… back to normal life\" — kundalik hayotdan qisqa qochish (D).","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":54.14,"en":97.5,"ev":"For me you really appreciate your moments of leisure when you've done lots of hard work… it's all to do with setting yourself a list of things to get through and then you've completed them, now you can be happy.","uz":"Men uchun ko'p mehnat qilgandan keyingina dam olishni qadrlaysan… hammasi o'zingga bajariladigan ishlar ro'yxatini qo'yib, ularni bajarib bo'lgach baxtli bo'lishda.","why":"Maqsadlarni bajarish — H. Pul va hazil — ikkinchi darajali.","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":101.08,"en":133.31,"ev":"But in my experience, happy people get through life more easily. If you take things seriously all the time, that's when you get stressed.","uz":"Lekin tajribamcha, baxtli odamlar hayotdan osonroq o'tadi. Hamma narsani doim jiddiy qabul qilsangiz, aynan o'shanda stressga tushasiz.","why":"\"Happy people get through life more easily\" — quvnoq tabiat muammolarni yengishga yordam beradi (A). Yosh haqida — F emas, \"not specific to one age group\".","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":136.89,"en":175.04,"ev":"I suddenly think of my children's smiling faces and realise how lucky I am… My life could have turned out much worse as it has for many people.","uz":"To'satdan bolalarimning kulib turgan yuzlarini eslayman va qanchalik omadli ekanimni anglayman… Hayotim ko'pchilikniki kabi ancha yomonroq bo'lishi mumkin edi.","why":"\"Realise how lucky I am\" — boriga shukr qilish (G). Oila ham tilga olinadi, lekin asosiy g'oya — minnatdorlik (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":178.68,"en":215.26,"ev":"It's all about your life not being too easy… when you can share your struggles with others and laugh about how you got through them. That's when you're truly happy.","uz":"Gap hayoting juda oson bo'lmasligida… qiyinchiliklaringni boshqalar bilan bo'lishib, ularni qanday yengganing ustidan kula olsang — mana o'shanda chinakam baxtlisan.","why":"Qiyinchiliklarni yengish tajribasi — C. Bo'lishish bor, lekin \"someone special\" emas (B emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.22,"e":9.21,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about happiness."},{"k":"h","s":14.39,"e":14.39,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.37,"e":18.3,"t":"what is happiness."},{"s":19.38,"e":29.05,"t":"From an early age, happiness for me is sitting in a boat in the middle of a lake on a summer's day and doing some serious fishing. All alone, just me and my thoughts."},{"s":29.59,"e":32.41,"t":"No stress, get away from it all for an hour or so."},{"s":32.86,"e":38.08,"t":"But maybe not completely aimless, not just lying on a beach somewhere, but having some task to do."},{"s":38.78,"e":45.18,"t":"Then when it's all over, it's back to normal life and problems and hassle and having to fight to get what you want."},{"s":46.23,"e":50.46,"t":"A brief moment of happiness helps me to reflect and make sense of my life."},{"k":"h","s":54.14,"e":54.14,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":57.43,"e":65.63,"t":"To be happy, you do obviously need some financial security. Not rich. I didn't say that because there's an important difference."},{"s":66.36,"e":71.87,"t":"Um, also I'd say you need humour in your life. That's kind of obvious too."},{"s":72.38,"e":75.39,"t":"Having lots of free time to do what you want."},{"s":76.18,"e":79.52,"t":"Sure there. I'd say quite the reverse actually."},{"s":79.99,"e":84.22,"t":"For me you really appreciate your moments of leisure when you've done lots of hard work."},{"s":84.76,"e":88.7,"t":"If it's all play and no work in your life then you don't enjoy it."},{"s":89.34,"e":97.5,"t":"So for me it's all to do with setting yourself a list of things to get through and then you've completed them, now you can be happy."},{"k":"h","s":101.08,"e":101.08,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":104.12,"e":116.03,"t":"I sometimes wonder if being happy is something to do with age. Very young children are happy most of the time, very old people are happy when they think of fond memories and also they're happy when they see their grandchildren happy."},{"s":116.6,"e":133.31,"t":"So happiness is not just specific to one age group. That's certainly the case with my family. But in my experience, happy people get through life more easily. If you take things seriously all the time, that's when you get stressed or have health issues, maybe. And sometimes life can be a real pain, let's be honest."},{"k":"h","s":136.89,"e":136.89,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":140.02,"e":142.56,"t":"Happiness comes in many shapes and forms."},{"s":143.06,"e":150.78,"t":"Personally, I'm happy when I'm active doing my sports and feeling all healthy, but maybe that's a rather self-centered view."},{"s":151.29,"e":159.49,"t":"I also get moments when I'm just, say, sitting on a train and suddenly I think of my children's smiling faces and realize how lucky I am."},{"s":159.99,"e":163.07,"t":"happy they make me. And my husband too, of course."},{"s":163.58,"e":167.17,"t":"My life could have turned out much worse as it has for many people."},{"s":167.8,"e":170.72,"t":"Will I still be happy when they've all grown up and gone away?"},{"s":171.42,"e":175.04,"t":"I'm sure when that time comes, I'll find a new form of happiness."},{"k":"h","s":178.68,"e":178.68,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":181.82,"e":188.51,"t":"It's sometimes said that you make your own happiness, and I've got some sympathy for that view, but in my experience,"},{"s":189.14,"e":190.21,"t":"It's something more than that"},{"s":191.03,"e":193.53,"t":"It might sound strange, but I honestly think..."},{"s":194.01,"e":196.48,"t":"It's all about your life not being too easy."},{"s":197.34,"e":200.86,"t":"if everything in your life is handed to you on a plate by rich parents."},{"s":201.37,"e":205.57,"t":"then I actually don't think you're as happy as someone who's had to struggle a bit in their life."},{"s":206.74,"e":210.49,"t":"when you can share your struggles with others and laugh about how you got through them."},{"s":211.26,"e":212.67,"t":"That's when you're truly happy."},{"s":213.53,"e":215.26,"t":"That's certainly how it's worked out for me"}]},{"n":10,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about classical music. What is the reason each person gives for starting to play classical music?","qu":"Odamlar klassik musiqa haqida gapiradi. Har biri nima sababdan klassik musiqa chala boshlagan?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about classical music","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"following a family tradition","u":"oilaviy an'anaga ergashish"},{"l":"B","t":"being introduced to a range of good music","u":"turli yaxshi musiqalar bilan tanishtirilgani"},{"l":"C","t":"the experience of attending a concert","u":"konsertga borish tajribasi"},{"l":"D","t":"the encouragement of a teacher","u":"o'qituvchining rag'batlantirishi"},{"l":"E","t":"hearing it in an everyday situation","u":"uni kundalik vaziyatda eshitish"},{"l":"F","t":"realising the importance of starting young","u":"yoshlikda boshlash muhimligini anglash"},{"l":"G","t":"the influence of someone famous","u":"mashhur kishining ta'siri"},{"l":"H","t":"finding other types of music unexciting","u":"boshqa musiqa turlarini zerikarli deb bilish"}],"dur":199.7,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":10.94,"en":53.15,"ev":"It's hard to interpret complex music, even with the best teacher in the world, unless you start training early on in life. Luckily for me, I came to this conclusion myself when I was in my early teens.","uz":"Hayotda erta mashq qilishni boshlamasangiz, eng zo'r o'qituvchi bilan ham murakkab musiqani talqin qilish qiyin. Baxtimga, bu xulosaga o'zim o'smirlik yoshimda keldim.","why":"Yoshlikda boshlash muhimligini anglash (F). Ota-onasi istamay rozi bo'lgan — oilaviy an'ana emas (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":55.13,"en":89.73,"ev":"One day I heard a big rock star going on about the most exciting piece of music ever written. Being a fan of his music, I felt I had to hear it… I found I really had an urge to play the violin myself.","uz":"Bir kuni mashhur bir rok yulduzining eng hayajonli asar haqida gapirayotganini eshitdim. Uning musiqasi muxlisi bo'lganim uchun uni tinglashim kerak edi… va o'zim skripka chalishni juda xohlab qoldim.","why":"Mashhur odamning ta'siri (G). Maktab — san'atga yo'naltirilgan bo'lsa ham, qiziqtirmagan.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":91.86,"en":125.53,"ev":"I recovered from that and got to know the work of some of the top composers thanks to my uncle. That got me excited enough to beg to have piano lessons.","uz":"Bundan o'zimga keldim va amakim tufayli eng zo'r bastakorlarning asarlari bilan tanishdim. Bu meni shunchalik ilhomlantirdiki, pianino darslari olishni iltimos qildim.","why":"Amakisi yaxshi musiqalar bilan tanishtirgan (B). O'qituvchi mashhur bo'lgan — lekin ta'sir qilmagan (G tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":127.74,"en":163.77,"ev":"I remember one day hearing a really famous classical piece being played on a commercial trying to attract young kids to some fast food place… But they had the opposite effect on me.","uz":"Bir kuni fastfud reklamasida juda mashhur klassik asar yangraganini eslayman… Lekin bu menga teskari ta'sir qildi — o'rganishga undadi.","why":"Kundalik vaziyatda (kino, multfilm, reklama) eshitish — E. O'qituvchi muvaffaqiyat qozonmagan (D emas).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":165.98,"en":198.53,"ev":"I resisted the efforts of my teacher to introduce me to classical music. She got there in the end, though, by sheer persistence.","uz":"O'qituvchimning meni klassik musiqa bilan tanishtirish urinishlariga qarshilik qildim. Lekin u qat'iyati bilan oxir-oqibat bunga erishdi.","why":"O'qituvchining sabotli rag'bati — D. Otasi nay chalishni o'rgatgan, lekin qiziqtirmagan (A emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.7,"e":8.67,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about classical music."},{"k":"h","s":10.94,"e":10.94,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":13.46,"e":28.51,"t":"Classical musics often seen as old-fashioned and though there's people everywhere who go to concerts and some classical musicians are big-name stars, it doesn't really excite young people that much. They prefer pop music or more modern stuff."},{"s":29.05,"e":37.53,"t":"But the truth is, it's hard to interpret complex music, even with the best teacher in the world, unless you start training early on in life."},{"s":38.01,"e":53.15,"t":"Luckily for me, I came to this conclusion myself when I was in my early teens, and when I said I wanted to become a classical guitarist, my parents rather reluctantly went along with the idea and bought me some lessons. Since then, I've played almost every day."},{"k":"h","s":55.13,"e":55.13,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":57.85,"e":83.9,"t":"I bought my first classical recording aged 14. It was a violin concerto by a Russian composer. Although my school had a strong arts focus, I had no particular interest in classical music till one day when I heard a big rock star going on about the most exciting piece of music ever written. Being a fan of his music, I felt I had to hear it. By the third listening, I was convinced he was right. What's more, I found I really had an urge to play the violin myself and found myself a teacher."},{"s":84.66,"e":89.73,"t":"Despite my dad's complaints about the noise I produced, I practiced every day at home. I've never looked back."},{"k":"h","s":91.86,"e":91.86,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":94.39,"e":115.45,"t":"At my school I was made to learn the recorder and I had to practice every day. The sound I produced was so dreadful that whatever piece of music I was supposed to be playing was hard to recognise despite all the efforts made by our music teacher who'd actually been quite a famous musician himself when younger. It took a while but I recovered from that and got to know the work of some of the top composers thanks to my uncle."},{"s":116.12,"e":119.9,"t":"got me excited enough to beg to have piano lessons when I was about 12."},{"s":120.34,"e":125.53,"t":"After that, everything just took off. Now here I am getting quite well known as a concert pianist."},{"k":"h","s":127.74,"e":127.74,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":130.33,"e":137.57,"t":"At school, our music teacher tried to get us into classical music without much success. He just seemed to go for the most unexciting pieces."},{"s":138.01,"e":163.77,"t":"It was me who noticed classical music turning up in movies, cartoons and stuff. Like, I remember one day hearing a really famous classical piece being played on a commercial trying to attract young kids to some fast food place. You'd think things like that would be enough to put anyone off classical music. But they had the opposite effect on me. Encouraging me to want to learn to play and seek out a good teacher, which is what I did, much to my mum's amazement I remember."},{"k":"h","s":165.98,"e":165.98,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":168.82,"e":179.84,"t":"Although my dad had taught me to play the flute at an early age, I didn't get interested in learning to play classical music then. I wasn't willing to try and understand it and didn't realise you have to do that in order to enjoy it."},{"s":180.34,"e":189.28,"t":"As a kid I wanted something that made me jump and got me going, made me feel happy or enthusiastic, so I resisted the efforts of my teacher to introduce me to classical music."},{"s":189.98,"e":198.53,"t":"She got there in the end, though, by sheer persistence, convincing me that there's great excitement to be found in the joy of playing something difficult and doing it well."}]},{"n":11,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about a radio station. What does each person say about it?","qu":"Odamlar bir radiostansiya haqida gapiradi. Har biri u haqida nima deydi?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about a radio station","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I appreciate the lack of commercials.","u":"Reklama yo'qligini qadrlayman."},{"l":"B","t":"There are suitable programmes for children.","u":"Bolalar uchun mos dasturlar bor."},{"l":"C","t":"One of the presenters is very funny.","u":"Boshlovchilardan biri juda kulgili."},{"l":"D","t":"There should be more coverage of sport.","u":"Sportga ko'proq e'tibor berilishi kerak."},{"l":"E","t":"It broadcasts high-quality news programmes.","u":"U sifatli yangiliklar dasturlarini efirga uzatadi."},{"l":"F","t":"I approve of what it does for the local area.","u":"Mahalliy hudud uchun qilayotgan ishlarini ma'qullayman."},{"l":"G","t":"The comedy shows are disappointing.","u":"Komediya ko'rsatuvlari umidsizlantiradi."},{"l":"H","t":"It should give more attention to international issues.","u":"Xalqaro masalalarga ko'proq e'tibor berishi kerak."}],"dur":192.5,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":12.09,"en":43.13,"ev":"The thing I like about the station is that it has stuff for all age groups… it makes itself accessible to even the youngest members of the community.","uz":"Stansiyaning menga yoqadigan tomoni — unda barcha yoshdagilar uchun narsa bor… u hatto jamiyatning eng yosh a'zolari uchun ham ochiq.","why":"\"Even the youngest members\" — bolalar uchun mos dasturlar (B). Reklama ko'p — A emas.","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":45.3,"en":80.0,"ev":"Sometimes I'd rather it took more notice of news and other subjects from overseas rather than just the local area or the country as a whole.","uz":"Ba'zan u faqat mahalliy hudud yoki butun mamlakat emas, chet eldagi yangiliklar va mavzularga ham ko'proq e'tibor berishini xohlardim.","why":"\"From overseas\" — xalqaro masalalar (H). Kulgili dastur ham tilga olinadi, lekin asosiy fikr — H.","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":82.2,"en":117.47,"ev":"And they don't broadcast advertisements, so you never get interruptions when you're enjoying a show.","uz":"Va ular reklama bermaydi, shuning uchun ko'rsatuvdan zavqlanayotganda hech narsa xalaqit bermaydi.","why":"\"Don't broadcast advertisements\" — reklama yo'qligi (A).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":119.58,"en":154.62,"ev":"It's presented by a very entertaining guy… he makes fun of everything… you can sit back and enjoy the humour in his approach.","uz":"Uni juda qiziqarli yigit olib boradi… u hamma narsani hazilga aylantiradi… uning yondashuvidagi hazildan bemalol zavqlanishingiz mumkin.","why":"Boshlovchi juda kulgili — C.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":156.7,"en":191.1,"ev":"The station's known for sponsoring charity organisations in this region, so it's offering more than just entertainment.","uz":"Stansiya bu hududdagi xayriya tashkilotlariga homiylik qilishi bilan mashhur, ya'ni u shunchaki ko'ngilochardan ko'proq narsa beradi.","why":"Mahalliy hududga qiladigan ishi — F.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.9,"e":8.57,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about a radio station."},{"k":"h","s":12.09,"e":12.09,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":14.68,"e":21.82,"t":"The station I listen to has the right balance of talk, sport and news and a great mixture of presenters, but there are far too many advertisements."},{"s":22.49,"e":30.46,"t":"In the mornings I usually listen to a short news programme and then a show about sports going on both locally and nationally, which is presented by a well-known ex-sports star."},{"s":31.29,"e":43.13,"t":"The thing I like about the station is that it has stuff for all age groups. There are a lot of good comedy shows and quizzes, but also stories about people and places in the area, and it makes itself accessible to even the youngest members of the community."},{"k":"h","s":45.3,"e":45.3,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":47.74,"e":53.44,"t":"It's a locally operated radio station and it broadcasts some of the top nationally rated talk radio programs."},{"s":53.88,"e":57.5,"t":"There are live shows 24 hours a day, and you can listen online if you prefer."},{"s":57.98,"e":59.9,"t":"I've enjoyed listening to it for many years now."},{"s":60.41,"e":67.84,"t":"I especially like one very amusing comedy programme which is on every weekday night and the Science Fantastic programme on Saturday evenings."},{"s":68.28,"e":80.0,"t":"I prefer this station to some of the national ones and I like the local news stories, although sometimes I'd rather it took more notice of news and other subjects from overseas rather than just the local area or the country as a whole."},{"k":"h","s":82.2,"e":82.2,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":84.89,"e":97.95,"t":"tend to listen to the radio a lot and I love the art show. That's the selling point for this station for me. The presenter is very serious about the arts and his in-depth approach helps me keep up to date with all the latest theatre, books and movies."},{"s":98.87,"e":103.33,"t":"and they don't broadcast advertisements, so you never get interruptions when you're enjoying a show."},{"s":104.06,"e":106.46,"t":"given up flipping through channels to avoid them now."},{"s":107.1,"e":117.47,"t":"Another thing is they don't have news every hour like so many stations. There are some really good quality radio dramas. It's an excellent way for young writers to get their work broadcast."},{"k":"h","s":119.58,"e":119.58,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":122.26,"e":128.61,"t":"Talk radio has grown in popularity in my area and there's a huge demand for more and more talk show stars."},{"s":129.08,"e":141.09,"t":"My favourite station has a show called Viewpoint. It's presented by a very entertaining guy. And sure, there'll be those out there who may not agree with his opinions, but that doesn't matter, because he makes fun of everything."},{"s":141.91,"e":147.61,"t":"Even if you don't agree with him, you can sit back and enjoy the humour in his approach to local or national news events."},{"s":148.28,"e":154.62,"t":"I find I'm still one of the few younger listeners to this station though. Most of my school friends don't really go for it."},{"k":"h","s":156.7,"e":156.7,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":159.38,"e":180.41,"t":"I even got a chance to go on this radio station myself. It was kind of embarrassing but quite fun because not everyone gets to go on a radio show and meet the presenters. All the shows are really interesting. They also play a lot of fun games and talk about popular issues. The station's known for sponsoring charity organisations in this region so it's offering more than just entertainment."},{"s":180.92,"e":191.1,"t":"There's one programme where they're training young news readers, so they picked out about 30 kids from nearby towns and are training them to be news readers and they get to do one short show each."}]},{"n":12,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about what makes a good teacher. What does each speaker say a good teacher should do?","qu":"Odamlar yaxshi o'qituvchi haqida gapiradi. Har birining fikricha, yaxshi o'qituvchi nima qilishi kerak?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about what makes a good teacher","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"set an example of hard work","u":"mehnatsevarlikda namuna bo'lish"},{"l":"B","t":"keep up-to-date with the latest ideas","u":"eng yangi g'oyalardan xabardor bo'lish"},{"l":"C","t":"give information on individual progress","u":"har bir o'quvchining o'sishi haqida ma'lumot berish"},{"l":"D","t":"be available outside class time","u":"darsdan tashqari vaqtda ham topiladigan bo'lish"},{"l":"E","t":"give a lot of encouragement","u":"ko'p rag'batlantirish"},{"l":"F","t":"have an entertaining approach","u":"qiziqarli yondashuvga ega bo'lish"},{"l":"G","t":"set a realistic amount of homework","u":"me'yorida uy vazifasi berish"},{"l":"H","t":"have good qualifications","u":"yaxshi malakaga ega bo'lish"}],"dur":185.0,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":10.94,"en":47.13,"ev":"The teachers I responded to best were the ones that tried to push me along a bit by getting me to try a little bit harder.","uz":"Menga eng yaxshi ta'sir qilgan o'qituvchilar — meni biroz ko'proq harakat qilishga undab, oldinga surganlar edi.","why":"\"Push me along… try harder\" — ko'p rag'batlantirish (E). Malaka tilga olinadi, lekin javob emas (H tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":49.4,"en":80.19,"ev":"Sometimes you might want to be able to ask your teacher something before or after class… It's the teachers who are there for you in those situations that are special.","uz":"Ba'zan o'qituvchidan darsdan oldin yoki keyin biror narsa so'ragingiz keladi… Bunday vaziyatlarda yoningizda bo'ladigan o'qituvchilar alohida.","why":"\"Before or after class\" — darsdan tashqari vaqtda topilish (D). Hisobot yozish — oddiy vazifa (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":82.39,"en":116.29,"ev":"Best teachers are the ones who make it look easy because they make it seem fun. Then the kids are fascinated, even amused by the subject.","uz":"Eng yaxshi o'qituvchilar — fanni qiziqarli qilib, oson ko'rsatadiganlar. Shunda bolalar fanga mahliyo bo'lib, hatto zavqlanadi.","why":"\"Make it seem fun… amused\" — qiziqarli yondashuv (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":118.46,"en":148.57,"ev":"You also have to demonstrate what you mean by this. So the teacher needs to put in the hours to mark the homework, to prepare lessons carefully. If kids know the teacher's doing it, then they'll want to do their part too.","uz":"Nima demoqchi ekaningizni o'zingiz ko'rsatishingiz ham kerak. O'qituvchi uy vazifasini tekshirish, darslarni puxta tayyorlash uchun vaqt sarflashi kerak. Bolalar buni ko'rsa, o'z ulushini qo'shishni xohlaydi.","why":"O'z mehnati bilan namuna bo'lish — A. \"Fashions come and go\" — yangi g'oyalarni ta'kidlamaydi (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":150.68,"en":184.06,"ev":"They only know if they're doing well if they're told by their teacher… You need to be told the facts about how well you're managing with your studies.","uz":"O'quvchilar yaxshi o'qiyotganini faqat o'qituvchi aytsagina biladi… O'qishda qanchalik uddalayotganing haqida aniq ma'lumot berilishi kerak.","why":"Har bir o'quvchining natijasi haqida ma'lumot berish — C. \"Not just fun\" — F rad etiladi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.42,"e":8.64,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about what makes a good teacher."},{"k":"h","s":10.94,"e":10.94,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":13.37,"e":28.73,"t":"I fully accept that everyone's different, so of course different teachers will suit different types of children and teenagers. Throughout my education though, the teachers I responded to best were the ones that tried to push me along a bit by getting me to try a little bit harder."},{"s":29.24,"e":47.13,"t":"Because the problem for me is that I'm naturally quite a lazy person and I've always been more interested in life outside the classroom than inside it. So I'm the kind of person that's perhaps a bit of a headache for teachers. The sort they're not really thinking about when they're studying for their teaching qualifications."},{"k":"h","s":49.4,"e":49.4,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":51.83,"e":61.34,"t":"Most of the time a teacher's just doing his or her job, I guess. I mean, they've done their qualification, they're in the classroom, they've got to write your report at the end of term saying how you've done, haven't they?"},{"s":61.85,"e":70.56,"t":"Sometimes you might want to be able to ask your teacher something before or after class, get some advice or extra information or tell them about some problem."},{"s":71.1,"e":76.19,"t":"It's the teachers who are there for you in those situations that are special, who take an individual approach."},{"s":76.66,"e":80.19,"t":"And I don't think it's too hard for them to do that. Give you a couple of minutes"},{"k":"h","s":82.39,"e":82.39,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":84.95,"e":95.49,"t":"Well, I'm a firm believer in the importance of the subject. If a teacher can get the kids absorbed by the subject, be it maths or geography or cookery or whatever, then the job is basically done."},{"s":96.12,"e":108.16,"t":"Best teachers are the ones who make it look easy because they make it seem fun. Then the kids are fascinated, even amused by the subject, so they want to learn and each and every one of them makes progress."},{"s":108.63,"e":116.29,"t":"I think this often involves the teacher getting everyone to see the relevance of the subject in the wide world beyond the confines of the classroom."},{"k":"h","s":118.46,"e":118.46,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":121.11,"e":142.24,"t":"Fashions come and go in teaching just as in everything else. We're at a stage at the moment where there's a lot of focus on the individual and getting every child to take responsibility for their own learning, that kind of thing. But you can't just tell kids to be better, to study harder. You also have to demonstrate what you mean by this. So the teacher needs to put in the hours to mark the homework, to prepare lessons carefully."},{"s":142.81,"e":148.57,"t":"If kids know the teacher's doing it, then they'll want to do their part too. I think that's the way to do it. Never mind what's in"},{"k":"h","s":150.68,"e":150.68,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":153.56,"e":162.72,"t":"the best thing is for teachers to reflect on how they themselves got to be teachers. How did they achieve success in their qualifications? How did they manage to do well at school?"},{"s":163.26,"e":172.7,"t":"It's down to a question of each and every student making his or her own way, and they only know if they're doing well if they're told by their teacher that they're doing well, or badly."},{"s":173.3,"e":179.01,"t":"You need to be told the facts about how well you're managing with your studies, in class and in your homework."},{"s":179.64,"e":184.06,"t":"But the truth is that learning's not a game, not just fun, but hard effort."}]},{"n":13,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about visits they have made to a hospital. What was the reason each attended the hospital?","qu":"Besh kishi kasalxonaga borgani haqida gapiradi. Har biri nima sababdan borgan?","topic":"different people talking about visits they have made to a hospital","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"collect some surgical knives","u":"jarrohlik pichoqlarini olib ketish"},{"l":"B","t":"collect somebody","u":"kimnidir olib ketish"},{"l":"C","t":"deliver supplies","u":"jihozlar (mahsulot) yetkazib berish"},{"l":"D","t":"visit a relative","u":"qarindoshini ko'rish"},{"l":"E","t":"have an operation","u":"operatsiya qilinish"},{"l":"F","t":"do maintenance work","u":"ta'mirlash ishlarini bajarish"},{"l":"G","t":"check a mental problem","u":"ruhiy muammoni tekshirtirish"},{"l":"H","t":"have a medical check-up","u":"tibbiy ko'rikdan o'tish"}],"dur":534.0,"items":[{"a":"H","ps":13.34,"en":50.05,"ev":"They needed an official piece of paper from any qualified doctor saying that I had healthy lungs, heart, liver and good eyesight.","uz":"Ularga malakali shifokordan o'pkam, yuragim, jigarim sog'lom va ko'rishim yaxshi ekani haqida rasmiy qog'oz kerak edi.","why":"Sog'lig'ini tekshirtirish — tibbiy ko'rik (H).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":53.59,"en":87.81,"ev":"I'd always thought they'd give me something to put me to sleep… But these days it's all done with a local anaesthetic. So you stay awake through the whole thing.","uz":"Doim meni uxlatib qo'yishadi deb o'ylardim… Lekin hozir hammasi mahalliy og'riqsizlantirish bilan qilinadi. Butun jarayon davomida uyg'oq qolasiz.","why":"Behushlik, choklar — operatsiya qilingan (E).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":91.22,"en":135.65,"ev":"When somebody has such a big operation, nothing really prepares you for what happens afterwards… When at last I managed to find the right room, I almost didn't recognise her.","uz":"Kimdir shunday katta operatsiyani boshidan kechirganda, keyin nima bo'lishiga hech narsa tayyorlamaydi… Nihoyat to'g'ri xonani topganimda, uni deyarli tanimadim.","why":"Operatsiya bo'lgan yaqinini ko'rgani borgan — D. Operatsiyani boshqa odam o'tkazgan (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":139.19,"en":198.53,"ev":"The call on my answer phone said there was this leaking roof in one of the wards… But when I got up there, the whole roof was in a shocking state.","uz":"Avtojavobgichdagi xabarda palatalardan birida tom oqayotgani aytilgan edi… Tepaga chiqqanimda, butun tom dahshatli ahvolda edi.","why":"Tomni tekshirgani borgan usta — ta'mirlash ishi (F).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":201.82,"en":257.44,"ev":"The address on the package says Room 4J… they certainly don't want a box of surgical knives… and then there's nobody there to sign the documents to say they've received it.","uz":"Posilkadagi manzil — 4J xona… ularga jarrohlik pichoqlari qutisi kerak emas… keyin qabul qilganini tasdiqlab imzo qo'yadigan hech kim yo'q.","why":"Posilka yetkazib bergan — C. Pichoqlarni olib ketmagan, olib kelgan (A tuzoq). Buvisini ko'rgani ilgari borgan (D emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.77,"e":6.17,"t":"You will hear five different people."},{"s":6.68,"e":9.57,"t":"talking about visits they have made to a hospital."},{"k":"h","s":13.34,"e":13.34,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.83,"e":21.57,"t":"Well, the last time I went to the hospital was because I needed a medical certificate."},{"s":22.52,"e":34.53,"t":"just been offered the job in Kuwait and they needed an official piece of paper from any qualified doctor saying that I had healthy lungs, heart, liver and good eyesight"},{"s":35.0,"e":41.25,"t":"and, well, I couldn't go to my regular doctor because I had already given his name as a reference."},{"s":41.85,"e":50.05,"t":"and well I was a bit nervous because if the doctor didn't declare that I was perfectly healthy I wouldn't get the job"},{"k":"h","s":53.59,"e":53.59,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.02,"e":59.52,"t":"I'd always thought they'd give me something to put me to sleep."},{"s":59.96,"e":65.95,"t":"and when I came round everything would be over and all I would see would be a few stitches."},{"s":66.46,"e":75.23,"t":"But these days it's all done with a local anaesthetic. So you stay awake through the whole thing and you can see everything they're doing."},{"s":75.8,"e":82.72,"t":"Of course, they tell you that you don't have to look, but you can't really look anywhere else, can you?"},{"s":83.58,"e":87.81,"t":"Of course you don't feel anything, but it's a bit scary."},{"k":"h","s":91.22,"e":91.22,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":93.59,"e":101.44,"t":"I didn't know what to expect. I mean, when somebody has such a big operation, nothing really prepares you for..."},{"s":102.2,"e":103.52,"t":"what happens afterwards."},{"s":104.47,"e":106.3,"t":"It's not a bit like it is on tell"},{"s":107.42,"e":112.09,"t":"When at last I managed to find the right room, I almost didn't recognize her."},{"s":113.3,"e":114.85,"t":"It really was a bit of a shock."},{"s":115.51,"e":120.83,"t":"The staff all seemed really pleased with her progress and were even talking about"},{"s":121.27,"e":123.81,"t":"going home in just a few days."},{"s":125.69,"e":128.77,"t":"don't know about these things and I believed what they said."},{"s":130.42,"e":135.65,"t":"If I'd known what was going to happen, I'd have stayed there all night, just to be with her right up to the end."},{"k":"h","s":139.19,"e":139.19,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":141.59,"e":149.25,"t":"Well, the call on my answer phone said there was this leaking roof in one of the wards. A drip."},{"s":149.72,"e":150.81,"t":"They called it..."},{"s":151.35,"e":163.2,"t":"Well, it hadn't been raining much, so I suppose it didn't seem too bad to them. But when I got up there, the whole roof was in a shocking state."},{"s":163.7,"e":177.57,"t":"It's a good thing I looked at it when I did, because one heavy rainstorm and all that lot was going to collapse, and with all the patients in their beds underneath."},{"s":178.26,"e":187.01,"t":"I mean I know the national health hasn't got much cash these days, but they should have had the whole roof fixed."},{"s":187.67,"e":195.01,"t":"So in the end, I told them to get someone else to do it. And I'll tell you another thing."},{"s":195.48,"e":198.53,"t":"I'm going private from now on."},{"k":"h","s":201.82,"e":201.82,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":204.25,"e":207.77,"t":"The address on the package says Room 4J."},{"s":208.63,"e":213.34,"t":"Anyway, I've been to the hospital loads of times to visit my gran."},{"s":213.85,"e":216.19,"t":"so I know the layout pretty well."},{"s":216.89,"e":224.96,"t":"Anyway, I find room 4H in no time. It says checkups on the door so it can't be the room I want."},{"s":225.46,"e":235.97,"t":"But then there's no room for I or 4J and room 4K is the maintenance office and they certainly don't want a box of surgical knives."},{"s":236.63,"e":247.01,"t":"So after I've been looking for a good ten minutes I ask someone and they tell me, as though everyone knows, it's on the next floor of course."},{"s":247.9,"e":248.93,"t":"What was I to know?"},{"s":249.43,"e":257.44,"t":"and then there's nobody there to sign the documents to say they've received it."}]},{"n":14,"q":"You will hear five different women talking about the same wedding. Who is each speaker speaking to?","qu":"Besh ayol bitta to'y haqida gapiradi. Har biri kim bilan gaplashyapti?","topic":"different women talking about the same wedding","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"her husband","u":"eri"},{"l":"B","t":"her boyfriend","u":"yigiti"},{"l":"C","t":"a child","u":"bola"},{"l":"D","t":"her father","u":"otasi"},{"l":"E","t":"her boss","u":"boshlig'i"},{"l":"F","t":"somebody she's just met","u":"hozirgina tanishgan odami"},{"l":"G","t":"her mother","u":"onasi"},{"l":"H","t":"the vicar","u":"ruhoniy (nikohni o'qiydigan)"}],"dur":391.8,"items":[{"a":"G","ps":12.28,"en":50.59,"ev":"Well, it really was a pity you couldn't be there… They wore pale yellow just like you wanted… Of course Dad was there with… But I don't suppose you want to hear about that.","uz":"Kela olmaganingiz juda achinarli… Ular siz xohlagandek och sariq kiyishdi… Albatta, dadam ham… bilan kelgan edi, lekin bu haqda eshitishni istamasangiz kerak.","why":"\"Dad was there with…\" — ajrashgan onasiga gapiryapti (G).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":54.23,"en":87.33,"ev":"Still, when we get married a few little things are going to change. There'll be no more nights out with the lads, not when I'm in charge.","uz":"Lekin biz turmush qurganimizda ba'zi narsalar o'zgaradi. Yigitlar bilan kechki sayrlar bo'lmaydi — men boshqaradigan bo'lganimda.","why":"\"When we get married\" — hali turmush qurmagan yigitiga (B), eriga emas (A tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":90.9,"en":120.0,"ev":"So you must have known Brian for quite some time now… I met him a couple of years ago… I suppose you know all this already.","uz":"Brayanni ancha vaqtdan beri taniysiz shekilli… Men u bilan bir-ikki yil oldin tanishganman… Bularning hammasini bilsangiz kerak.","why":"Suhbatdoshi haqida hech narsa bilmaydi — endigina tanishgan odam (F). Ish haqida gapiradi, lekin boshliqqa emas (E emas).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":123.48,"en":154.81,"ev":"Did you take all these pictures yourself? You are clever… Your Auntie Julia will probably like a copy of that one. And so would your granny.","uz":"Bu suratlarning hammasini o'zing oldingmi? Qanday aqlli! Julia xolang bundan bir nusxa olishni xohlasa kerak. Buving ham.","why":"\"Your Auntie… your granny… you are clever\" — bolaga (C).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":158.1,"en":192.16,"ev":"I mean, if you hadn't given me the Friday off, I simply wouldn't have been able to get there on time.","uz":"Agar menga juma kuni dam bermaganingizda, o'z vaqtida yetib bora olmagan bo'lardim.","why":"Dam kuni bergan odam — boshlig'i (E).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.66,"e":8.64,"t":"You'll hear five different women talking about the same wedding."},{"k":"h","s":12.28,"e":12.28,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":14.58,"e":17.09,"t":"Well it really was a pity you couldn't be there."},{"s":17.59,"e":22.11,"t":"Ryan and Julie look so wonderful and everything went off perfectly."},{"s":22.74,"e":26.65,"t":"The vicar gave a beautiful dress and the reception was gorgeous."},{"s":27.13,"e":29.73,"t":"Everyone commented on the bridesmaid's dresses."},{"s":30.3,"e":32.61,"t":"They wore pale yellow just like you wanted."},{"s":33.66,"e":34.85,"t":"and I want this forgot."},{"s":35.32,"e":40.48,"t":"Brian mentioned you in his speech. He said, \"Judas got everything a wife could offer.\""},{"s":41.11,"e":43.07,"t":"But he still likes your cooking best."},{"s":43.77,"e":46.88,"t":"I think he meant it too. Of course Dad was there with..."},{"s":47.35,"e":50.59,"t":"But I don't suppose you want to hear about that."},{"k":"h","s":54.23,"e":54.23,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.63,"e":72.77,"t":"Brian's not going to have an easy time of it. After all, Julia's not going to coddle him like that mother of his does, and it's a good thing too if you ask me. It's about time he learnt to be useful around the house. 70 years of feminism doesn't seem to have done much for our family either."},{"s":73.4,"e":87.33,"t":"Still, when we get married a few little things are going to change. There'll be no more nights out with the lads, not when I'm in charge. And I'll tell you another thing, if I were Julia, I'd be keeping a good eye on one of those bridesmaids too."},{"k":"h","s":90.9,"e":90.9,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":93.21,"e":118.14,"t":"So you must have known Brian for quite some time now. Has he always been this handsome? No, don't tell me, I can imagine. Well anyway, I met him a couple of years ago when they moved our unit up to head office and he was already working there as an entertainment officer. You know, all the big firms have them these days. He organises surprise parties and hires entertainers and kissagrams and then comes round the office collecting money for them afterwards."},{"s":118.33,"e":120.0,"t":"I suppose you know all this already."},{"k":"h","s":123.48,"e":123.48,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":125.91,"e":146.43,"t":"Did you take all these pictures yourself? You are clever. And look, there's one of me. I don't remember you taking that one. Oh, and here's one of everybody outside the church. Your Auntie Julia will probably like a copy of that one. And so would your granny. Mind you, it's a pity it's got your granddad in with that Marjorie."},{"s":147.13,"e":150.11,"t":"Oh! Could you be a darling and get some copies done?"},{"s":150.55,"e":154.81,"t":"We could send them for Christmas. They always send you something nice."},{"k":"h","s":158.1,"e":158.1,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":160.5,"e":177.63,"t":"It was really one of the best weddings I've ever been to. The service was short, the bride arrived on time, the groom was sober, the food was excellent, the speakers were funny. Not like my wedding at all. They really must have put so much thought into it and so much preparation."},{"s":178.3,"e":192.16,"t":"which must show that they're serious about each other because so many young people aren't these days. The only sad thing is that they live so far away. I mean, if you hadn't given me the Friday off, I simply wouldn't have been able to get there on time."}]},{"n":15,"q":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about holiday jobs they have done. What does each speaker say about the job they did?","qu":"Odamlar ta'tildagi ishlari haqida gapiradi. Har biri ishi haqida nima deydi?","topic":"short extracts in which people are talking about holiday jobs they have done","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I was disappointed not to earn more.","u":"Ko'proq pul topmaganimdan xafa bo'ldim."},{"l":"B","t":"The routine made it very boring.","u":"Bir xillik uni juda zerikarli qildi."},{"l":"C","t":"I didn't like the way some people were rude to me.","u":"Ba'zi odamlarning menga qo'pol muomalasi yoqmadi."},{"l":"D","t":"I didn't have to work very hard.","u":"Juda qattiq ishlashim shart emas edi."},{"l":"E","t":"My boss was very demanding.","u":"Boshlig'im juda talabchan edi."},{"l":"F","t":"I needed to be very sociable.","u":"Juda kirishimli bo'lishim kerak edi."},{"l":"G","t":"Some of my colleagues were very friendly.","u":"Ba'zi hamkasblarim juda do'stona edi."},{"l":"H","t":"I had to be prepared for unexpected events.","u":"Kutilmagan voqealarga tayyor turishim kerak edi."}],"dur":191.5,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":12.02,"en":47.1,"ev":"It wasn't the actual tasks themselves that got to me… But the way everyone went for breaks and lunch at exactly the same time every day.","uz":"Meni bezdirgan narsa vazifalarning o'zi emas edi… balki hamma har kuni aynan bir vaqtda tanaffus va tushlikka chiqishi edi.","why":"Har kungi bir xil tartib zeriktirgan — B. Hamkasblar qo'pol emas (C emas).","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":49.34,"en":83.29,"ev":"The thing with being on the reception desk in a hotel… is you never really know what's going to happen next.","uz":"Mehmonxona qabulxonasida ishlashning o'ziga xosligi — keyin nima bo'lishini hech qachon bilmaysiz.","why":"\"Never know what's going to happen next\" — kutilmagan voqealarga tayyor turish (H). Menejer yaxshi edi (E emas).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":85.53,"en":118.46,"ev":"It was tiring being on your feet all the time and having to smile and be nice and show an interest in everyone and laugh at some pretty terrible jokes.","uz":"Doim oyoqda turish, tabassum qilish, xushmuomala bo'lish, hammaga qiziqish bildirish va juda yomon hazillarga kulish charchatardi.","why":"Doim odamlarga xushmuomala bo'lish — kirishimli bo'lish kerak edi (F). Pul yaxshi edi (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":120.66,"en":152.54,"ev":"I didn't exactly have a lot of responsibility… most of the time I just sat about to be honest, or did a bit of gentle tidying.","uz":"Unchalik ko'p mas'uliyatim yo'q edi… rostini aytsam, ko'p vaqt shunchaki o'tirardim yoki ozgina narsalarni tartibga keltirardim.","why":"\"Just sat about\" — qattiq ishlash shart emas edi (D). Menejer sovuq edi — lekin talabchan emas.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":154.74,"en":188.09,"ev":"I got shouted at or treated badly by families turning up late… Nothing was my fault, so why blame me like that?","uz":"Kech kelgan oilalar menga baqirishardi yoki yomon muomala qilishardi… Hech narsa mening aybim emas edi, nega meni bunday ayblashadi?","why":"Odamlarning qo'pol muomalasi — C. Boshliq umuman ko'rinmasdi (E emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.25,"e":9.31,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people are talking about holiday jobs they have done."},{"k":"h","s":12.02,"e":12.02,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":14.39,"e":18.3,"t":"I'm glad I took the job. If nothing else it's taught me that I never want to do it again"},{"s":19.1,"e":27.84,"t":"It was just what I had expected, really, although maybe a bit harder. Packing things into boxes and boxes into crates. It's never going to be fascinating, is it?"},{"s":28.57,"e":37.37,"t":"But actually, it wasn't the actual tasks themselves that got to me, because you can just go into a sort of dream world, do it on automatic while thinking about other nicer things."},{"s":37.82,"e":42.37,"t":"But the way everyone went for breaks and lunch at exactly the same time every day"},{"s":43.13,"e":47.1,"t":"The others were okay, you know, I mean not rude or anything so I shouldn't moan."},{"k":"h","s":49.34,"e":49.34,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":51.77,"e":72.73,"t":"It wasn't an all easy you know, but I thought it would be a breeze. I guess the thing with being on the reception desk in a hotel, even a budget hotel, or maybe especially a budget hotel, is you never really know what's going to happen next. You might find yourself dealing with an incredibly rude guest, tell yourself he's very stressed, or someone who's locked out of their room, or anything."},{"s":73.34,"e":77.47,"t":"Some days were so busy you couldn't catch your breath and others dragged by."},{"s":77.91,"e":83.29,"t":"My manager was great, really positive, but some of the other staff were just, well, dull."},{"k":"h","s":85.53,"e":85.53,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":88.06,"e":91.71,"t":"When I first finished the job, I thought I'll never do that again, no way."},{"s":92.15,"e":101.6,"t":"But now that I've recovered a bit, I think I might well try to do it again next summer. With tips, the money turned out to be quite good, and some of the other waiters were quite funny, so it kept me amused."},{"s":102.1,"e":118.46,"t":"Every day was pretty similar to the last and the next and I found that quite reassuring. It was tiring being on your feet all the time and having to smile and be nice and show an interest in everyone and laugh at some pretty terrible jokes. All that was what took the energy but yeah I'll do it again."},{"k":"h","s":120.66,"e":120.66,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":123.22,"e":125.09,"t":"Well, I was working in this shop."},{"s":125.75,"e":131.39,"t":"It sold small craft things, models and little pictures and things, mainly to tourists really."},{"s":131.96,"e":143.81,"t":"I didn't exactly have a lot of responsibility. If anything interesting happened, like a delivery or a customer spending a lot of money, then I had to get the manager to come and deal with it. She was rather a cold person, actually. They're very polite."},{"s":144.44,"e":152.54,"t":"But it wasn't very good weather and there weren't very many tourists, so most of the time I just sat about to be honest, or did a bit of gentle tidying of the stuff on sale."},{"k":"h","s":154.74,"e":154.74,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":157.4,"e":168.8,"t":"I didn't understand what was involved when I got the job. I thought working on a campsite meant helping people put up their tents, stuff like that. But I found I had to do cleaning and also serving in the little shop they had there."},{"s":169.4,"e":175.13,"t":"There were a couple of other guys working there, but they kept themselves to themselves, and the boss was nowhere to be seen, ever."},{"s":175.67,"e":185.02,"t":"So problems landed on my plate and I got shouted at or treated badly by families turning up late and finding we didn't have any spaces or that their tent had a hole in it or something."},{"s":185.66,"e":188.09,"t":"Nothing was my fault, so why blame me like that?"}]},{"n":16,"q":"You will hear five different employees talking about what makes a good boss. What idea does each speaker express?","qu":"Besh xodim yaxshi boshliq haqida gapiradi. Har biri qanday fikr bildiradi?","topic":"different employees talking about what makes a good boss","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"allowing staff to take decisions","u":"xodimlarga qaror qabul qilishga imkon berish"},{"l":"B","t":"encouraging staff to work in teams","u":"xodimlarni jamoada ishlashga undash"},{"l":"C","t":"listening to complaints from staff","u":"xodimlarning shikoyatlarini tinglash"},{"l":"D","t":"giving information on individual progress","u":"har bir xodimning o'sishi haqida ma'lumot berish"},{"l":"E","t":"having good qualifications","u":"yaxshi malakaga ega bo'lish"},{"l":"F","t":"setting an example of working hard","u":"mehnatsevarlikda namuna bo'lish"}],"dur":413.1,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":14.01,"en":51.42,"ev":"If a boss says to me, for example, \"Luke, your computer skills need upgrading,\" I'll think, \"Right, this person has a degree in computing. I don't, so he must be right.\"","uz":"Masalan, boshliq menga \"Lyuk, kompyuter ko'nikmalaringni oshirishing kerak\" desa, \"Ha, bu odamda kompyuter bo'yicha diplom bor, menda yo'q, demak u haq\" deb o'ylayman.","why":"Diplom, daraja — yaxshi malaka (E). \"Leaders are born\" fikrini rad etadi.","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":55.29,"en":89.53,"ev":"To be a really good boss you have to be good at encouraging the people under you to decide on important issues, creating a situation in which other people can shine.","uz":"Haqiqatan yaxshi boshliq bo'lish uchun qo'l ostidagilarni muhim masalalarda qaror qabul qilishga undash, boshqalar porlashi uchun sharoit yaratish kerak.","why":"\"Encouraging… to decide on important issues\" — qaror qabul qilishga imkon (A).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":93.56,"en":128.89,"ev":"To develop all my potential I need to be told when I'm doing something well and also the areas where I could improve… it's good to meet regularly with your boss.","uz":"Imkoniyatlarimni to'liq ochish uchun qachon yaxshi ishlayotganimni va qayerda o'sishim mumkinligini aytib turishlari kerak… boshliq bilan muntazam uchrashish foydali.","why":"Feedback — shaxsiy o'sish haqida ma'lumot (D).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":132.89,"en":168.51,"ev":"However, what really matters is the ability to bring people together. Leaders often mistakenly encourage people to work on their own.","uz":"Lekin eng muhimi — odamlarni birlashtira olish. Rahbarlar ko'pincha xato qilib, odamlarni yakka ishlashga undaydi.","why":"\"Bring people together\" — jamoada ishlashga undash (B).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":172.44,"en":204.38,"ev":"We are being asked to do an enormous amount of extra work, and some of the bosses don't seem to be doing long hours like the rest of us.","uz":"Bizdan juda ko'p qo'shimcha ish qilish talab qilinyapti, ba'zi boshliqlar esa biz kabi uzoq soat ishlamaydi.","why":"Boshliq ham qattiq ishlab namuna bo'lishi kerak (F).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.47,"e":8.89,"t":"You'll hear five different employees talking about what makes a good boss."},{"k":"h","s":14.01,"e":14.01,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":18.46,"e":22.14,"t":"People still think that leaders are born, not made."},{"s":22.74,"e":32.54,"t":"They say, no matter how hard you study and how many diplomas you collect, at the end of the day, if you've got natural skills, such as a strong character, that's all you'll need."},{"s":33.14,"e":34.3,"t":"I think that's nonsense."},{"s":34.97,"e":47.17,"t":"Leadership is all about commanding respect. If a boss says to me, for example, \"Luke, your computer skills need upgrading.\" I'll think, \"Right, this person has a degree in computing. I don't, so he must be right.\""},{"s":48.12,"e":51.42,"t":"But if it's the other way around, then you feel well. Maybe I should be boss"},{"k":"h","s":55.29,"e":55.29,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":59.19,"e":68.64,"t":"The sort of leaders that I actually admire are not the top dogs in suits with a degree in management and a belief that nobody can do things as well as they can."},{"s":69.27,"e":79.04,"t":"One thing I've learned from all my experience in different jobs is that to be a really good boss you have to be good at encouraging the people under you to decide on important issues."},{"s":79.61,"e":82.24,"t":"creating a situation in which other people can shine."},{"s":83.06,"e":87.13,"t":"Of course, this does not mean the boss's job is any easier. Still a challenge."},{"s":87.61,"e":89.53,"t":"were so much more rewarding for everyone."},{"k":"h","s":93.56,"e":93.56,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":97.4,"e":100.83,"t":"But since I left school, I've done a number of short-term office jobs."},{"s":101.27,"e":107.01,"t":"And I must say I'm beginning to realise how important it is to have the right sort of person directing your work."},{"s":107.74,"e":114.33,"t":"To develop all my potential I need to be told when I'm doing something well and also the areas where I could improve."},{"s":115.0,"e":128.89,"t":"I think the earlier you get formal and informal feedback the better. Otherwise you develop bad habits. Some of my workmates don't agree with me when I say it's good to meet regularly with your boss. They think I'm trying to be better than them."},{"k":"h","s":132.89,"e":132.89,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":136.66,"e":146.3,"t":"Of course we all want bosses who are knowledgeable and who bring energy to the job. And I must say, in my opinion, most people who reach top job positions do possess these qualities."},{"s":146.84,"e":163.29,"t":"However, what really matters is the ability to bring people together. Leaders often mistakenly encourage people to work on their own, kind of in isolation because they're afraid of the strengths of groups. They think maybe they'll criticise or even join forces against the leader."},{"s":163.96,"e":168.51,"t":"Such laders need to go on management courses to look at good examples of ladership."},{"k":"h","s":172.44,"e":172.44,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":176.12,"e":184.64,"t":"Well, in the organisation where I work, each department has a leader, a boss. And because I've worked in six of these departments, I've had six different bosses."},{"s":185.37,"e":194.81,"t":"I must say there's been very little to complain about, except that we are being asked to do an enormous amount of extra work, and some of the bosses don't seem to be doing long hours like the rest of us."},{"s":195.48,"e":204.38,"t":"It is true that after work they may have to attend special management courses or meet individual members of staff to discuss performance, but this only happens occasionally."}]},{"n":17,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about the way they study. Which opinion does each speaker express?","qu":"Besh kishi qanday o'qishi haqida gapiradi. Har biri qaysi fikrni bildiradi?","topic":"different people talking about the way they study","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"Music helps me concentrate when I'm studying.","u":"O'qiyotganimda musiqa diqqatimni jamlashga yordam beradi."},{"l":"B","t":"I study best in the morning when I can think clearly.","u":"Fikrim tiniq bo'lgan ertalab eng yaxshi o'qiyman."},{"l":"C","t":"I prefer to study when I'm lying down.","u":"Yotgan holda o'qishni afzal ko'raman."},{"l":"D","t":"I find I can concentrate better when I study with a friend.","u":"Do'stim bilan o'qiganda diqqatim yaxshiroq jamlanadi."},{"l":"E","t":"It is much easier for me to study late at night.","u":"Kechasi kech o'qish menga ancha oson."},{"l":"F","t":"Learning new things comes naturally to me.","u":"Yangi narsalarni o'rganish menga tabiiy ravishda oson."}],"dur":407.9,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":12.18,"en":47.29,"ev":"I set my alarm early and work with a fresh mind before everyone else is up.","uz":"Budilnikni erta qo'yaman va hamma turishidan oldin tiniq miya bilan ishlayman.","why":"\"Early… fresh mind\" — ertalab (B). Bog'da yotib o'qish — do'stining usuli (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":51.03,"en":87.42,"ev":"What I frequently do instead now is put on my personal stereo and have something blasting away. It doesn't matter what. It blocks out everything else and I get through the work in no time.","uz":"Endi ko'pincha pleyerimni qo'yib, baland ovozda nimadir eshitaman. Nima ekani muhim emas. U boshqa hamma narsani to'sib qo'yadi va ishni tezda tugataman.","why":"Musiqa diqqatni jamlaydi (A). Sinfdosh bilan deyarli ishlamaydi (D emas).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":91.1,"en":126.97,"ev":"After sitting on a hard chair all day, I need to stretch out with my head on a pillow.","uz":"Kun bo'yi qattiq stulda o'tirgandan keyin boshimni yostiqqa qo'yib cho'zilishim kerak.","why":"Yotib o'qish — C. Musiqa unga xalaqit beradi (A tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":130.74,"en":167.49,"ev":"I've never worked with a friend before and so I said no, but she was desperate. Eventually I gave in and it really worked out for us both.","uz":"Ilgari hech qachon do'stim bilan ishlamaganman, shuning uchun yo'q dedim, lekin u juda iltimos qildi. Oxiri rozi bo'ldim va bu ikkalamizga ham juda foyda berdi.","why":"Do'st bilan ishlash yordam bergan (D).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":171.26,"en":200.96,"ev":"I need to be able to work undisturbed. That's often a bit difficult in our house, unless I put it off until everyone's in bed.","uz":"Menga xalaqitsiz ishlash kerak. Uyimizda bu ko'pincha qiyin — hamma uxlaguncha kechiktirmasam.","why":"\"Until everyone's in bed\" — kechasi (E). Matematikani yaxshi ko'radi, lekin \"comes naturally\" demaydi (F emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.9,"e":7.61,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about the way they study."},{"k":"h","s":12.18,"e":12.18,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.29,"e":25.15,"t":"I must say I've never found it easy to study at home. I've tried all sorts of places. One of my friends prefers to study outside, lying on a rug in the garden."},{"s":25.75,"e":35.61,"t":"I try that from time to time, and it's nice and airy, though my concentration tends to wander a bit and I find I'm looking at the trees or people passing by rather than at my notes."},{"s":36.89,"e":47.29,"t":"better in my bedroom, where it's nice and quiet. I've got a large desk there to put my computer on, and I set my alarm early and work with a fresh mind before everyone else is up."},{"k":"h","s":51.03,"e":51.03,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":54.2,"e":55.9,"t":"You know how sociable I am normally."},{"s":56.92,"e":63.39,"t":"It's strange, but I find people talking really puts me off when I'm trying to study, so I hardly ever work with a classmate."},{"s":63.9,"e":65.31,"t":"although it's much more fun."},{"s":66.14,"e":76.38,"t":"You'd think that the Faculty Library would be the best place for me then, an academic atmosphere and no distractions. You always get a few people whispering and coughing though and that annoys me."},{"s":77.05,"e":83.61,"t":"What I frequently do instead now is put on my personal stereo and have something blasting away. It doesn't matter what."},{"s":84.28,"e":87.42,"t":"blocks out everything else and I get through the work in no time."},{"k":"h","s":91.1,"e":91.1,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":94.49,"e":97.41,"t":"When I do my homework, I have to feel right."},{"s":98.01,"e":102.69,"t":"After sitting on a hard chair all day, I need to stretch out with my head on a pillow."},{"s":103.45,"e":112.99,"t":"Mum says I can't possibly concentrate like that, but actually I don't fall asleep as long as I don't go on too late and I have the window open to get some fresh air."},{"s":113.88,"e":120.13,"t":"I'd love to work with music on. A lot of my friends do and they say it really helps them concentrate."},{"s":121.08,"e":126.97,"t":"The point is, I like music too much. It takes over from whatever I'm supposed to be doing."},{"k":"h","s":130.74,"e":130.74,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":133.94,"e":136.06,"t":"I'm hopeless at doing school projects."},{"s":136.6,"e":140.89,"t":"I make timetables so that I can complete the project well before the deadline."},{"s":141.34,"e":142.33,"t":"but I don't stick to"},{"s":142.87,"e":146.24,"t":"I've tried everything. Strong coffee, quiet rooms, fresh air."},{"s":146.68,"e":150.91,"t":"Even though I'm wide awake and there's nothing to disturb me, the work still doesn't get done."},{"s":151.51,"e":155.68,"t":"I was getting really worried last week when Mary came round and asked if she could work in my room."},{"s":156.18,"e":158.08,"t":"Hers is too dark and stuffy."},{"s":158.65,"e":162.65,"t":"I've never worked with a friend before and so I said no, but she was desperate"},{"s":163.13,"e":167.49,"t":"Eventually I gave in and it really worked out for us both. I couldn't believe it."},{"k":"h","s":171.26,"e":171.26,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":174.55,"e":190.53,"t":"I really like some of the subjects I'm doing this year, particularly maths and physics. I don't mind studying them at all, although some of the homework assignments we're given are quite tricky, so I need to be able to work undisturbed. That's often a bit difficult in our house, unless I put it off until everyone's in bed."},{"s":191.13,"e":200.96,"t":"Did you know that my younger brother Fred plays the guitar in a band? I love some of their music. It's really cool. You'd love it too. But it's pointless trying to work when he's playing."}]},{"n":18,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about hotels they have recently stayed in with their children. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi bolalari bilan yaqinda turgan mehmonxonalari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about hotels they have recently stayed in with their ch","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"Teenagers might not enjoy staying at this particular hotel.","u":"O'smirlarga aynan shu mehmonxona yoqmasligi mumkin."},{"l":"B","t":"The hotel was quite expensive.","u":"Mehmonxona ancha qimmat edi."},{"l":"C","t":"A playground would have improved the facilities.","u":"O'yin maydonchasi qulayliklarni yaxshilagan bo'lardi."},{"l":"D","t":"The hotel needed to know if you wanted your children to eat early.","u":"Bolalaringiz erta ovqatlanishini istasangiz, mehmonxonaga oldindan aytish kerak edi."},{"l":"E","t":"There was no swimming pool available in the hotel.","u":"Mehmonxonada suzish havzasi yo'q edi."},{"l":"F","t":"Children under ten were not allowed to stay at the hotel.","u":"O'n yoshgacha bolalarga mehmonxonada turish mumkin emas edi."}],"dur":399.2,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":16.28,"en":43.42,"ev":"They provided an early supper if you told them in good time so that the parents could eat in peace later.","uz":"Oldindan aytib qo'ysangiz, bolalarga erta kechki ovqat berishardi, shunda ota-onalar keyinroq tinch ovqatlanishi mumkin edi.","why":"\"If you told them in good time\" — oldindan aytish kerak (D). Arzon edi (B emas), bog'da maydoncha bor (C emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":47.13,"en":88.61,"ev":"Although it wasn't the cheapest around, far from it in fact, it was worth it.","uz":"Atrofdagi eng arzoni emasdi, aksincha, lekin bunga arzirdi.","why":"Qimmat bo'lgan (B). Hovuz bor edi (E emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":92.57,"en":127.2,"ev":"There was lots to do including horse riding and tennis, but if you wanted to swim you had to go to the local leisure centre.","uz":"Ot minish, tennis kabi ko'p mashg'ulotlar bor edi, lekin suzmoqchi bo'lsangiz, mahalliy dam olish markaziga borishingiz kerak edi.","why":"Hovuz yo'q — E. 10 yoshgacha bolalar bepul (F tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":131.32,"en":161.79,"ev":"So long as your children like swimming, you're alright, because there wasn't much else for them to do. I did think that they could have put in a playground too.","uz":"Bolalaringiz suzishni yaxshi ko'rsa, hammasi joyida, chunki ular uchun boshqa mashg'ulot kam edi. O'yin maydonchasi ham qurishsa bo'lardi deb o'yladim.","why":"Maydoncha yaxshilagan bo'lardi (C). 10 yoshgacha bolalar faqat ovqat xonasiga kirmaydi (F tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":165.88,"en":198.97,"ev":"The older children aren't really catered for and this hotel is probably better for those with younger kids.","uz":"Kattaroq bolalar uchun sharoit yo'q, bu mehmonxona kichik bolali oilalarga ko'proq mos.","why":"O'smirlarga yoqmasligi mumkin (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.12,"e":9.18,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about hotels they've recently stayed in with their children."},{"k":"h","s":16.28,"e":16.28,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":19.26,"e":23.55,"t":"We chose this hotel because we knew that the owners had young children of their own."},{"s":24.02,"e":27.45,"t":"The room could have been a bit bigger but then it was quite inexpensive."},{"s":28.15,"e":34.62,"t":"They provided an early supper if you told them in good time so that the parents could eat in peace later in the cosy dining room."},{"s":35.38,"e":41.21,"t":"There were hundreds of toys for the children to play with. A huge garden with a playground, ponds and a playhouse."},{"s":41.72,"e":43.42,"t":"We hardly saw our two all week."},{"k":"h","s":47.13,"e":47.13,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":50.14,"e":53.95,"t":"We always have difficulty finding hotels which welcome our children."},{"s":54.62,"e":59.23,"t":"This one was particularly good because the bedroom had a separate sitting room."},{"s":59.7,"e":61.95,"t":"so we weren't all squashed together in one room."},{"s":62.81,"e":66.56,"t":"Although it wasn't the cheapest around, far from it in fact,"},{"s":67.13,"e":67.93,"t":"It was worth it"},{"s":68.5,"e":80.7,"t":"Our teenage kids love the outdoor heated swimming pool and the mountain bikes which were provided free by the hotel. Apparently, the owners' kids who've grown up and left home now had been mad on mountain biking."},{"s":81.43,"e":83.77,"t":"There was also an all-weather tennis court."},{"s":84.34,"e":88.61,"t":"Another thing we liked was the separate dining room for people with young families."},{"k":"h","s":92.57,"e":92.57,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":95.61,"e":100.19,"t":"We'd had a bad experience the year before at a hotel which didn't cater for children."},{"s":100.66,"e":104.48,"t":"But this year we were very impressed by the hospitality of the hotel."},{"s":105.02,"e":112.32,"t":"The rooms were large enough to accommodate four beds comfortably, and there was an adventure playground in the garden for the younger kids."},{"s":112.76,"e":118.97,"t":"You don't have to pay for children under 10 sharing the room. Even meals were free for them, so that was another bonus."},{"s":119.42,"e":127.2,"t":"There was lots to do including horse riding and tennis, but if you wanted to swim you had to go to the local leisure centre, which the kids love."},{"k":"h","s":131.32,"e":131.32,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":134.36,"e":144.57,"t":"In the hotel we went to, we had a family suite which was very spacious. There was an outdoor heated pool and large grounds, so the kids spent most of the time in the pool."},{"s":145.11,"e":149.85,"t":"So long as your children like swimming, you're alright, because there wasn't much else for them to do."},{"s":150.42,"e":153.02,"t":"I did think that they could have put in a playground too."},{"s":153.5,"e":161.79,"t":"Young children under 10 aren't allowed in the dining room, but there was an early supper for them. This meant that we could have a quiet dinner for two when they were in bed."},{"k":"h","s":165.88,"e":165.88,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":169.27,"e":192.96,"t":"What we liked about our hotel was its size. It was only a small hotel and we were looked after like family. The room had loads of soft toys, wooden toys and books which the children loved. The guest lounge and conservatory was a child-free zone after 7.30, which suited us fine, because there was a special children's supper at 6, which meant that they could go to bed early and get a good night's sleep."},{"s":193.56,"e":198.97,"t":"The older children aren't really catered for and this hotel is probably better for those with younger kids."}]},{"n":19,"q":"You will hear five different cyclists talking about a long-distance race they took part in. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh velosipedchi qatnashgan uzoq masofali poyga haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different cyclists talking about a long-distance race they took part in","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I started the race but then decided not to continue.","u":"Poygani boshladim, lekin keyin davom ettirmaslikka qaror qildim."},{"l":"B","t":"I had to change bicycles during the race.","u":"Poyga davomida velosipedni almashtirishga majbur bo'ldim."},{"l":"C","t":"I felt uncomfortable on my bicycle throughout the race.","u":"Butun poyga davomida velosipedda o'zimni noqulay his qildim."},{"l":"D","t":"I had done some serious physical training for the race.","u":"Poygaga jiddiy jismoniy tayyorgarlik ko'rgan edim."},{"l":"E","t":"I think the organisers of the race were inefficient.","u":"Menimcha, poyga tashkilotchilari yaxshi ishlamadi."},{"l":"F","t":"I was satisfied with my performance in the race.","u":"Poygadagi natijamdan mamnun edim."}],"dur":417.3,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":13.46,"en":52.86,"ev":"When you ride at speed on rough tracks, it's hard to find an easy riding position, and as a result, you get an unpleasant stiffness in your back… The slight pain in my back didn't get any better.","uz":"Notekis yo'llarda tez haydaganda qulay holat topish qiyin, natijada belingiz yoqimsiz qotib qoladi… Belimdagi og'riq oxirigacha yaxshilanmadi.","why":"Butun poyga davomida noqulay (C). Velosiped shikastlanmagan, poygani tugatgan (A, B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":56.82,"en":91.33,"ev":"I'd been told before the start that there'd be a support team… Well they certainly weren't capable of running things properly because I had to wait far too long.","uz":"Startdan oldin yordam guruhi bo'lishi aytilgan edi… Lekin ular ishni to'g'ri tashkil qila olmadi, chunki juda uzoq kutishimga to'g'ri keldi.","why":"Tashkilotchilar yaxshi ishlamagan (E).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":95.26,"en":129.98,"ev":"However, halfway through, I realised my best option was to turn back. I hadn't done enough training.","uz":"Biroq yarim yo'lda eng to'g'ri yo'l — ortga qaytish ekanini angladim. Yetarlicha mashq qilmagan edim.","why":"Boshlab, keyin to'xtagan — A. Mashq qilmagan (D tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":134.14,"en":169.63,"ev":"I'm content with what I've achieved, although I didn't win any of the prizes.","uz":"Hech qanday sovrin olmagan bo'lsam ham, erishganlarimdan mamnunman.","why":"\"Content with what I've achieved\" — natijadan mamnun (F). Velosipedni avval ta'mirlatgan — poygada almashtirmagan (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":173.56,"en":206.37,"ev":"I was ready for the challenge after months of weightlifting to increase my strength.","uz":"Kuchimni oshirish uchun oylab og'ir atletika bilan shug'ullangach, sinovga tayyor edim.","why":"Jiddiy jismoniy tayyorgarlik — D. Velosiped buzilgan, lekin uni almashtirgani aytilmaydi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.22,"e":8.29,"t":"You'll hear five different cyclists talking about a long distance race they took part in."},{"k":"h","s":13.46,"e":13.46,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":16.47,"e":19.68,"t":"This was my first bike ride across the really difficult ground."},{"s":20.38,"e":29.31,"t":"When you ride at speed on rough tracks, it's hard to find an easy riding position, and as a result, you get an unpleasant stiffness in your back."},{"s":30.1,"e":33.28,"t":"You can stand up on the bike and that sometimes helps."},{"s":33.82,"e":35.04,"t":"But it didn't with me."},{"s":35.54,"e":36.41,"t":"on the country."},{"s":36.95,"e":43.04,"t":"I found myself flying over the handlebars a couple of times, landing on soft grass, luckily."},{"s":43.83,"e":47.84,"t":"If the bike had been damaged, I'd have stopped then and there, but it was okay."},{"s":48.6,"e":49.82,"t":"I carried on to the end."},{"s":50.39,"e":52.86,"t":"The slight pain in my back didn't get any better."},{"k":"h","s":56.82,"e":56.82,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":60.09,"e":73.73,"t":"We cycled through towns and also through remote areas and everything was fine until I came to a hilly bit. I knew I had an advantage here because I'm good at speeding up slopes. No aching muscles for me. But at some point during the climb"},{"s":74.17,"e":76.22,"t":"I noticed one of the wheels needed adjusting."},{"s":76.95,"e":91.33,"t":"been told before the start that there'd be a support team, so even if your bike broke down they'd be there to help you immediately. Well they certainly weren't capable of running things properly because I had to wait far too long and so was one of the last competitors to reach the finishing line."},{"k":"h","s":95.26,"e":95.26,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":98.84,"e":103.68,"t":"been involved in all the planning stages of the race and so it seemed a good idea to take part."},{"s":104.12,"e":107.97,"t":"However, halfway through, I realised my best option was to turn back."},{"s":108.41,"e":115.29,"t":"I hadn't done enough training. In a race like that you need to keep a regular speed even when you're going up what looks like a mountainside."},{"s":115.86,"e":120.67,"t":"If you are not fit enough, your leg muscles may seem to refuse to keep on pedalling hard."},{"s":121.56,"e":124.64,"t":"I saw other riders speeding past me. I couldn't believe it."},{"s":125.37,"e":129.98,"t":"Anyway, I thought this is silly. I may end up with a torn muscle. So that was that."},{"k":"h","s":134.14,"e":134.14,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":137.5,"e":145.66,"t":"Well I think I was just plain unlucky. I came up this village road and there were all these cars moving slowly uphill. There'd been an accident or something."},{"s":146.23,"e":150.62,"t":"Anyway, it was impossible to overtake them on such a narrow path, so they slowed me down."},{"s":151.32,"e":169.63,"t":"content with what I've achieved, although I didn't win any of the prizes. Basically, I managed all the difficult bits of the race, and I know that if it hadn't been for that problem, I would have had a good chance of winning. Also, my bike was great. I'd had it repaired recently and wasn't sure it would stand this test."},{"k":"h","s":173.56,"e":173.56,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":177.02,"e":183.23,"t":"I have lots of cycling experience but I knew this was going to be a long race and your muscles can get very tired and strained."},{"s":183.7,"e":187.13,"t":"but I was ready for the challenge after months of weightlifting to increase my strength."},{"s":187.8,"e":195.01,"t":"In fact, I could almost say I overdid it because I developed an elbow problem a couple of months before the race, which fortunately was not serious."},{"s":195.9,"e":198.4,"t":"I certainly wasn't expecting my bike to give me any trouble."},{"s":198.97,"e":200.51,"t":"But that's what happened, unfortunately."},{"s":200.98,"e":206.37,"t":"I had started the race feeling fitter than ever, so it was all the more disappointing that it had to end like this."}]},{"n":20,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about holidays they have had. How does each person feel about the holiday?","qu":"Besh kishi o'tkazgan ta'tili haqida gapiradi. Har biri ta'tili haqida qanday fikrda?","topic":"different people talking about holidays they have had","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"spent a long time planning the holiday","u":"ta'tilni uzoq rejalashtirgan"},{"l":"B","t":"regrets spending a lot of money","u":"ko'p pul sarflaganidan afsuslanadi"},{"l":"C","t":"was disappointed with the hotel","u":"mehmonxonadan hafsalasi pir bo'lgan"},{"l":"D","t":"had a very long holiday","u":"juda uzoq ta'til o'tkazgan"},{"l":"E","t":"enjoyed a very luxurious hotel","u":"juda hashamatli mehmonxonadan zavqlangan"},{"l":"F","t":"went somewhere interesting","u":"qiziqarli joyga borgan"}],"dur":266.3,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":9.53,"en":57.28,"ev":"She… said why didn't we just take off for a year and travel around the world?","uz":"U… nega bir yilga hammasini tashlab, dunyo bo'ylab sayohat qilmaymiz, dedi.","why":"Bir yillik sayohat — juda uzoq ta'til (D).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":60.38,"en":113.41,"ev":"It's something I've been looking into for some time… I started to do some serious research.","uz":"Bu men ancha vaqtdan beri o'rganayotgan narsa edi… jiddiy izlanish boshladim.","why":"Uzoq rejalashtirgan — A. Pul — arzon bo'lgan, afsus yo'q (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":116.54,"en":160.38,"ev":"All the time I kept thinking that it would have been a better idea if we'd used that money to buy a washing machine and some new furniture instead of going to all that expense.","uz":"Shu pulga kir yuvish mashinasi va yangi mebel olsak yaxshiroq bo'lardi, deb doim o'ylardim.","why":"Ko'p pul sarflaganidan afsuslanadi (B). Hashamatli mehmonxona yoqmagan (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":163.99,"en":208.45,"ev":"To tell you the truth, the hotel was a bit of a letdown… will definitely stay in a different hotel. That one wasn't good value for money at all.","uz":"Rostini aytsam, mehmonxona hafsalani pir qildi… albatta boshqa mehmonxonada turamiz. U narxiga umuman arzimasdi.","why":"Mehmonxonadan hafsalasi pir — C. Hudud yoqgan.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":211.61,"en":264.54,"ev":"From the moment you arrive there, you feel immersed in its history… When you see some of the collections they have in the museums… it's an extraordinary feeling.","uz":"Yetib kelgan zahotiyoq uning tarixiga sho'ng'iysiz… Muzeylardagi kolleksiyalarni ko'rganingizda… g'ayrioddiy his paydo bo'ladi.","why":"Tarixiy, qiziqarli joy — F. \"Need a month\" — ta'til bir hafta edi (D emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.22,"e":7.81,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about holidays they have had."},{"k":"h","s":9.53,"e":9.53,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":12.31,"e":14.56,"t":"It came as a complete surprise."},{"s":15.19,"e":26.72,"t":"Right out of the blue she came home and told me she'd been made redundant from work and said why didn't we just take off for a year and travel around the world? Well, it just all seemed to make sense."},{"s":27.26,"e":31.77,"t":"I wasn't enjoying my work at the time and was thinking about doing something else."},{"s":32.76,"e":38.56,"t":"had given her quite a generous redundancy package and also we could rent out our house for the year."},{"s":39.51,"e":48.96,"t":"give us enough to live on for the year as long as we were careful with our money. And I'm pleased to say that we were. Apart from the occasional few luxuries here and there."},{"s":49.53,"e":55.87,"t":"you know, meals and expensive restaurants for special occasions like birthdays or anniversaries."},{"s":56.79,"e":57.28,"t":"of thing"},{"k":"h","s":60.38,"e":60.38,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":63.22,"e":65.5,"t":"It's something I've been looking into for some time."},{"s":66.58,"e":67.65,"t":"to tell you the truth."},{"s":68.15,"e":70.91,"t":"It's something I've wanted to do ever since I was a kid."},{"s":71.93,"e":74.91,"t":"It just never seemed that it would be something I could realistically do."},{"s":75.96,"e":77.34,"t":"so it just remained a dream."},{"s":78.52,"e":84.7,"t":"But after somebody told me how cheap it was when you actually got there, I started to do some serious research."},{"s":86.04,"e":89.44,"t":"And really, although actually getting there is very expensive..."},{"s":90.07,"e":101.89,"t":"The price of the hotels, restaurants and travelling around the country is so low compared to places in Europe. It means that in total, you're not paying much more than you would for a cheap holiday on the beach in Greece or Spain."},{"s":103.16,"e":106.78,"t":"And it's a lot more interesting than just lying around on a beach somewhere."},{"s":107.48,"e":110.27,"t":"It was great. I'm going back there next year."},{"s":111.16,"e":113.41,"t":"I didn't think I would ever be able to say that."},{"k":"h","s":116.54,"e":116.54,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":119.45,"e":128.67,"t":"It's not every day you go on honeymoon, but if you ask me, it was all a bit over the top. We had our own private beach and the staff couldn't do enough for us."},{"s":129.24,"e":139.65,"t":"they wouldn't let us do a thing for ourselves. For example, if I try to pour myself a drink, somebody would suddenly appear and take the bottle out of my hand and finish pouring it."},{"s":140.12,"e":146.17,"t":"I know it's all these luxuries that you're paying for, but it's a bit much for me and wasn't something I was comfortable with."},{"s":147.32,"e":160.38,"t":"I suppose you must just get used to it after a while. But all the time I kept thinking that it would have been a better idea if we'd use that money to buy a washing machine and some new furniture instead of going to all that expense."},{"k":"h","s":163.99,"e":163.99,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":166.42,"e":169.44,"t":"To tell you the truth, the hotel was a bit of a letdown."},{"s":170.74,"e":181.05,"t":"in the brochure were flattering to say the very least. The restaurant was supposed to be five star, but I can honestly say I've had better food in a motorway service station."},{"s":181.91,"e":183.58,"t":"It wasn't all bad though."},{"s":184.06,"e":185.79,"t":"The area itself was lovely."},{"s":186.52,"e":190.21,"t":"beach near the village was lovely and had everything you could ask for."},{"s":190.78,"e":194.97,"t":"clean white sand, beautiful blue sea, palm trees,"},{"s":195.48,"e":199.55,"t":"and the locals were really friendly and really made a fuss of the kids."},{"s":200.31,"e":202.21,"t":"I think we'll go back there soon."},{"s":202.68,"e":208.45,"t":"but will definitely stay in a different hotel. That one wasn't good value for money at all."},{"k":"h","s":211.61,"e":211.61,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":214.55,"e":219.93,"t":"I'd really been looking forward to going there, and I wasn't disappointed. Not in the least."},{"s":220.54,"e":227.81,"t":"From the moment you arrive there, you feel immersed in its history. Hits the birthplace of civilization after all."},{"s":228.54,"e":231.45,"t":"Every street you walk down reminds you of this."},{"s":232.25,"e":239.84,"t":"I know some people wouldn't find it much fun to be going from boring museum to boring museum, but it wasn't like that."},{"s":240.47,"e":250.01,"t":"When you see some of the collections they have in the museums and you see it in context of the city itself, well, it's an extraordinary feeling."},{"s":250.81,"e":259.58,"t":"The weather wasn't great, but I don't think that's spoiled it for us at all. It's not like you go to a place like that just to sit on the beach and get a tan."},{"s":260.38,"e":264.54,"t":"We had a week there, but really you'd need a month just to see everything."}]},{"n":21,"q":"You will hear five different horoscopes on the radio. What does each horoscope say?","qu":"Radioda beshta munajjimlar bashorati (goroskop) eshitiladi. Har biri nima deydi?","topic":"different horoscopes on the radio","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"You will have a difficult year.","u":"Sizni qiyin yil kutmoqda."},{"l":"B","t":"You should think about getting married.","u":"Turmush qurish haqida o'ylashingiz kerak."},{"l":"C","t":"You can meet new companions.","u":"Yangi hamrohlar (do'stlar) bilan tanishishingiz mumkin."},{"l":"D","t":"You should take care at work.","u":"Ishda ehtiyot bo'lishingiz kerak."},{"l":"E","t":"You might get promoted.","u":"Lavozimingiz oshishi mumkin."},{"l":"F","t":"You are good with money.","u":"Pulni yaxshi boshqarasiz."}],"dur":322.7,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":11.9,"en":37.18,"ev":"Those of you with a job which involves routines should beware. You will feel like being carefree and irresponsible and this may cause difficulties in your employment.","uz":"Ishi bir xil tartibdan iborat bo'lganlar ehtiyot bo'lsin. O'zingizni beparvo va mas'uliyatsiz his qilasiz, bu ishingizda qiyinchiliklar tug'dirishi mumkin.","why":"Ishda ehtiyot bo'lish — D.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":40.34,"en":68.25,"ev":"You are naturally skilful in financial matters and someone will ask you for a loan. Don't do it!","uz":"Siz tabiatan moliyaviy ishlarda mohirsiz va kimdir sizdan qarz so'raydi. Bermang!","why":"Pulni yaxshi boshqaradi — F.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":71.32,"en":101.95,"ev":"This will be especially helpful in your job where advancement is a real possibility and you could go further up the ladder of success.","uz":"Bu ayniqsa ishingizda foydali bo'ladi: lavozimda ko'tarilish haqiqiy imkoniyat, muvaffaqiyat zinapoyasidan yuqoriroq chiqishingiz mumkin.","why":"\"Advancement… up the ladder\" — lavozim oshishi (E).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":104.98,"en":130.59,"ev":"For those of you thinking about choosing the right partner to settle down with, go ahead and propose. There'll never be a better time.","uz":"Hayotini birga o'tkazadigan juft tanlashni o'ylayotganlar — oldinga, turmush qurish taklifini qiling. Bundan yaxshiroq vaqt bo'lmaydi.","why":"\"Propose… settle down\" — turmush qurish (B).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":133.94,"en":156.8,"ev":"Situations will arise where you feel more confident about widening your social circle… your lonely days are at an end.","uz":"Tanishlar doirangizni kengaytirishda o'zingizni ishonchliroq his qiladigan vaziyatlar bo'ladi… yolg'izlik kunlaringiz tugaydi.","why":"Yangi tanishlar — C.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.62,"e":5.37,"t":"You'll hear five different horoscopes on the radio."},{"k":"h","s":11.9,"e":11.9,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.42,"e":21.37,"t":"Yours is an artistic and creative personality, and you work best independently, achieving a great deal."},{"s":22.23,"e":25.28,"t":"those of you with a job which involves routines should beware."},{"s":26.2,"e":31.26,"t":"You will feel like being carefree and irresponsible and this may cause difficulties in your employment."},{"s":31.8,"e":37.18,"t":"In your personal life, however, you can be less cautious and let your fun-loving imagination take over."},{"k":"h","s":40.34,"e":40.34,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":43.64,"e":51.23,"t":"You have a powerful and forceful nature, and the influence of the planet Mars at this time makes these characteristics even stronger."},{"s":51.93,"e":58.11,"t":"So, make sure you think carefully about your dealings with others and avoid upsetting them with your behavior and attitude."},{"s":59.22,"e":64.7,"t":"You are naturally skillful in financial matters and someone will ask you for a loan. Don't do it!"},{"s":65.14,"e":68.25,"t":"Instead, give them some good advice on how to budget."},{"k":"h","s":71.32,"e":71.32,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":74.78,"e":81.73,"t":"Your sign is that of the romantic and the dreamer. You prefer to sit back and think about great ideas rather than carry them out."},{"s":82.39,"e":88.06,"t":"Now you are under the influence of the planet Pluto, and it's time to take decisions and be more positive."},{"s":88.79,"e":95.77,"t":"This will be especially helpful in your job where advancement is a real possibility and you could go further up the ladder of success."},{"s":96.6,"e":101.95,"t":"Beware though that this newfound energy doesn't threaten your usual good health. Get plenty of sleep."},{"k":"h","s":104.98,"e":104.98,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":108.41,"e":114.69,"t":"For those of you born under this sign, partnership, either romantic or professional, will be most important this year."},{"s":115.32,"e":121.98,"t":"You don't naturally make decisions easily, but this could be a good time to make up your mind, especially where romance is concerned."},{"s":123.0,"e":130.59,"t":"For those of you thinking about choosing the right partner to settle down with, go ahead and propose. They'll never be a better time. Love is in the air."},{"k":"h","s":133.94,"e":133.94,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":137.34,"e":150.05,"t":"You are a naturally shy person who finds it difficult meeting new people and forming relationships. But things look more positive for you this year, and situations will arise where you feel more confident about widening your social circle."},{"s":151.16,"e":156.8,"t":"Don't be afraid to give it a try and you'll find your lonely days are at an end. Go out and enjoy yourself."}]},{"n":22,"q":"You will hear a woman describing five different recipes for desserts. Which recipe fits each description?","qu":"Ayol beshta shirinlik retseptini tasvirlaydi. Har bir ta'rif qaysi retseptga mos?","topic":"woman describing five different recipes for desserts","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"It is not suitable for vegetarians.","u":"Vegetarianlar uchun mos emas."},{"l":"B","t":"It cannot be made with fresh ingredients at Christmas.","u":"Rojdestvoda uni yangi masalliqlardan tayyorlab bo'lmaydi."},{"l":"C","t":"It is from an ancient recipe.","u":"Qadimiy retseptga asoslangan."},{"l":"D","t":"It involves no cooking.","u":"Pishirish talab qilinmaydi."},{"l":"E","t":"It is the easiest to make.","u":"Tayyorlash eng oson."},{"l":"F","t":"It is rather expensive.","u":"Ancha qimmat."}],"dur":518.3,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":16.12,"en":55.29,"ev":"You drip the honey over a thick layer of yoghurt… Then press the fruit into the honey and scatter chopped nuts over the top.","uz":"Qalin qatlam yogurt ustiga asal tomizasiz… Keyin mevani asalga bosib, ustiga maydalangan yong'oq sepasiz.","why":"Hamma bosqich — tayyor masalliqlarni yig'ish, pishirish yo'q (D). \"Isn't too difficult\" — lekin eng osoni emas.","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":58.39,"en":96.99,"ev":"I must just mention that gelatin is made from the hooves of cows, so unfortunately some people won't be too keen on this.","uz":"Aytib o'tishim kerak: jelatin sigir tuyog'idan tayyorlanadi, shuning uchun ba'zilarga bu yoqmaydi.","why":"Jelatin — vegetarianlar uchun mos emas (A).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":99.67,"en":146.53,"ev":"Strawberries need to be fresh so you will only really be able to make this recipe from May to early July… raspberries can be used instead up to late August.","uz":"Qulupnay yangi bo'lishi kerak, shuning uchun bu retseptni faqat maydan iyul boshigacha tayyorlash mumkin… avgust oxirigacha malina ishlatsa bo'ladi.","why":"Yozda yangi meva — demak Rojdestvo (dekabr)da yangi masalliq yo'q (B).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":149.11,"en":190.88,"ev":"It's such a simple method that they could even make it themselves.","uz":"Bu shunchalik oddiy usulki, bolalarning o'zi ham tayyorlay oladi.","why":"Eng oson — E. Arzon ham (\"inexpensive\") — F emas.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":193.75,"en":259.2,"ev":"You will need 250 grams of ground almonds. Now these are about £1.50 for a 50 gram packet, so you'll not want to waste any.","uz":"250 gramm maydalangan bodom kerak. 50 grammlik paketi taxminan 1,50 funt, shuning uchun isrof qilishni istamaysiz.","why":"Bodom qimmat — F.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.25,"e":10.24,"t":"You will hear five different people describing five different recipes for desserts."},{"k":"h","s":16.12,"e":16.12,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":16.12,"e":23.52,"t":"This is one of my favourite desserts and it isn't too difficult if you've got a bit of time on your hands."},{"s":24.54,"e":30.01,"t":"Traditional recipe uses brown sugar, but I have always preferred honey"},{"s":30.58,"e":36.0,"t":"You drip the honey over a thick layer of yoghurt to form a thin covering."},{"s":36.5,"e":40.25,"t":"This can be quite tricky and you need a steady hand."},{"s":40.79,"e":45.89,"t":"Then press the fruit into the honey and scatter chopped nuts over the top."},{"s":46.74,"e":55.29,"t":"Finally, to add that extra special something, put a few pinches of ground cinnamon over it shortly before serving."},{"k":"h","s":58.39,"e":58.39,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":60.44,"e":67.39,"t":"Once you've assembled all your chopped fruit pieces in a bowl, you need to make the blancmange mixture to pour over them."},{"s":68.15,"e":74.97,"t":"This is made by beating together cream, apple juice, honey and two tablespoons of rum."},{"s":75.86,"e":79.07,"t":"then heating the mixture before dissolving the gelatin."},{"s":80.12,"e":88.89,"t":"I must just mention that gelatin is made from the hooves of cows, so unfortunately some people won't be too keen on this."},{"s":89.69,"e":90.14,"t":"Anyway."},{"s":90.74,"e":96.99,"t":"Once the mixture has cooled sufficiently, it can be poured over the fruit and left to set in the refrigerator."},{"k":"h","s":99.67,"e":99.67,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":102.04,"e":111.55,"t":"Take the sponge cake base out of the oven and then turn it out to cool on a wire rack. Now you can turn your attention to the topping."},{"s":112.5,"e":125.31,"t":"Strawberries need to be fresh so you will only really be able to make this recipe from May to early July. After that, raspberries can be used instead up to late August."},{"s":126.04,"e":130.33,"t":"The fruit should be halved and have the tough cores removed."},{"s":131.19,"e":133.79,"t":"You may need a good sharp knife for this."},{"s":134.71,"e":146.53,"t":"After that, arrange the halves in a symmetrical pattern around the top of the sponge. And finally, spread fresh yoghurt over this and garnish with grated chocolate."},{"k":"h","s":149.11,"e":149.11,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":151.48,"e":154.72,"t":"Now this one is always popular with youngsters."},{"s":155.26,"e":162.78,"t":"There is really no point nowadays in making your own vanilla ice cream since the quality in the shops is so good."},{"s":163.35,"e":169.02,"t":"But homemade chocolate sauce is another matter and quite inexpensive to make."},{"s":169.72,"e":178.01,"t":"You just heat some cooking chocolate in a pan with a little water and brown sugar and bring to the boil for a few minutes."},{"s":178.62,"e":180.99,"t":"When it has cooled you'll have a thick"},{"s":181.53,"e":190.88,"t":"dark sticky sauce that the kids will love and indeed it's such a simple method that they could even make it themselves."},{"k":"h","s":193.75,"e":193.75,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":196.22,"e":198.69,"t":"Once again you leave the sponge cake."},{"s":199.13,"e":203.55,"t":"Cool after baking and turn your attention to the marzipan."},{"s":204.28,"e":218.85,"t":"you will need 250 grams of ground almonds. Now these are about £1.50 for a 50 gram packet, so you'll not want to waste any."},{"s":220.15,"e":237.15,"t":"ground almonds with 250 grams of caster sugar and add a whole egg that's been thoroughly beaten and laced with dark rum and almond flavoring."},{"s":237.78,"e":248.57,"t":"knead the mixture into a thick paste and then roll flat on a work surface sprinkled with icing sugar."},{"s":249.5,"e":259.2,"t":"Brush the sponge cake with a mixture of rum and almond flavouring before placing the marzipan around it."}]},{"n":23,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about the head teacher or principal of their former secondary school. What is each speaker saying?","qu":"Besh kishi sobiq maktab direktori haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about the head teacher or principal of their former sec","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"She favoured the talented students.","u":"U iqtidorli o'quvchilarni afzal ko'rardi."},{"l":"B","t":"She prepared us for the real world.","u":"U bizni haqiqiy hayotga tayyorladi."},{"l":"C","t":"She encouraged us to be imaginative.","u":"U bizni ijodkor (xayolparast) bo'lishga undadi."},{"l":"D","t":"She was ahead of her time.","u":"U o'z davridan oldinda edi."},{"l":"E","t":"She was concerned about the environment.","u":"U atrof-muhit haqida qayg'urardi."},{"l":"F","t":"She encouraged competitiveness.","u":"U raqobatni rag'batlantirardi."}],"dur":389.5,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":14.39,"en":49.79,"ev":"She was always encouraging us not to drop litter and to think about things like preserving the countryside and so on.","uz":"U bizni doim axlat tashlamaslikka va tabiatni asrash kabi narsalar haqida o'ylashga undardi.","why":"Atrof-muhit haqida qayg'urgan (E).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":53.3,"en":82.43,"ev":"Whatever we were doing she was always pushing us to do it faster than anyone else or jump higher than our friends.","uz":"Nima qilmaylik, u bizni doim boshqalardan tezroq bajarishga yoki do'stlarimizdan balandroq sakrashga undardi.","why":"Raqobatni rag'batlantirgan (F). Iqtidordan qat'i nazar — iqtidorlilarni afzal ko'rmagan (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":86.14,"en":117.37,"ev":"There were people in my class who were really talented artists… She always preferred the more unusual stuff. She said it showed we had ideas of our own.","uz":"Sinfimizda haqiqatan iqtidorli rassomlar bor edi… U doim g'ayrioddiyroq ishlarni afzal ko'rardi. Bu bizning o'z g'oyalarimiz borligini ko'rsatadi, derdi.","why":"Ijodkorlikni rag'batlantirgan (C). Iqtidorlilarni emas, g'ayrioddiy g'oyalarni qadrlagan (A tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":121.02,"en":154.4,"ev":"So many ideas she had which were never taken up are being used in schools today.","uz":"Uning o'sha paytda qabul qilinmagan ko'plab g'oyalari bugun maktablarda qo'llanilmoqda.","why":"O'z davridan oldinda bo'lgan (D).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":158.07,"en":192.77,"ev":"Our head teacher built up a good network of contacts with local people… giving us an insight into what it might be like, say, working in a hospital or office.","uz":"Direktorimiz mahalliy odamlar bilan yaxshi aloqalar o'rnatgan edi… ular bizga kasalxona yoki ofisda ishlash qanday bo'lishini ko'rsatishdi.","why":"Haqiqiy hayotga tayyorlagan (B). \"Wasn't a new idea\" — D emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.06,"e":10.17,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about the head teacher or principal of their former secondary school."},{"k":"h","s":14.39,"e":14.39,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.43,"e":19.26,"t":"It's strange looking back because..."},{"s":20.15,"e":22.24,"t":"time you don't always appreciate people"},{"s":23.1,"e":25.37,"t":"And certainly I think that's true of your teachers."},{"s":26.26,"e":27.61,"t":"particularly a head teacher."},{"s":28.95,"e":35.58,"t":"I mean, she was always encouraging us not to drop litter and to think about things like preserving the countryside and so on."},{"s":36.79,"e":37.53,"t":"and she'd say"},{"s":38.26,"e":41.21,"t":"Don't you want your children to live in a better world?"},{"s":41.94,"e":45.31,"t":"But when you're 15, you can't imagine having a family."},{"s":45.85,"e":49.79,"t":"All you care about is getting your homework done and going out with your friends."},{"k":"h","s":53.3,"e":53.3,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.5,"e":64.13,"t":"I don't know if it's the same in all countries, but where I live, your head teacher usually teaches classes too. And we had our head for athletics."},{"s":64.73,"e":82.43,"t":"In one way it was exciting because she was very good at it herself like she could outrun any of the boys in our class. But whatever we were doing she was always pushing us to do it faster than anyone else or jump higher than our friends regardless of the talent or ability we had and with some it was pointless."},{"k":"h","s":86.14,"e":86.14,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":89.24,"e":93.44,"t":"I think if it hadn't been for our head teacher I'd be doing something quite different now."},{"s":94.39,"e":100.25,"t":"She used to assess our art exams and although there were people in my class who were really talented artists..."},{"s":101.24,"e":104.35,"t":"you know, they could paint anything from real life and it looked brilliant."},{"s":104.98,"e":109.89,"t":"She always preferred the more unusual stuff. She said it showed we had ideas of our own."},{"s":110.68,"e":113.31,"t":"and she really liked that so I did well"},{"s":113.94,"e":117.37,"t":"I mean, now I make a living putting designs on greeting cards."},{"k":"h","s":121.02,"e":121.02,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":124.15,"e":129.92,"t":"I always felt that our head teacher was undervalued and that she might have done better in a different environment."},{"s":130.46,"e":133.02,"t":"Her own staff held her up a bit."},{"s":133.5,"e":138.56,"t":"They all seemed... Oh, I don't know. Maybe they just didn't like the idea of change."},{"s":139.48,"e":146.59,"t":"I remember she wanted to introduce a new teaching method for French classes and the department head just dismissed the idea."},{"s":147.26,"e":152.03,"t":"and so many ideas she had which were never taken up or being used in schools today."},{"s":152.7,"e":154.4,"t":"I sometimes wonder how she feels."},{"k":"h","s":158.07,"e":158.07,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":161.3,"e":165.25,"t":"I've got some friends who say they left school and they suddenly felt lost."},{"s":166.1,"e":171.04,"t":"spent a long time getting an education but didn't know what to do once they'd got it."},{"s":171.9,"e":177.82,"t":"I think we were lucky because our head teacher built up a good network of contacts with local people."},{"s":178.36,"e":184.77,"t":"And so they didn't mind giving us an insight into what it might be like, say, working in a hospital or office."},{"s":185.72,"e":192.77,"t":"I know it wasn't a new idea or anything, but I think she gave us a good sense of direction, which I valued all my life."}]},{"n":24,"q":"You will hear part of a radio programme called Morning Market. Five listeners have telephoned because they have something to sell. What is each person's reason for selling?","qu":"\"Morning Market\" radio dasturiga besh tinglovchi biror narsasini sotish uchun qo'ng'iroq qiladi. Har birining sotish sababi nima?","topic":"part of a radio programme called Morning Market","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I didn't enjoy using it.","u":"Uni ishlatish menga yoqmadi."},{"l":"B","t":"I made a mistake.","u":"Xato qildim."},{"l":"C","t":"It's an unwanted prize.","u":"Bu menga kerak bo'lmagan sovrin."},{"l":"D","t":"It takes up too much space.","u":"U juda ko'p joy egallaydi."},{"l":"E","t":"I've got something better.","u":"Menda yaxshiroq narsa bor."},{"l":"F","t":"I have health problems.","u":"Sog'lig'imda muammo bor."}],"dur":450.7,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":18.42,"en":56.32,"ev":"I won it actually… I'll never use it because I was after the holiday which was won by whoever came first in the competition.","uz":"Aslida uni yutib olganman… Uni hech qachon ishlatmayman, chunki men tanlovda birinchi o'rin uchun berilgan ta'tilni yutmoqchi edim.","why":"Kerak bo'lmagan sovrin (C). \"Won't take up too much space\" — D tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":59.86,"en":100.38,"ev":"It's still in its original packing case because I ordered the wrong colour.","uz":"U hali ham asl qutisida, chunki noto'g'ri rang buyurtma qilgan edim.","why":"Xato qilgan (B).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":105.08,"en":144.8,"ev":"With us having a baby on the way, it's got to make way for more essential items as we've only got a tiny flat at the moment.","uz":"Farzand kutayotganimiz uchun u muhimroq narsalarga joy bo'shatishi kerak — hozircha kichkina kvartiramiz bor.","why":"Juda ko'p joy egallaydi (D).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":148.98,"en":189.47,"ev":"I've got back trouble and I've been advised not to ride it.","uz":"Belimda muammo bor va uni minmaslikni maslahat berishdi.","why":"Sog'lig'ida muammo (F). Velosipedni ko'p ishlatgan — yoqmagan emas (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":193.18,"en":225.05,"ev":"At one time I was intending to do a lot of this type of cooking… but I've been given a microwave instead now, so much easier to use.","uz":"Bir paytlar bunday ovqatlarni ko'p pishirmoqchi edim… lekin endi menga mikroto'lqinli pech berishdi, uni ishlatish ancha oson.","why":"Yaxshiroq narsa bor — E.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.9,"e":7.49,"t":"You'll hear part of a radio program called Morning Market."},{"s":8.41,"e":12.54,"t":"Five listeners have telephoned the program because they have something to sell."},{"k":"h","s":18.42,"e":18.42,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":21.43,"e":23.1,"t":"I've got a brand new rowing machine."},{"s":23.74,"e":24.7,"t":"won it actually."},{"s":25.18,"e":27.55,"t":"about two months ago and it's still in its box."},{"s":28.18,"e":31.58,"t":"It's got an electric timer on it which tells you how much rowing you've done and all"},{"s":32.06,"e":35.81,"t":"So anyone who's into exercise can do lots of rowing and keep fit and healthy."},{"s":36.47,"e":42.65,"t":"It folds up really small so it won't take up too much space in a bedroom or anything."},{"s":43.86,"e":44.29,"t":"I mean"},{"s":44.86,"e":49.6,"t":"I'll never use it because I was after the holiday which was won by whoever came first in the competition."},{"s":50.3,"e":53.15,"t":"So I'm looking for around 45 pounds."},{"s":53.59,"e":56.32,"t":"and my number is uh... double seven three"},{"k":"h","s":59.86,"e":59.86,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":63.19,"e":76.61,"t":"I've got a kidney-shaped bath, a colour soft cream for sale. It's still in its original packing case because I ordered the wrong colour. You know, it didn't go with the rest of the bathroom suite I'd got."},{"s":77.05,"e":87.36,"t":"So I contacted, you know, the suppliers who said they'll send me a replacement at a price, of course. But I've now got to get rid of this one."},{"s":88.7,"e":98.69,"t":"I passed originally 175 pounds and I'm letting it go for 50 if anyone's interested. Okay, my numbers..."},{"s":99.22,"e":100.38,"t":"017"},{"k":"h","s":105.08,"e":105.08,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":108.38,"e":116.16,"t":"I've got a real bargain. It's a Lieberstein electric organ and it's got two keyboards and a rhythm section."},{"s":116.7,"e":122.97,"t":"It's in good condition, plays quite well and it's not difficult to use or anything."},{"s":124.5,"e":132.13,"t":"With us having a baby on the way, it's got to make way for more essential items as we've only got a tiny flat at the moment."},{"s":132.66,"e":136.61,"t":"So, as I say, if anyone wants it, they can make me an offer."},{"s":137.3,"e":141.25,"t":"The only problem is anyone interested would have to come and collect it."},{"s":141.85,"e":144.8,"t":"the number to ring is 672..."},{"k":"h","s":148.98,"e":148.98,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":152.22,"e":152.83,"t":"Hello?"},{"s":153.72,"e":155.74,"t":"I got a lady's cycle for sale."},{"s":156.18,"e":162.91,"t":"I've got back trouble and I've been advised not to ride it. So rather than be tempted, I'll get rid of it."},{"s":163.7,"e":168.29,"t":"I hate the idea because we're not well served with public transport out here."},{"s":168.79,"e":170.21,"t":"and I used it quite a lot."},{"s":170.87,"e":178.46,"t":"But as I daren't ride it anymore, I think it would be a mistake to hang on to it. You know, in case I had second thoughts."},{"s":179.13,"e":179.49,"t":"soup"},{"s":180.02,"e":181.31,"t":"It's a rally chopper."},{"s":181.91,"e":182.4,"t":"Pink."},{"s":182.84,"e":185.25,"t":"and I'd like £35 for it please."},{"s":186.2,"e":189.47,"t":"can be contacted on 0181"},{"k":"h","s":193.18,"e":193.18,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":196.82,"e":200.83,"t":"got two frying pans, you know, the sort for cooking stir frying."},{"s":201.3,"e":203.29,"t":"and a seven piece tool set to go with them."},{"s":203.8,"e":204.93,"t":"all boxed and everything"},{"s":205.69,"e":218.27,"t":"Anyway, they've only been used because at one time I was intending to do a lot of this type of cooking because I've only got a small kitchenette like no oven but I've been given a microwave instead now so much easier to use."},{"s":218.78,"e":225.05,"t":"So that's 10 pounds for both pans and the tools."}]},{"n":25,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about their work as teachers. Which statement applies to each person?","qu":"Besh kishi o'qituvchilik ishi haqida gapiradi. Qaysi gap kimga tegishli?","topic":"different people talking about their work as teachers","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"This teacher is not always confident.","u":"Bu o'qituvchi har doim ham o'ziga ishonmaydi."},{"l":"B","t":"This teacher cannot use a computer.","u":"Bu o'qituvchi kompyuterdan foydalana olmaydi."},{"l":"C","t":"This teacher has a lot of talented students.","u":"Bu o'qituvchining iqtidorli o'quvchilari ko'p."},{"l":"D","t":"This teacher advises colleagues on teaching.","u":"Bu o'qituvchi hamkasblariga o'qitish bo'yicha maslahat beradi."},{"l":"E","t":"This teacher continues to learn more about teaching.","u":"Bu o'qituvchi o'qitish haqida o'rganishda davom etmoqda."},{"l":"F","t":"This teacher takes their students on educational trips.","u":"Bu o'qituvchi o'quvchilarini ma'rifiy sayohatlarga olib boradi."}],"dur":496.2,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":13.72,"en":49.15,"ev":"I've attended a number of in-service training courses to make sure I'm up to date with new methods of teaching maths.","uz":"Matematika o'qitishning yangi usullaridan xabardor bo'lish uchun bir qancha malaka oshirish kurslarida qatnashdim.","why":"O'qitish haqida o'rganishda davom etadi (E). Kompyuter qiyin, lekin \"cannot use\" emas (B tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":52.57,"en":94.43,"ev":"I'd like to think my own colleagues at school look to me for guidance on matters of methodology. I'd like to pass on my experience to my department.","uz":"Hamkasblarim metodika bo'yicha mendan yo'l-yo'riq so'raydi deb o'ylashni xohlayman. Tajribamni kafedramga yetkazmoqchiman.","why":"Hamkasblarga maslahat beradi (D).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":99.64,"en":156.48,"ev":"We also have a lot of trips to museums and other places of interest, and this motivates students enormously.","uz":"Bizda muzeylar va boshqa qiziqarli joylarga ko'p sayohatlar bor, bu o'quvchilarni juda rag'batlantiradi.","why":"Ma'rifiy sayohatlar (F).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":161.94,"en":202.37,"ev":"Oh, they're so gifted some of these children. We always get five or six with music scholarships to university or music college.","uz":"Oh, bu bolalarning ba'zilari juda iqtidorli. Har yili besh-oltitasi universitet yoki musiqa kollejiga grant oladi.","why":"Iqtidorli o'quvchilar ko'p (C).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":207.64,"en":242.94,"ev":"I don't know if they really work though. I get very nervous in front of the class and I think it shows. I'm sure the other teachers are better.","uz":"Ular haqiqatan ishlaydimi, bilmayman. Sinf oldida juda hayajonlanaman, bu sezilsa kerak. Boshqa o'qituvchilar mendan yaxshiroq deb o'ylayman.","why":"O'ziga ishonmaydi (A). O'quvchilari aqlli, lekin javob — A.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.71,"e":4.57,"t":"You will hear five different people."},{"s":5.05,"e":7.13,"t":"talking about their work as teachers."},{"k":"h","s":13.72,"e":13.72,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.08,"e":19.39,"t":"been teaching maths for 35 years."},{"s":20.15,"e":22.78,"t":"And naturally I've seen a lot of changes in that time."},{"s":23.64,"e":30.21,"t":"I've attended a number of in-service training courses to make sure I'm up to date with new methods of teaching maths."},{"s":31.48,"e":34.75,"t":"It's useful to hear about different ways to teach successfully."},{"s":35.32,"e":36.8,"t":"I think that's important."},{"s":37.78,"e":42.37,"t":"Of course it's the computer age now, so that's taken quite a lot of getting used to."},{"s":43.9,"e":49.15,"t":"I have to admit, some of my students seem to know a lot more about computers than I do."},{"k":"h","s":52.57,"e":52.57,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":55.61,"e":64.61,"t":"I went to Cambridge University and trained to be a teacher to get the best possible background for successful teaching career."},{"s":65.43,"e":77.31,"t":"I regularly take magazines like modern English teacher and English teaching today and I even write articles for them. I'd like to give new teachers some ideas to help them."},{"s":77.94,"e":83.52,"t":"I'd like to think my own colleagues at school look to me for guidance on matters of methodology."},{"s":83.99,"e":90.4,"t":"I'd like to pass on my experience to my department. Of course, I don't want to dictate to my colleagues."},{"s":91.0,"e":94.43,"t":"But I always appreciated the help I was given as a new teacher."},{"k":"h","s":99.64,"e":99.64,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":102.52,"e":103.9,"t":"I teach history."},{"s":104.44,"e":109.09,"t":"And I think most of my students find it an interesting subject."},{"s":109.91,"e":114.08,"t":"I hope we give the students an overall view of the subject."},{"s":115.03,"e":118.01,"t":"The department believes in choosing a topic."},{"s":118.49,"e":127.52,"t":"for instance, the Romans, and looking at it not just from a purely historical point of view, you know, names and dates."},{"s":127.96,"e":131.39,"t":"but the geographical and sociological angle as well."},{"s":132.44,"e":135.26,"t":"the students do a lot of project based work."},{"s":135.83,"e":140.19,"t":"and by doing this they get more involved in the topics."},{"s":140.79,"e":146.01,"t":"We also have a lot of trips to museums and other places of interest."},{"s":146.62,"e":149.44,"t":"and this motivates students enormously."},{"s":150.26,"e":156.48,"t":"It helps for them not only to read books, but to see where historic events took place."},{"k":"h","s":161.94,"e":161.94,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":164.92,"e":167.04,"t":"Yes, the music department isn't bad."},{"s":167.7,"e":172.06,"t":"We encourage all the pupils to play an instrument and sing in one of the choirs."},{"s":172.66,"e":174.62,"t":"It's very pleasing that most of them do."},{"s":175.29,"e":178.43,"t":"We had to create a third orchestra to cope with the demand."},{"s":179.1,"e":183.61,"t":"The boys and girls like to take exams too. That's a change from when I came."},{"s":184.22,"e":189.02,"t":"We have a pass rate of well over 90%, by far the best in the area."},{"s":189.72,"e":192.06,"t":"Oh, they're so gifted some of these children."},{"s":192.76,"e":197.15,"t":"We always get five or six with music scholarships to university or music college."},{"s":197.88,"e":202.37,"t":"and one of our violinists won the British Young Musician of the Year a couple of years ago."},{"k":"h","s":207.64,"e":207.64,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":210.3,"e":213.79,"t":"It's so difficult with science teaching to know if you're doing it right."},{"s":214.26,"e":218.08,"t":"The pupils here are so clever and they really deserve every chance I can give them."},{"s":218.71,"e":225.53,"t":"I try to take the syllabus and find new ways of explaining the subjects. And I design experiments to illustrate them."},{"s":226.1,"e":227.9,"t":"I don't know if they really work though."},{"s":228.57,"e":231.68,"t":"I get very nervous in front of the class and I think it shows."},{"s":232.25,"e":233.95,"t":"I'm sure the other teachers are better."},{"s":234.68,"e":242.94,"t":"Still, the exam results were quite good last year and the pupils gave me a present at the end of the last class before the summer holidays. It was really very nice of them."}]},{"n":26,"q":"You will hear five different people being interviewed on the radio about Christmas. Which words best describe their feelings about this celebration?","qu":"Radioda besh kishidan Rojdestvo haqida intervyu olinadi. Ularning bu bayramga munosabati qanday?","topic":"different people being interviewed on the radio about Christmas","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"feels enthusiastic","u":"ishtiyoqli"},{"l":"B","t":"feels bored with it","u":"undan zerikkan"},{"l":"C","t":"feels upset by it","u":"undan xafa (bezovta)"},{"l":"D","t":"feels unappreciated","u":"o'zini qadrlanmagan his qiladi"},{"l":"E","t":"feels satisfied","u":"mamnun"},{"l":"F","t":"feels happier than expected","u":"kutganidan ko'ra xursandroq"}],"dur":456.4,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":12.6,"en":43.42,"ev":"I went to a lot of effort this year to make it something special… And I don't seem to remember a single person actually saying thank you and really meaning it.","uz":"Bu yil uni alohida qilish uchun ko'p harakat qildim… Va hech kim chin dildan \"rahmat\" deganini eslolmayman.","why":"Mehnati qadrlanmagan — D.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":47.19,"en":93.76,"ev":"Just as I was putting the chicken into the oven, there was a knock at the door… would I like to join them. And of course, I had a wonderful time.","uz":"Tovuqni pechga qo'yayotganimda eshik taqilladi… ularga qo'shilishni taklif qilishdi. Albatta, ajoyib vaqt o'tkazdim.","why":"Yolg'iz qolishni kutgan, lekin ajoyib o'tdi — kutganidan xursandroq (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":97.37,"en":137.15,"ev":"It isn't over yet… there's so much more to Christmas than that… So I'll be taking my grandchildren up to Coniston Hill for some tobogganing.","uz":"Hali tugamadi… Rojdestvo faqat shu emas… Nevaralarimni chana uchish uchun Koniston tepaligiga olib boraman.","why":"Ko'plab rejalar, ishtiyoq — A.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":140.6,"en":182.85,"ev":"It wasn't as good as it's been in the past… our video machine broke down on Christmas day, so there's been nothing to watch all Christmas.","uz":"O'tmishdagidek yaxshi bo'lmadi… Rojdestvo kuni videomagnitofonimiz buzildi, butun bayram ko'radigan hech narsa bo'lmadi.","why":"Zerikkan — B.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":186.33,"en":226.08,"ev":"You should have seen the number of baby cats, dogs and rabbits that people were buying as presents… But what's most distressing is the tropical birds.","uz":"Odamlar sovg'a uchun qancha mushukcha, kuchukcha va quyoncha sotib olayotganini ko'rsangiz edi… Eng achinarlisi — tropik qushlar.","why":"\"Distressing\" — xafa, bezovta (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.55,"e":7.2,"t":"You will hear five different people being interviewed on the radio about Christmas."},{"k":"h","s":12.6,"e":12.6,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":14.97,"e":43.42,"t":"Well, I suppose some of it was quite nice, but it really could have been so much better. After all, I went to a lot of effort this year to make it something special, but somehow it didn't quite work. I mean, everybody had masses to eat. There were eight of us sitting down to dinner, and we must have spent a fortune on presents this year. But looking around the room, you couldn't see it in people's faces. And then there was all the quarrelling over what we were going to watch on TV. And I don't seem to remember a single person actually saying thank you and really meaning it."},{"k":"h","s":47.19,"e":47.19,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":49.37,"e":60.35,"t":"I was all set to have another unexcited Christmas in the bedsitter where I'm living now. Of course I'd sent my kids Christmas presents but I knew I wouldn't be hearing from them."},{"s":60.95,"e":62.72,"t":"My ex-wife doesn't allow it."},{"s":63.22,"e":77.31,"t":"So I bought myself a two pound chicken from Dewhurst's and a four pack of Lime Brand Extra and I got a stack of pound coins for the electric meter so that at least I could be warm and watch some telly."},{"s":78.23,"e":78.75,"t":"and then"},{"s":79.19,"e":93.76,"t":"Just as I was putting the chicken into the oven, there was a knock at the door, and it was the father of the family just across the road, saying they noticed that I was going to be alone that day, and would I like to join them. And of course, I had a wonderful time."},{"k":"h","s":97.37,"e":97.37,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":99.64,"e":107.39,"t":"It isn't over yet. I mean, we've had the actual festivities on the 25th, but there's so much more to Christmas than that."},{"s":108.41,"e":113.63,"t":"Our parish church is putting on a festival of nine lessons and carols on Sunday evening."},{"s":114.07,"e":120.48,"t":"and if that's not your cup of tea, then there's the Charitable Association Santa Claus Prime Race on Monday"},{"s":120.98,"e":123.29,"t":"although I won't be taking part in that this year."},{"s":123.93,"e":126.24,"t":"And this Christmas it's even been snowing!"},{"s":126.78,"e":130.81,"t":"So I'll be taking my grandchildren up to Coniston Hill for some tobogganing."},{"s":131.35,"e":134.43,"t":"Or they can build a snowman if the snow is good enough."},{"s":134.87,"e":137.15,"t":"That's on Tuesday. And then..."},{"k":"h","s":140.6,"e":140.6,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":142.97,"e":145.76,"t":"It wasn't as good as it's been in the past."},{"s":146.52,"e":151.29,"t":"For a start the tele was pretty disappointing, especially after last years."},{"s":151.86,"e":158.37,"t":"I mean, we had Terminator last Christmas Eve, but all we got this year was RoboCop again."},{"s":159.0,"e":162.37,"t":"And the weather, the weather's been really bad."},{"s":162.81,"e":172.38,"t":"So most of the football was cancelled. And then to top it all, our video machine broke down on Christmas day, so there's been nothing to watch all Christmas."},{"s":172.98,"e":179.58,"t":"And then, just to finish off any last chance of a decent holiday, someone suggested we all play Monopoly."},{"s":180.12,"e":182.85,"t":"Well, I went out to walk the dog in the snow."},{"k":"h","s":186.33,"e":186.33,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":188.57,"e":208.96,"t":"Well, I wouldn't say I enjoyed it. I spent the three days before the 25th standing outside Fielding's pet shop with a placard trying to stop people buying pets as presents. And did they listen? People were going in and out of the pet shop all day and you should have seen the number of baby cats, dogs and rabbits that people were buying as presents."},{"s":209.4,"e":226.08,"t":"And you know what's going to happen to them? The same as every year. A week after Christmas, they'll be out on the streets, fending for themselves in temperatures well below zero. But what's most distressing is the tropical birds. These beautiful animals can die in a matter of hours if left outside."}]},{"n":27,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about exercise. Which statement applies to each person?","qu":"Besh kishi jismoniy mashqlar haqida gapiradi. Qaysi gap kimga tegishli?","topic":"different people talking about exercise","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"This person spends most of their free time exercising.","u":"Bu kishi bo'sh vaqtining ko'pini mashq bilan o'tkazadi."},{"l":"B","t":"This person is made to do exercise against their will.","u":"Bu kishi xohishiga qarshi mashq qilishga majbur."},{"l":"C","t":"This person does a lot of exercise in spite of their age.","u":"Bu kishi yoshiga qaramay ko'p mashq qiladi."},{"l":"D","t":"This person does exercise as part of their job.","u":"Bu kishi ishining bir qismi sifatida mashq qiladi."},{"l":"E","t":"This person does exercise as part of a social event.","u":"Bu kishi ijtimoiy tadbir doirasida mashq qiladi."},{"l":"F","t":"This person's good health depends on exercise.","u":"Bu kishining sog'lig'i mashqqa bog'liq."}],"dur":455.3,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":10.81,"en":45.76,"ev":"It seems a bit crazy having all these ambitions at 70, but I've never really been your typical stay-at-home grandmother.","uz":"70 yoshda bunday orzular biroz aqldan ozganlikdek tuyuladi, lekin men hech qachon uyda o'tiradigan oddiy buvi bo'lmaganman.","why":"Yoshiga qaramay ko'p mashq qiladi (C).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":49.11,"en":92.22,"ev":"I swim two miles a day before work, and after I get home from the office, I work out in the gym for about two or three hours… My friends sometimes complain that I don't have enough time for them.","uz":"Ishdan oldin har kuni ikki mil suzaman, ofisdan qaytgach, sport zalida ikki-uch soat shug'ullanaman… Do'stlarim ba'zan ularga vaqtim yo'qligidan shikoyat qilishadi.","why":"Bo'sh vaqtining ko'pi mashqqa ketadi (A).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":95.64,"en":136.25,"ev":"It's fun, 'cause we're all mates. We've known each other for years, and so it means we get to see each other regularly.","uz":"Bu qiziqarli, chunki hammamiz do'stmiz. Bir-birimizni yillar davomida taniymiz, shu tufayli muntazam ko'rishib turamiz.","why":"Do'stlar bilan ijtimoiy tadbir sifatida (E).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":139.7,"en":183.23,"ev":"Every day we're sent outside, even when it's freezing cold, to play hockey or football… I hate it.","uz":"Har kuni, hatto qahraton sovuqda ham, bizni xokkey yoki futbol o'ynashga tashqariga chiqarishadi… Men buni yomon ko'raman.","why":"Xohishiga qarshi majburlangan maktab o'quvchisi (B).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":186.65,"en":223.71,"ev":"The doctor says I should try to get regular exercise… I didn't really have an active life before the attack, but it really scared me.","uz":"Shifokor muntazam mashq qilishimni aytdi… Xurujdan oldin faol hayot kechirmasdim, lekin u meni juda qo'rqitdi.","why":"Sog'lig'i mashqqa bog'liq (F).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.13,"e":6.94,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about exercise."},{"k":"h","s":10.81,"e":10.81,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":13.85,"e":20.93,"t":"Although at my age, some people might expect me to be sitting in a comfortable chair knitting socks. I like more than anything to get out and train."},{"s":21.53,"e":23.55,"t":"I'm in the middle of quite a vigorous training schedule."},{"s":23.99,"e":28.41,"t":"and I would love to compete for Britain, maybe in the triathlon or something with a bit of variety."},{"s":28.92,"e":34.33,"t":"It seems a bit crazy having all these ambitions at 70, but I've never really been your typical stay-at-home grandmother."},{"s":35.19,"e":39.87,"t":"I'd rather go for a jog round the village than stay in the kitchen baking cakes. Maybe I'm mad."},{"s":40.31,"e":45.76,"t":"What I'd love to do is get a group of all us old age pensioners together and start training them. A sort of keep fit for the aged."},{"k":"h","s":49.11,"e":49.11,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":52.22,"e":59.74,"t":"I firmly believe that the body is a temple, so I actually regulate very carefully what goes into mine and what I do with it."},{"s":60.25,"e":77.73,"t":"Well, I swim two miles a day before work, and after I get home from the office, I work out in the gym for about two or three hours. At weekends, when I have more time, I like nothing more than to go for a long run. It really helps me to think and get all the week's events and problems into perspective."},{"s":78.3,"e":82.11,"t":"I guess exercise can be a bit like a drug. It does give me a high."},{"s":82.55,"e":87.39,"t":"My friends sometimes complain that I don't have enough time for them because I'd rather be down at the gym."},{"s":87.93,"e":92.22,"t":"But if I want to stay looking this good, I think it's a small price to pay."},{"k":"h","s":95.64,"e":95.64,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":99.0,"e":100.7,"t":"I'm out every weekend with the boys."},{"s":101.53,"e":105.53,"t":"kick a ball around and we also organise games with some of the other local clubs."},{"s":106.1,"e":108.41,"t":"I suppose we've got a mini league going, really."},{"s":109.11,"e":114.69,"t":"It's fun, 'cause we're all mates. We've known each other for years, and so it means we get to see each other regularly."},{"s":115.42,"e":119.87,"t":"If we're playing a match then all the wives and kids come along and cheer us on."},{"s":120.44,"e":125.73,"t":"None of us are really fit, I mean, look at me, I'm hardly what you call in great shape."},{"s":126.2,"e":127.65,"t":"We just do it for a bit of"},{"s":128.38,"e":133.82,"t":"I don't think we'd enjoy it so much if you got serious and competitive. It's just fun getting out and running around a pitch."},{"s":134.26,"e":135.07,"t":"keeps us feeling young"},{"s":135.77,"e":136.25,"t":"Pose"},{"k":"h","s":139.7,"e":139.7,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":142.81,"e":148.96,"t":"Everyday we're sent outside, even when it's freezing cold, to play hockey or football or whatever."},{"s":149.85,"e":154.37,"t":"Two hours we're made to stand there in our shorts or run up and down. I hate it."},{"s":155.26,"e":159.01,"t":"Try getting doctor's notes to say I can't play, but it makes no difference."},{"s":159.67,"e":164.03,"t":"Teachers say that doing sport is character building, but I say it's character destroying."},{"s":164.63,"e":170.65,"t":"I'd so much rather be sitting somewhere warm, reading or watching TV or, you know, exercising the mind."},{"s":171.29,"e":177.02,"t":"When I get into the sixth form, sports won't be compulsory anymore, and on that day I'm going to celebrate."},{"s":177.66,"e":183.23,"t":"Yeah, okay, so some people actually enjoy sport. But surely if you don't like it, you shouldn't have to do it."},{"k":"h","s":186.65,"e":186.65,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":190.17,"e":194.81,"t":"The doctor says I should try to get regular exercise. You know, a bit every day."},{"s":195.61,"e":199.52,"t":"That's why I got the dog, so I could take it for long walks."},{"s":200.12,"e":201.82,"t":"It gets me out of the house really."},{"s":202.68,"e":207.52,"t":"My condition's not serious. Other specialists say I could live for another 50 years."},{"s":208.12,"e":217.02,"t":"I didn't really have an active life before the attack, but it really scared me. And now I'm out and about walking, and sometimes I even do a bit of swimming."},{"s":217.82,"e":219.84,"t":"I don't watch TV so much anymore."},{"s":220.73,"e":223.71,"t":"I suppose I'm worried I'll slip back into bad habits."}]},{"n":28,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about the business that each runs. Which business is each person describing?","qu":"Besh kishi o'z biznesi haqida gapiradi. Har biri qaysi biznesni tasvirlayapti?","topic":"different people talking about the business that each runs","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"a second-hand bookshop","u":"ishlatilgan kitoblar do'koni"},{"l":"B","t":"a driving school","u":"haydovchilik maktabi"},{"l":"C","t":"an antique shop","u":"antikvar do'kon"},{"l":"D","t":"a fitness centre","u":"fitnes markazi"},{"l":"E","t":"a travel agency","u":"sayyohlik agentligi"},{"l":"F","t":"a computer shop","u":"kompyuter do'koni"}],"dur":404.4,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":11.38,"en":47.81,"ev":"I've always loved collecting old things… What makes it really special is when someone brings in something incredibly rare. Some antique they've had tucked away at home somewhere for years.","uz":"Doim eski narsalarni yig'ishni yaxshi ko'rganman… Eng qizig'i — kimdir juda noyob narsa olib kelganda: uyida yillar davomida yashirib qo'ygan biror antiqa buyum.","why":"Antikvar do'kon (C). Kompaniyada kompyuterda ishlagan — F tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":51.29,"en":84.13,"ev":"Of course, the internet's a great help. I don't have to go digging through brochures and calling airlines every two minutes like in the old days.","uz":"Albatta, internet katta yordam. Avvalgidek broshyuralarni titkilab, har ikki daqiqada aviakompaniyalarga qo'ng'iroq qilishim shart emas.","why":"Aviakompaniyalar, sayohat bron qilish — sayyohlik agentligi (E).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":87.61,"en":115.97,"ev":"I have to make sure the machines are in good order… But my main job is to design training programmes for the customers.","uz":"Trenajyorlar soz bo'lishini ta'minlashim kerak… Lekin asosiy ishim — mijozlar uchun mashg'ulot dasturlarini tuzish.","why":"Fitnes markazi (D). \"Look after their car\" — o'xshatish, haydovchilik maktabi emas (B tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":119.67,"en":156.99,"ev":"I started out with just a small collection, mostly old stuff I'd had for years: fiction, poetry, biographies… Then people started coming in to trade what they'd already read.","uz":"Kichik to'plam bilan boshladim, asosan yillar davomida yig'ilgan eski kitoblar: badiiy, she'riyat, tarjimai hollar… Keyin odamlar o'qib bo'lgan kitoblarini almashtirgani kela boshladi.","why":"Ishlatilgan kitoblar do'koni (A).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":160.41,"en":198.11,"ev":"My dad started up the business… it was just business machines… I got interested in computers and all that… It grew from there.","uz":"Biznesni otam boshlagan… u paytda faqat ofis mashinalari edi… Men kompyuterlarga qiziqib qoldim… shundan o'sib chiqdi.","why":"Kompyuter do'koni (F).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.1,"e":6.43,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about the business that each runs."},{"k":"h","s":11.38,"e":11.38,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":14.49,"e":16.06,"t":"It was risky at first, you know."},{"s":16.82,"e":26.11,"t":"I had been working for a big firm on computers, but I wanted to do something on my own, and I've always loved collecting old things, so I thought, why not try it?"},{"s":27.03,"e":32.73,"t":"I had to learn to drive because you have to travel a lot, to sales and auctions. I never had a car before."},{"s":33.66,"e":40.96,"t":"What makes it really special is when someone brings in something incredibly rare. Some antique they've had tucked away at home somewhere for years."},{"s":41.75,"e":47.81,"t":"I love the look on their faces when you say, \"Yes, well, that old vase you have there is worth half a million pounds.\""},{"k":"h","s":51.29,"e":51.29,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":54.36,"e":57.05,"t":"you might think it's exciting and glamorous and all that."},{"s":57.56,"e":60.06,"t":"But in fact, I hardly ever get out of the place."},{"s":60.54,"e":69.12,"t":"I work pretty much alone, so there I sit in front of a computer, with customers in and out all the time and the phones ringing, and it does get tiring."},{"s":69.91,"e":77.02,"t":"Of course, the internet's a great help. I don't have to go digging through brochures and calling airlines every two minutes like in the old days."},{"s":77.62,"e":84.13,"t":"It's really so easy nowadays. I mean anyone can read all about where they want to go and book online if they want to."},{"k":"h","s":87.61,"e":87.61,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":91.06,"e":92.7,"t":"It's a big responsibility, yeah."},{"s":93.37,"e":96.93,"t":"You have to make sure people get what they want out of their training or they might just give up."},{"s":98.1,"e":102.17,"t":"I tell them that they should look after themselves as carefully as they look after their car."},{"s":103.1,"e":107.81,"t":"Of course, I have to make sure the machines are in good order. You can have an accident if they aren't."},{"s":108.28,"e":111.74,"t":"But my main job is to design training programs for the customers."},{"s":112.54,"e":115.97,"t":"I really like helping them get into shape, you know, looking and feeling better."},{"k":"h","s":119.67,"e":119.67,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":123.45,"e":126.24,"t":"Well, I never dreamt it would get so big."},{"s":126.74,"e":131.61,"t":"I started out with just a small collection, mostly old stuff I'd had for years."},{"s":132.41,"e":140.13,"t":"fiction, poetry, biographies, cookery, travel, quite a lot of travel because I went abroad a lot when I was younger."},{"s":140.82,"e":146.33,"t":"Then people started coming in to trade what they'd already read. And the business really took off."},{"s":147.03,"e":149.73,"t":"Nowadays I sell a lot over the internet too."},{"s":150.39,"e":156.99,"t":"They say television is killing reading, but I don't think that's true, not from the amount of orders we get."},{"k":"h","s":160.41,"e":160.41,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":164.31,"e":165.98,"t":"My dad started up the business.\""},{"s":166.97,"e":171.29,"t":"Of course it wasn't the same then, it was just business machines, basic manual stuff."},{"s":172.02,"e":176.7,"t":"But then he decided to retire and all the stuff in the place started to look out of date."},{"s":177.53,"e":179.23,"t":"I got interested in computers and all that."},{"s":179.7,"e":180.96,"t":"They were completely new then."},{"s":181.62,"e":182.46,"t":"grew from there."},{"s":183.99,"e":184.99,"t":"It's a good business."},{"s":185.53,"e":188.89,"t":"But the technology is changing so fast it's impossible to keep up."},{"s":189.56,"e":193.25,"t":"People, kids you know, use these things from a really early age."},{"s":193.94,"e":198.11,"t":"Makes you wonder, when a 12 year old can set up a system faster than you can."}]},{"n":29,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about the place they live in. How does each person feel about their place of residence?","qu":"Besh kishi yashaydigan joyi haqida gapiradi. Har biri yashash joyiga qanday munosabatda?","topic":"different people talking about the place they live in","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"hasn't lived there very long","u":"u yerda uzoq yashamagan"},{"l":"B","t":"knows many people in the area","u":"hududda ko'p odamni taniydi"},{"l":"C","t":"feels sorry about moving there","u":"u yerga ko'chganidan afsuslanadi"},{"l":"D","t":"considering moving somewhere else","u":"boshqa joyga ko'chishni o'ylayapti"},{"l":"E","t":"believes that the place has become dangerous","u":"joy xavfli bo'lib qolgan deb hisoblaydi"},{"l":"F","t":"is moving somewhere else","u":"boshqa joyga ko'chyapti"}],"dur":275.4,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":8.92,"en":55.55,"ev":"People tell me I should cash in on it. Sell up, move out to the country… so I'm not sure if I should stick around now… It's food for thought.","uz":"Odamlar menga bundan foydalanib qolishimni aytishadi: sotib, qishloqqa ko'chib ketishni… endi qolishim kerakmi, bilmayman… Bu o'ylab ko'rishga arziydi.","why":"Ko'chishni o'ylayapti — D. Qo'shnilarni tanimaydi (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":58.74,"en":98.69,"ev":"Over the last few years it's got worse and worse… Mrs Peters at number 36, she was mugged just last Thursday.","uz":"So'nggi yillarda vaziyat tobora yomonlashdi… 36-uydagi Missis Petersni o'tgan payshanba talashdi.","why":"Joy xavfli bo'lib qolgan (E). \"Everybody knew everybody\" — o'tmish (B emas).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":100.28,"en":145.6,"ev":"But we seem to be settling in. Most of the local shopkeepers seem to know our names now.","uz":"Lekin asta-sekin o'rnashyapmiz. Mahalliy do'kondorlarning ko'pchiligi endi ismimizni biladi.","why":"Yaqinda ko'chib kelgan (A). Yo'l xavfi — E emas, faqat ehtiyotkorlik.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":149.02,"en":199.87,"ev":"The idea of moving was hard at first, leaving all these memories behind… It's only a 10-minute drive and I can pop back whenever I like.","uz":"Ko'chish fikri avvaliga qiyin edi — bu xotiralarni tashlab ketish… Faqat 10 daqiqalik yo'l, xohlagan paytimda kelib ketaman.","why":"Ko'chib ketyapti (F). Afsuslanmaydi — \"it's for the best\".","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":203.06,"en":272.99,"ev":"I realise now it wasn't the right thing to do. We jumped in too quick… I guess we should have given it a bit more practical thought before we dived in and moved.","uz":"Endi bu to'g'ri qaror emasligini tushundim. Juda shoshildik… Ko'chishdan oldin amaliy tomonini ko'proq o'ylashimiz kerak edi.","why":"Ko'chib kelganidan afsuslanadi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.81,"e":7.29,"t":"you will hear five different people talking about the place where they live."},{"k":"h","s":8.92,"e":8.92,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":11.77,"e":15.9,"t":"People tell me I should cash in on it. Sell up, move out to the country."},{"s":16.86,"e":20.99,"t":"Prices have gone up so much around here that I could get a lovely place somewhere rural."},{"s":22.07,"e":22.97,"t":"I don't know though"},{"s":23.42,"e":25.53,"t":"It had never really occurred to me before."},{"s":26.42,"e":30.72,"t":"I've lived half my life here and don't really see much reason for a change."},{"s":31.83,"e":37.76,"t":"While you might say the area has gone up market and improved with these new bistros and shops,"},{"s":38.33,"e":40.48,"t":"Well, it's lost something too."},{"s":41.11,"e":42.85,"t":"A lot of the character it used to have."},{"s":43.64,"e":47.39,"t":"I mean, now I don't even know my neighbour's names and they don't know mine."},{"s":48.25,"e":50.65,"t":"so I'm not sure if I should stick around now."},{"s":51.77,"e":52.25,"t":"moving"},{"s":53.3,"e":53.63,"t":"Well"},{"s":54.49,"e":55.55,"t":"It's food for thought."},{"k":"h","s":58.74,"e":58.74,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":61.69,"e":67.58,"t":"There was a time around here that you could leave your front door open morning, noon and night."},{"s":68.28,"e":75.07,"t":"The kids just played in the street unsupervised and only came home when it got dark or their dinner was on the table."},{"s":76.28,"e":81.6,"t":"Everybody knew everybody else and their business so it wasn't all great."},{"s":82.52,"e":89.47,"t":"Ah, but over the last few years it's got worse and worse and I've no idea why. I really don't."},{"s":90.36,"e":95.26,"t":"Mrs Peters at number 36. She was mugged just last Thursday."},{"s":96.28,"e":98.69,"t":"pounds and her mobile phone she lost."},{"k":"h","s":100.28,"e":100.28,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":103.19,"e":105.6,"t":"When we saw it, we just fell in love with it."},{"s":106.17,"e":114.27,"t":"The old wooden floors, the heavy oak doors, the delightful bay windows and the garden. The garden's going to be glorious in spring."},{"s":114.81,"e":117.47,"t":"We'll have picnics, maybe even barbecues."},{"s":118.2,"e":122.21,"t":"Of course there's lots of work to be done before it's perfect, if it ever will be."},{"s":122.84,"e":124.19,"t":"but we seem to be settling in."},{"s":124.86,"e":130.17,"t":"Most of the local shopkeepers seem to know our names now and most people say hello in the street."},{"s":130.65,"e":132.86,"t":"It's such a change from living in the city."},{"s":133.5,"e":137.92,"t":"And when the kids go back to school, there's a really good one at the other end of the village."},{"s":138.52,"e":145.6,"t":"Probably have to walk them there though. The high street is very busy with cars and I don't want to risk them crossing a busy road on their own."},{"k":"h","s":149.02,"e":149.02,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":151.8,"e":157.79,"t":"Well, with the kids now, there's just not enough room for all of us. We had to do it really."},{"s":158.36,"e":160.93,"t":"Obviously, I would have liked to have stayed here."},{"s":161.4,"e":164.8,"t":"But it's for the best. It was just impractical, really."},{"s":165.4,"e":169.66,"t":"And now we'll have a lovely place. I've lived here since I left home."},{"s":170.3,"e":173.34,"t":"I never imagined then how much my life would change."},{"s":174.33,"e":175.45,"t":"Look out of the window."},{"s":175.99,"e":176.77,"t":"see that shop."},{"s":177.27,"e":180.77,"t":"That's where I bought my first suit for my first day of work."},{"s":181.34,"e":183.93,"t":"And there's the cafe where I met Karen, my wife."},{"s":185.02,"e":190.27,"t":"The idea of moving was hard at first, leaving all these memories behind."},{"s":191.67,"e":195.65,"t":"It's for the best, and it's not like we're moving to the other side of the world."},{"s":196.15,"e":199.87,"t":"It's only a 10 minute drive and I can pop back whenever I like."},{"k":"h","s":203.06,"e":203.06,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":206.01,"e":215.13,"t":"I realised now it wasn't the right thing to do. We jumped in too quick. We just took one look at the cottage and the village and we fell in love."},{"s":215.83,"e":218.4,"t":"We didn't really think about the practicalities."},{"s":218.84,"e":231.01,"t":"It all seemed so idyllic really. Country houses with beautiful gardens. Cricket on the village green. The village fate, the duck pond. It seemed like we were going back in time."},{"s":231.83,"e":236.54,"t":"But once you're used to all that, spent a year or so here, well..."},{"s":237.18,"e":238.78,"t":"when the realities kick in."},{"s":239.58,"e":241.18,"t":"There's not really much to do."},{"s":241.78,"e":247.04,"t":"If we want to go to the cinema, it's a half hour drive to the multiplex on the ring road."},{"s":247.7,"e":252.86,"t":"If we want to eat in a good restaurant or see an exhibition, we have to go into town."},{"s":253.56,"e":256.64,"t":"which with traffic can take over an hour and a half."},{"s":257.24,"e":262.88,"t":"And while the kids don't mind it now, I dread to think what they'll be like when they're a bit older."},{"s":263.51,"e":266.69,"t":"There's literally nothing for teenagers to do here."},{"s":268.34,"e":272.99,"t":"I guess we should have given it a bit more practical thought before we dived in and moved."}]},{"n":30,"q":"You will hear five people talking about their first employment experiences. What does each person say about it?","qu":"Besh kishi birinchi ish tajribasi haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about their first employment experiences","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"they lied about something","u":"biror narsa haqida yolg'on gapirgan"},{"l":"B","t":"they were injured","u":"jarohat olgan"},{"l":"C","t":"they were made redundant at work","u":"ishdan qisqartirilgan"},{"l":"D","t":"they were issued a warning","u":"ogohlantirish olgan"},{"l":"E","t":"they were doing a number of different things","u":"bir nechta turli ishlarni bajargan"},{"l":"F","t":"it affected their career choice","u":"bu kasb tanlashiga ta'sir qilgan"}],"dur":229.4,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":8.7,"en":45.85,"ev":"One day the boss came over and told me that if I didn't improve, he would have no choice but to sack me.","uz":"Bir kuni boshliq kelib, agar yaxshilanmasam, meni ishdan bo'shatishdan boshqa iloji qolmasligini aytdi.","why":"Ogohlantirish olgan (D). Ishdan bo'shatilmagan — \"everything turned out okay\".","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":49.11,"en":105.02,"ev":"I put it on my CV that I spoke fluent French — rather stretching the truth, to say the least. I could just about order a coffee.","uz":"Rezyumemga frantsuz tilida erkin gapiraman deb yozdim — bu haqiqatni ancha bo'rttirish edi. Zo'rg'a qahva buyurtma qila olardim.","why":"Yolg'on gapirgan (A).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":109.05,"en":143.81,"ev":"By the time the placement ended… I'd made up my mind… I was going to spend my life helping people. And that's why I became a paramedic.","uz":"Amaliyot tugaganda… qaror qilib bo'lgandim… hayotimni odamlarga yordam berishga bag'ishlayman. Shuning uchun tez yordam xodimi bo'ldim.","why":"Kasb tanlashiga ta'sir qilgan (F).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":147.42,"en":188.7,"ev":"I got a twig caught in my eye while we were picking pears and the pain was unbearable. There was no way I could carry on working after that.","uz":"Nok terayotganimizda ko'zimga shox kirib ketdi, og'riq chidab bo'lmas edi. Shundan keyin ishlashni davom ettira olmasdim.","why":"Jarohat olgan (B). Turli mevalar terilgan — E tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":192.38,"en":226.72,"ev":"\"Make a cup of tea, Darren, fill up the photocopier with paper, Darren, clean the shelves, Darren.\" It was non-stop and I'd never know from one day to the next what I'd be spending my day doing.","uz":"\"Darren, choy qil; Darren, kserokopiyaga qog'oz sol; Darren, javonlarni tozala.\" Tinimsiz edi, ertaga nima bilan band bo'lishimni hech qachon bilmasdim.","why":"Turli xil ishlar bajargan (E).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.17,"e":6.4,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about their first job."},{"k":"h","s":8.7,"e":8.7,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":11.77,"e":17.63,"t":"It was only a summer job when I was at university. Just a couple of months work and the pay was awful."},{"s":18.23,"e":21.25,"t":"I suppose I was just young, I didn't take it seriously."},{"s":22.01,"e":24.96,"t":"I think if I'm honest, I thought it was beneath me."},{"s":25.43,"e":29.6,"t":"I was an academic after all. I thought I could do it with my eyes closed."},{"s":30.39,"e":37.09,"t":"Anyway, one day the boss came over and told me that if I didn't improve, he would have no choice but to sag me."},{"s":37.91,"e":42.81,"t":"I think I was so embarrassed that I began to take it seriously and everything turned out okay."},{"s":43.45,"e":45.85,"t":"I spent the money I'd earned on a holiday in Greece."},{"k":"h","s":49.11,"e":49.11,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":52.54,"e":55.29,"t":"I suppose it was a bit of a silly thing to do really."},{"s":56.09,"e":58.85,"t":"Put it on my CV that I spoke fluent French."},{"s":59.29,"e":64.32,"t":"rather stretching the truth to say the least. I could just about order a coffee if I had to."},{"s":65.34,"e":69.6,"t":"Well, I didn't think much about it. Doubt I'd ever have to prove it."},{"s":70.2,"e":75.29,"t":"But one day the boss called me over and said he had an important new client with a French wife."},{"s":75.74,"e":82.14,"t":"who didn't speak a word of English, and would I show her around the city for the day while her husband was in a company meeting?"},{"s":82.78,"e":86.46,"t":"There was nothing I could do about it. I couldn't just tell him the truth."},{"s":86.97,"e":88.29,"t":"So I spent the day with her"},{"s":88.73,"e":94.33,"t":"Luckily she didn't let me get a word in edgeways and I just smiled and nodded at appropriate moments."},{"s":95.06,"e":105.02,"t":"The next day I was sure my boss would ask to see me and that would be it. I'd be history. But he never did. I don't think the wife even noticed I hardly spoke a word."},{"k":"h","s":109.05,"e":109.05,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":112.09,"e":113.92,"t":"It was a work placement really."},{"s":114.42,"e":116.57,"t":"But I'd still consider it my first job."},{"s":117.27,"e":121.69,"t":"I mean, I work the same hours as everybody else, nucked in with everybody else."},{"s":122.33,"e":124.8,"t":"I'd never really thought about the work they did before."},{"s":125.85,"e":127.87,"t":"Time really opened my eyes."},{"s":128.92,"e":137.98,"t":"By the time the placement ended and I had to leave, I'd made up my mind. There was no way I was going into a boring 9-5 office job just for the money."},{"s":138.84,"e":141.09,"t":"I was going to spend my life helping people."},{"s":141.85,"e":143.81,"t":"And that's why I became a paramedic."},{"k":"h","s":147.42,"e":147.42,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":150.65,"e":157.5,"t":"Some friends and I went to France to spend the summer picking fruit, just moving from place to place wherever the work was."},{"s":157.94,"e":175.9,"t":"I suppose we had an over-romantic idea about the whole thing. We had no idea just how back-breaking the work would be. The amount of different things we picked - strawberries, grapes, apples, raspberries, pears - it didn't matter what it was. At the end of the day, you could hardly move."},{"s":176.44,"e":188.7,"t":"Anyway, we had to cut the whole thing short and come back to Scotland. I got a twig caught in my eye while we were picking pairs and the pain was unbearable. There was no way I could carry on working after that."},{"k":"h","s":192.38,"e":192.38,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":195.86,"e":197.82,"t":"Dog's body. That's the word."},{"s":198.39,"e":201.85,"t":"I suppose you have to expect it at that age and in your first job."},{"s":202.46,"e":204.35,"t":"but at the time it really got to me."},{"s":205.3,"e":208.8,"t":"I don't know if I expected to be doing more important things or what."},{"s":209.59,"e":214.01,"t":"come home boiling with rage thinking, that's it, tomorrow I quit."},{"s":214.52,"e":219.68,"t":"cup of tea Darren, fill up the photocopier with paper Darren, clean the shelves Darren"},{"s":220.63,"e":226.72,"t":"It was non-stop and I'd never know from one day to the next what I'd be spending my day doing."}]},{"n":31,"q":"You will hear five women talking about living in blocks of flats. What is the main reason each woman gives for choosing the flat where she lives now?","qu":"Besh ayol ko'p qavatli uylarda yashash haqida gapiradi. Har biri hozirgi kvartirasini nima sababdan tanlagan?","topic":"women talking about living in blocks of flats","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"the size of the rooms","u":"xonalarning kattaligi"},{"l":"B","t":"the proximity of local amenities","u":"yaqin atrofdagi qulayliklar (do'kon, xizmatlar)"},{"l":"C","t":"good transport links","u":"qulay transport aloqasi"},{"l":"D","t":"the friendliness of neighbours","u":"qo'shnilarning samimiyligi"},{"l":"E","t":"a feeling of security","u":"xavfsizlik hissi"},{"l":"F","t":"the level of maintenance","u":"binoga qarov (ta'mirlash) darajasi"}],"dur":219.2,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":12.31,"en":43.65,"ev":"I wanted to be able to pop to the post office and get in a few basic provisions without wasting half my day. All the bigger flats I looked at were a bus ride away from the shops.","uz":"Kunimning yarmini yo'qotmasdan pochtaga borib, oddiy oziq-ovqat olib kelishni xohlardim. Men ko'rgan kattaroq kvartiralarning hammasi do'konlardan avtobusda yuriladigan masofada edi.","why":"Yaqin atrofdagi qulayliklar (B). Kattaroq xonalardan voz kechgan (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":51.22,"en":86.27,"ev":"What attracted me was the fact that there's a man on the door downstairs who checks who's coming in and what's going on. Being on your own at my age, that's a comfort.","uz":"Meni jalb qilgani — pastda eshik oldida kim kirib-chiqayotganini tekshiradigan odam borligi edi. Mening yoshimda yolg'iz yashaganda bu xotirjamlik beradi.","why":"Xavfsizlik hissi (E). Stansiya yaqinligi — sabab emas (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":94.71,"en":125.79,"ev":"As soon as I saw how much space you got for your money, I jumped at the chance. I'd been looking at places with tiny rooms just because they were on good bus routes.","uz":"Pulingizga qancha joy olishingizni ko'rishim bilan imkoniyatni qo'ldan bermadim. Avval yaxshi avtobus yo'nalishida bo'lgani uchun kichkina xonali joylarni ko'rib yurgan edim.","why":"Xonalar kattaligi (A). Transport — rad etilgan (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":134.17,"en":170.14,"ev":"I bought it from a friend who introduced me to the people upstairs. They were very welcoming… I like the idea of being close to such nice people.","uz":"Uni do'stimdan sotib oldim, u meni yuqoridagi qo'shnilar bilan tanishtirdi. Ular juda mehmondo'st edi… bunday yoqimli odamlar yonida yashash menga yoqadi.","why":"Qo'shnilar samimiyligi (D). Do'konlar va qarov — keyin bilgan.","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":178.04,"en":213.92,"ev":"The building itself was falling to pieces… So I moved out to this place instead because there's a caretaker who's paid to keep the place in order.","uz":"Oldingi bino qulab tushay deb turardi… Shuning uchun bu yerga ko'chdim, chunki bu yerda binoni tartibda saqlash uchun haq oladigan qorovul bor.","why":"Binoga qarov darajasi (F). Xavfsizlik — qo'shimcha natija.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.22,"e":7.49,"t":"You will hear five women talking about living in blocks of flats."},{"k":"h","s":12.31,"e":12.31,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":12.31,"e":33.79,"t":"I've been here about five years. At first, I wasn't sure that I'd made the right choice because it was quite a while before I got to know the neighbours. For me, it was a question of position. I worked from home, so it wasn't that I had to travel into work or anything, but I wanted to be able to pop to the post office and get in a few basic provisions without wasting half my day."},{"s":34.3,"e":43.65,"t":"All the bigger flats I looked at were a bus ride away from the shops. I don't have a car and I didn't like the idea of being cut off so I settled for less space."},{"k":"h","s":51.22,"e":51.22,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":51.22,"e":54.81,"t":"I'm so close to the station you can hear the trains from my flat."},{"s":55.32,"e":58.81,"t":"I didn't realise that until I moved in, but I've got used to it now."},{"s":59.35,"e":60.8,"t":"I came here when I retired."},{"s":61.24,"e":64.61,"t":"I used to have a much larger place but no longer needed the space."},{"s":65.18,"e":74.53,"t":"What attracted me was the fact that there's a man on the door downstairs who checks, who's coming in and what's going on. Being on your own at my age, that's a comfort."},{"s":75.19,"e":80.48,"t":"I thought he'd also do little maintenance jobs for me, but that's not part of his job, apparently."},{"s":81.3,"e":86.27,"t":"Fortunately, I made friends with a nice couple downstairs who helped me out when anything needs doing."},{"k":"h","s":94.71,"e":94.71,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":94.71,"e":99.9,"t":"I was looking for somewhere close to my work because I didn't want to waste time travelling back and forth."},{"s":100.47,"e":103.17,"t":"so I wasn't really looking in this area at all."},{"s":103.67,"e":115.61,"t":"Then a colleague who lived in the block told me that this place was free. As soon as I saw how much space you got for your money, I jumped at the chance. I'd been looking at places with tiny rooms just because they were on good bus routes."},{"s":116.06,"e":125.79,"t":"It was only after I'd moved in that I realised how good the local shops are and what a nice part of town it is. You really feel safe walking round here, even late at night."},{"k":"h","s":134.17,"e":134.17,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":134.17,"e":160.54,"t":"When I first saw this flat, I was put off by the fact that it's on a very busy road. It's the main commuter route into the city centre. But actually, I bought it from a friend who introduced me to the people upstairs. They were very welcoming and convinced me that it really wasn't a problem. I like the idea of being close to such nice people, so I decided that although I'd have liked bigger rooms, it was probably a good buy."},{"s":161.02,"e":170.14,"t":"It was only later that I discovered how good the local shops are and that the block itself is well maintained by the security guard who lives on the ground floor."},{"k":"h","s":178.04,"e":178.04,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":178.04,"e":197.21,"t":"My last flat was very convenient, handy for the shops and well connected for public transport, but the building itself was falling to pieces and I got fed up trying to get the owner to do something about it. So I moved out to this place instead because there's a caretaker who's paid to keep the place in order."},{"s":198.01,"e":206.33,"t":"I wasn't looking for much bigger rooms but actually I've had no trouble using the space and the other residents turned out to be really friendly."},{"s":207.06,"e":213.92,"t":"Gives you a nice feeling of security to know that if you have a problem you can always pop next door for help."}]},{"n":32,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about cookery courses. What does each speaker say about the course they took?","qu":"Besh kishi pazandachilik kurslari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about cookery courses","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"It helped me to renew my enthusiasm for cooking.","u":"Ovqat pishirishga ishtiyoqimni qaytardi."},{"l":"B","t":"It taught me how to use the latest kitchen equipment.","u":"Eng yangi oshxona jihozlaridan foydalanishni o'rgatdi."},{"l":"C","t":"It took into account the fact that I wasn't a beginner.","u":"Boshlovchi emasligimni hisobga oldi."},{"l":"D","t":"It required me to do things rather than just watch.","u":"Faqat tomosha qilish emas, o'zim bajarishimni talab qildi."},{"l":"E","t":"It gave me skills I wish I'd acquired earlier in life.","u":"Hayotda ertaroq o'rganishni istagan ko'nikmalarimni berdi."},{"l":"F","t":"It included an unexpected search for ingredients.","u":"Unda masalliqlarni kutilmagan izlash ham bor edi."}],"dur":238.4,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":15.51,"en":58.4,"ev":"I wanted to pick up some new ideas for entertaining but didn't need any basic techniques, so the course at the Brandale Cookery School suited me well. There were some people there who didn't know how to boil an egg, but there was extra tuition for them.","uz":"Mehmon kutish uchun yangi g'oyalar olmoqchi edim, asosiy usullar kerak emasdi, shuning uchun Brandale maktabidagi kurs menga mos keldi. Tuxum qaynatishni bilmaydiganlar uchun qo'shimcha darslar bor edi.","why":"Boshlovchi emasligi hisobga olingan (C).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":62.04,"en":105.25,"ev":"You can imagine the look on our faces though when we were told we were going to visit the open-air fish market down by the port.","uz":"Port yonidagi ochiq baliq bozoriga borishimizni aytishganda yuzimizdagi hayratni tasavvur qilishingiz mumkin.","why":"Kutilmagan masalliq izlash (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":108.76,"en":149.76,"ev":"I came away bursting with ideas for giving a dinner party, something I hadn't felt like doing in a long time.","uz":"Kechki ziyofat berish g'oyalariga to'lib-toshib qaytdim — anchadan beri bunday istak bo'lmagandi.","why":"Pishirishga ishtiyoq qaytgan (A). Ko'proq tomosha qilishgan (D emas).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":153.02,"en":193.73,"ev":"I was there to make up for the fact that sadly as a youngster I was hardly ever allowed into the kitchen.","uz":"Afsuski, bolaligimda oshxonaga deyarli kiritilmaganimning o'rnini to'ldirish uchun bordim.","why":"Yoshligida o'rganishni istagan ko'nikmalar (E).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":196.95,"en":235.68,"ev":"I wouldn't have been happy with taking notes and following demonstrations… I wanted to get my hands dirty.","uz":"Faqat yozib olish va namoyishlarni kuzatish meni qoniqtirmasdi… O'zim qo'l urib ishlashni xohlardim.","why":"Tomosha emas, amaliy ish (D). Mahalliy baliq — kutilmagan izlash emas (F tuzoq).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.02,"e":7.87,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about cookery courses."},{"k":"h","s":15.51,"e":15.51,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":18.46,"e":22.08,"t":"There's such a vast range of cookery schools, it's unbelievable."},{"s":22.68,"e":26.78,"t":"Before booking a course, it's advisable to decide what you want from it."},{"s":27.26,"e":37.34,"t":"For me it was easy. I wanted to pick up some new ideas for entertaining but didn't need any basic techniques so the course at the Brandale Cookery School suited me well."},{"s":38.04,"e":42.85,"t":"There were some people there who didn't know how to boil an egg, but there was extra tuition for them."},{"s":43.64,"e":58.4,"t":"courses run by Sylvie Brandale, who's written cookbooks and appeared on TV. And subjects included stress-free parties and sources from around the world. All great topics and all of the ingredients were provided."},{"k":"h","s":62.04,"e":62.04,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":64.09,"e":71.97,"t":"I was very lucky, really. I was on holiday and I happened to hear that there was a new cookery school at the nearby Four Seasons Hotel."},{"s":72.66,"e":77.15,"t":"They had four-hour classes every Saturday, starting at 7am."},{"s":78.23,"e":90.78,"t":"The day I attended, there was a group of ten enthusiastic participants, all eagerly awaiting instructions, though I gathered from their conversations that, unlike me, they were all fairly experienced cooks."},{"s":91.35,"e":97.92,"t":"You can imagine the look on our faces though when we were told we were going to visit the open-air fish market down by the port."},{"s":98.49,"e":105.25,"t":"We all came back having selected freshly caught seafood and were then taught the art of preparing it. Great stuff."},{"k":"h","s":108.76,"e":108.76,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":110.87,"e":128.03,"t":"I'm a good cook, or so my sister says, so she thought I'd do an advanced course, but I was keen to go through the basics again. And this time I was determined to enjoy it. I registered for Glynn Harvey's cookery classes. Only four people in a class."},{"s":128.6,"e":132.8,"t":"We watched while he prepared the dishes, making it all seem so effortless."},{"s":133.43,"e":149.76,"t":"There wasn't much real cooking, although he did invite us to help slice the potatoes and tomatoes, and we were given some tasty, easy-to-cook recipes to take home. I came away bursting with ideas for giving a dinner party, something I hadn't felt like doing in a long time."},{"k":"h","s":153.02,"e":153.02,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":155.26,"e":161.95,"t":"Of course I attended covered a range of techniques from basic to advanced and it gave you lots of practical tips."},{"s":162.9,"e":170.24,"t":"I was there to make up for the fact that sadly as a youngster I was hardly ever allowed into the kitchen, which meant I'd turned into a"},{"s":170.74,"e":172.54,"t":"and shook it in the pan sort of cook."},{"s":173.37,"e":176.77,"t":"the teacher was very chatty and full of enthusiasm."},{"s":177.3,"e":184.51,"t":"She demonstrated several dishes in the morning while we took notes and then we were given some equipment and it was our turn to have a go."},{"s":185.37,"e":188.61,"t":"I made a splendid vegetable tart which we ate at lunch."},{"s":189.08,"e":193.73,"t":"Now I'm planning to go again and this time I'll concentrate on the more demanding recipes."},{"k":"h","s":196.95,"e":196.95,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":199.61,"e":206.08,"t":"This weekend cookery course I did had an emphasis on local ingredients with hands-on practice with the chefs."},{"s":206.74,"e":212.8,"t":"I wouldn't have been happy with taking notes and following demonstrations, no matter how impressive the food produced."},{"s":213.27,"e":218.4,"t":"I wanted to get my hands dirty, just as I'd done as a little girl in school cookery lessons."},{"s":218.94,"e":226.17,"t":"It was at a seaside resort and you stay in a hotel which is very close to the fishing port and so get to cook the local seafood."},{"s":226.68,"e":235.68,"t":"It's really intensive and you cook two-course lunches as well as four-course dinners. But you get enough free time to make it an enjoyable weekend too."}]},{"n":33,"q":"You will hear five different people talking about concerts they went to. What opinion does each speaker express about the concert?","qu":"Besh kishi borgan konsertlari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different people talking about concerts they went to","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"The performers got a better reception than they deserved.","u":"Ijrochilarni munosib bo'lganidan ham yaxshiroq kutib olishdi."},{"l":"B","t":"These musicians are at their best in live performances.","u":"Bu musiqachilar jonli ijroda eng zo'r."},{"l":"C","t":"The concert improved after a disappointing beginning.","u":"Hafsalani pir qilgan boshlanishdan keyin konsert yaxshilandi."},{"l":"D","t":"I enjoyed the band's choice of material for the concert.","u":"Guruhning konsert uchun tanlagan qo'shiqlari yoqdi."},{"l":"E","t":"I'd like to have seen more bands for the price I paid.","u":"To'lagan pulimga ko'proq guruh ko'rishni istardim."},{"l":"F","t":"I was pleased the concert was raising money for a good cause.","u":"Konsert xayrli ish uchun pul yig'ayotganidan xursand bo'ldim."}],"dur":231.7,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":12.66,"en":54.59,"ev":"What made the evening worthwhile for me was the fact that all profits from ticket sales were going to a charity devoted to childcare.","uz":"Kechani arziydigan qilgan narsa — chiptalardan tushgan barcha foyda bolalarga g'amxo'rlik qiluvchi xayriya tashkilotiga ketishi edi.","why":"Xayriya uchun pul yig'ilgani (F). Ko'p guruh bor edi — E emas.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":58.14,"en":94.69,"ev":"The first part was all new stuff and a bit boring… Anyway, after a while we all started getting into the new material and by the end the audience response was great.","uz":"Birinchi qism faqat yangi qo'shiqlar va biroz zerikarli edi… Lekin birozdan keyin hammamiz yangi qo'shiqlarga berilib ketdik, oxirida tomoshabinlar juda yaxshi kutib oldi.","why":"Yomon boshlanib, keyin yaxshilangan (C).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":98.01,"en":136.99,"ev":"At times it felt a bit like a high school recital, with the audience clapping and cheering all the time when there was nothing much to shout about.","uz":"Ba'zan maktab konsertiga o'xshardi: tomoshabinlar maqtaydigan narsa bo'lmasa ham doim qarsak chalib, olqishlashardi.","why":"Ijrochilar munosib bo'lganidan ko'proq olqish olgan (A). Xayriya konsertlari — boshqa holat (F tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":140.25,"en":179.65,"ev":"I know some people would have wanted her to include her latest songs but I was happy enough that the night was all about the old favourites.","uz":"Ba'zilar uning so'nggi qo'shiqlarini ham kuylashini xohlagan bo'lardi, lekin kecha eski sevimli qo'shiqlarga bag'ishlanganidan mamnun edim.","why":"Qo'shiq tanlovi yoqgan (D).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":183.03,"en":229.5,"ev":"They've done some CDs, but they've never yet made a record that really captures what they do on stage.","uz":"Bir nechta disk chiqarishgan, lekin sahnada qiladiganlarini to'liq aks ettiradigan yozuv hali qilishmagan.","why":"Jonli ijroda eng zo'r (B). Sevimli qo'shiqlar kam — D emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.9,"e":6.78,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about concerts they went to."},{"k":"h","s":12.66,"e":12.66,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.54,"e":20.83,"t":"The concert went on for three hours and it featured a variety of bands."},{"s":21.46,"e":25.92,"t":"I'd have preferred something shorter and of higher quality to be honest."},{"s":26.42,"e":31.61,"t":"The first band to come on, The Beats, didn't seem to have rehearsed their set very well."},{"s":32.12,"e":36.96,"t":"Nice catchy rhythms, but otherwise it was a mess"},{"s":37.53,"e":45.79,"t":"What made the evening worthwhile for me was the fact that all profits from ticket sales were going to a charity devoted to childcare."},{"s":46.58,"e":54.59,"t":"There was a huge audience because you don't often get the chance to see so many bands at one venue, and only for a few dollars."},{"k":"h","s":58.14,"e":58.14,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":62.04,"e":67.87,"t":"This was a concert by Brighton Club, a great rock band just back from a successful tour of Latin America."},{"s":68.41,"e":77.53,"t":"But the first part was all new stuff and a bit boring. And although everyone was shouting out the titles of songs they wanted to hear, the band took no notice, which was a shame."},{"s":78.17,"e":84.73,"t":"I mean, it's a bit bad when you finally get the chance to see your favourite band live and then they refuse to play their best songs."},{"s":85.46,"e":94.69,"t":"Anyway, after a while we all started getting into the new material and by the end the audience response was great. So I don't think anybody minded the $40 they'd paid."},{"k":"h","s":98.01,"e":98.01,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":101.11,"e":106.75,"t":"This was a concert by Celia Sampson and her band who play pop with some touches of jazz and country."},{"s":107.26,"e":111.2,"t":"She's got a beautiful voice, but the rest of the band let her down rather."},{"s":111.7,"e":118.85,"t":"The times it felt a bit like a high school recital, with the audience clapping and cheering all the time when there was nothing much to shout about."},{"s":119.54,"e":128.38,"t":"all fine and good, except I don't particularly enjoy paying $30 for a high school performance where profits go to second-class musicians."},{"s":129.11,"e":136.99,"t":"Mind you, I've paid that kind of money in the past for concerts to help research or to fight world poverty, but that's a different thing entirely."},{"k":"h","s":140.25,"e":140.25,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":143.38,"e":145.92,"t":"This was a concert by the Brenda Amis band."},{"s":146.39,"e":158.11,"t":"I wouldn't have wanted to miss the beginning. A huge cloud of smoke swelled on the stage and out of it emerged Brenda Amos with jet black hair piled up with a feather and a big flower on top."},{"s":158.74,"e":168.22,"t":"I know some people would have wanted her to include her latest songs but I was happy enough that the night was all about the old favourites I've listened to so many times."},{"s":168.7,"e":179.65,"t":"At the end, she had a short exchange with the audience. \"Thanks so much guys, you're so nice!\" And then she sang \"Only for big girls\" and got a standing ovation."},{"k":"h","s":183.03,"e":183.03,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":186.17,"e":191.77,"t":"This was a gig by the Sam Barnes Band. Sam's my favourite guitarist right now."},{"s":192.22,"e":196.25,"t":"His approach to the instrument is the complete opposite to tradition."},{"s":196.76,"e":200.61,"t":"hold the guitar upside down with the neck touching the ground."},{"s":201.21,"e":207.61,"t":"The music's punk and he's got a great band, particularly the bass player and the drummer."},{"s":208.22,"e":215.01,"t":"They've done some CDs, but they've never yet made a record that really captures what they do on stage."},{"s":215.58,"e":223.65,"t":"You're less likely to be impressed by their recordings. But people would just stand at the gig. It blew everybody's mind."},{"s":224.12,"e":229.5,"t":"I only wished they'd played more of my favourite tracks, but you can't have everything."}]},{"n":34,"q":"You will hear five different students talking about their first year at university. What does each student say about the course they took?","qu":"Besh talaba universitetdagi birinchi yili haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different students talking about their first year at university","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I had to face some criticism when I chose a subject to study.","u":"Fan tanlaganimda tanqidga duch keldim."},{"l":"B","t":"I was able to change an earlier decision about my studies.","u":"O'qishim haqidagi avvalgi qarorimni o'zgartira oldim."},{"l":"C","t":"I'm pleased that I'm able to combine studying with a job.","u":"O'qishni ish bilan birga olib bora olayotganimdan xursandman."},{"l":"D","t":"I had to be careful when choosing which college to study at.","u":"Qaysi kollejda o'qishni tanlashda ehtiyot bo'lishim kerak edi."},{"l":"E","t":"I had to give up a good job to concentrate on my studies.","u":"O'qishga e'tibor qaratish uchun yaxshi ishimdan voz kechdim."},{"l":"F","t":"I'm happy to have an active social life while at college.","u":"Kollejda faol ijtimoiy hayotim borligidan xursandman."}],"dur":237.9,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":13.21,"en":49.69,"ev":"History at one university can be very different to history at another. So I had to do some research about the three colleges where I might have wanted to study.","uz":"Bir universitetdagi tarix boshqasidagidan juda farq qilishi mumkin. Shuning uchun o'qishim mumkin bo'lgan uchta kollej haqida izlanish qilishim kerak edi.","why":"Kollej tanlashda ehtiyotkorlik (D). Ziyofatlarga vaqt yo'q (F emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":53.14,"en":99.74,"ev":"I'd always thought I wanted to study medicine… But then I had second thoughts about my choice of subject and went for nursing.","uz":"Doim tibbiyotni o'qimoqchi deb o'ylardim… Keyin fan tanlovimni qayta o'ylab, hamshiralikni tanladim.","why":"Avvalgi qarorni o'zgartirgan (B).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":103.35,"en":144.7,"ev":"Part-time study is mainly for people like me who have other responsibilities. I work mornings in a school and I'm keen to keep it that way.","uz":"Sirtqi o'qish asosan men kabi boshqa majburiyatlari borlar uchun. Ertalablari maktabda ishlayman va shunday davom ettirishni istayman.","why":"O'qish va ishni birga olib boradi (C). Ziyofatlar yo'q (F emas).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":148.18,"en":194.72,"ev":"My parents tried hard, but failed, to make me change my mind. They said I was making the wrong choice and that I wouldn't be able to make a living.","uz":"Ota-onam fikrimni o'zgartirishga qattiq urinishdi, lekin uddalay olishmadi. Noto'g'ri tanlov qilyapsan, bu bilan kun ko'ra olmaysan, deyishdi.","why":"Fan tanlagani uchun tanqidga uchragan (A).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":198.01,"en":236.03,"ev":"What really does it for me is that it's been brilliant in other ways. Pretty much every weekend there's a chance for students to go out.","uz":"Menga eng yoqqani — boshqa jihatdan ham zo'r. Deyarli har dam olish kunida talabalar uchun ko'ngil ochish imkoniyati bor.","why":"Faol ijtimoiy hayot (F). Yarim stavka ish — kelajak rejasi (C emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.15,"e":8.86,"t":"You'll hear five different students talking about their first year at university."},{"k":"h","s":13.21,"e":13.21,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":16.06,"e":19.74,"t":"I decided to study history. I want to be a lecturer one day."},{"s":20.38,"e":25.79,"t":"And when you want to do a degree, say in pharmacy, there's little difference in content between universities I think."},{"s":26.26,"e":33.79,"t":"But history at one university can be very different to history at another. So I had to do some research about the three colleges where I might have wanted to study."},{"s":34.49,"e":38.62,"t":"I'd heard good things about Dundee University and they all prove correct."},{"s":39.19,"e":44.54,"t":"I'm from Ireland and I got to study Irish history plus a focus on the European Union."},{"s":45.02,"e":49.69,"t":"I've been so busy I've had no time to enjoy student parties, but that'll come I'm sure."},{"k":"h","s":53.14,"e":53.14,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.28,"e":65.79,"t":"I'd always thought I wanted to study medicine, but the college I wanted to go to only had 20 places, and I didn't get a place."},{"s":66.71,"e":75.04,"t":"That was disappointing, and I even thought I might take a year out. But then I had second thoughts about my choice of subject."},{"s":75.51,"e":76.64,"t":"and went for nursing."},{"s":77.4,"e":85.31,"t":"I'm now at Sheffield Hallam College, which is linked to a variety of hospitals and isn't too far away from home."},{"s":86.65,"e":88.73,"t":"far enough for me to be independent."},{"s":89.27,"e":99.74,"t":"People who'd gone there told me it was really good and the tutors had time for you. The course is brilliant and there's a friendly campus atmosphere."},{"k":"h","s":103.35,"e":103.35,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":106.33,"e":111.2,"t":"I'm studying for a degree in French at Sussex University. It's a part-time course."},{"s":111.74,"e":115.55,"t":"Very few students would want to study part-time for a first degree of course."},{"s":116.18,"e":120.61,"t":"Part time study is mainly for people like me who have other responsibilities."},{"s":121.08,"e":124.54,"t":"I work mornings in a school and I'm keen to keep it that way."},{"s":125.4,"e":128.99,"t":"I'm learning a lot, though it's been different to what I expected."},{"s":129.43,"e":131.36,"t":"I thought it was going to be easier."},{"s":132.7,"e":143.01,"t":"Unlike me, full-time students live in accommodation on the campus and I hear wonderful stories about the great parties they organise. They say I don't know what I'm missing."},{"s":143.51,"e":144.7,"t":"But I don't mind really."},{"k":"h","s":148.18,"e":148.18,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":151.48,"e":159.68,"t":"Psychology was always my choice of degree subject. I studied it at school and soon realised it was what I wanted to do at university."},{"s":160.25,"e":164.64,"t":"My parents tried hard, but failed, to make me change my mind."},{"s":165.08,"e":169.02,"t":"They said I was making the wrong choice and that I wouldn't be able to make a living."},{"s":169.78,"e":179.23,"t":"I love it! I'm interested in social psychology, how people interact. It's fascinating and I know I'll be able to find work easily."},{"s":179.9,"e":185.28,"t":"I'm at Coventry University living in student accommodation which is very convenient."},{"s":185.94,"e":190.27,"t":"The Coventry is really student oriented and the teachers are very friendly."},{"s":190.74,"e":194.72,"t":"and my brother lives only 20 minutes away, so I see him often."},{"k":"h","s":198.01,"e":198.01,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":201.08,"e":205.15,"t":"I'm studying Geography at Swansea University because I love this area."},{"s":205.98,"e":207.84,"t":"I came the first day thinking"},{"s":208.31,"e":210.97,"t":"What if I find out the course isn't what I wanted?"},{"s":211.58,"e":212.54,"t":"But it's amazing."},{"s":213.02,"e":218.85,"t":"The department is really good and what really does it for me is that it's been brilliant in other ways."},{"s":219.32,"e":222.91,"t":"Pretty much every weekend there's a chance for students to go out."},{"s":223.51,"e":227.87,"t":"There's a group of us who knew each other from school and we're all starting together."},{"s":228.73,"e":229.92,"t":"I'm still living at home.\""},{"s":230.39,"e":236.03,"t":"but I hope to be able to do some part-time work and rent a small flat with a couple of friends next year."}]},{"n":35,"q":"You will hear five different craft workers giving advice to people who want to start a home-based business to sell the things they make. What advice does each speaker give?","qu":"Besh hunarmand uyda biznes boshlamoqchi bo'lganlarga maslahat beradi.","topic":"different craft workers giving advice to people who want to start a home-based b","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"expand your business by advertising locally","u":"mahalliy reklama orqali biznesni kengaytiring"},{"l":"B","t":"continue to learn in order to perfect your product","u":"mahsulotni mukammal qilish uchun o'rganishda davom eting"},{"l":"C","t":"employ family and friends to market your product","u":"mahsulotni sotishga oila va do'stlarni jalb qiling"},{"l":"D","t":"spend time organising your workspace properly","u":"ish joyingizni to'g'ri tashkil qilishga vaqt ajrating"},{"l":"E","t":"increase business by selling online","u":"onlayn sotish orqali biznesni oshiring"},{"l":"F","t":"produce a clear marketing plan for your business","u":"biznesingiz uchun aniq marketing reja tuzing"}],"dur":227.6,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":16.15,"en":56.16,"ev":"My style has changed over time because I've kept doing research into the latest techniques. There's nothing worse than thinking you know it all.","uz":"Uslubim vaqt o'tishi bilan o'zgardi, chunki eng yangi usullarni o'rganishda davom etdim. Hammasini bilaman deb o'ylashdan yomoni yo'q.","why":"Mahsulotni mukammal qilish uchun o'rganish (B). Reklama yetarli emas — A tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":59.61,"en":102.17,"ev":"I wished I'd given more thought to setting up an area where I'd do the work. I lost time and money because I ended up getting in such a mess.","uz":"Ishlaydigan joyni tashkil qilish haqida ko'proq o'ylaganimda edi. Hammayoq tartibsiz bo'lib, vaqt va pul yo'qotdim.","why":"Ish joyini to'g'ri tashkil qilish (D). Onlayn sotadi, lekin bu maslahat emas (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":105.62,"en":140.67,"ev":"It's essential to have a rough bookkeeping system in place and to have worked out the profits you expect and deducted your expenditure and possible losses.","uz":"Taxminiy hisob-kitob tizimi bo'lishi va kutilayotgan foydani, xarajat va ehtimoliy zararni hisoblab chiqish shart.","why":"Aniq marketing (biznes) reja (F). Xodim yollash — kelajak rejasi (C emas).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":143.96,"en":185.02,"ev":"It may well pay to invest in a colourful brochure and posters, which can be left in shops in the area.","uz":"Hududdagi do'konlarga qo'yish uchun rangli broshyura va plakatlarga pul sarflash o'zini oqlashi mumkin.","why":"Mahalliy reklama (A). Sayt — erta qilingan xato (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":188.47,"en":225.79,"ev":"I owe part of my success to my brother who designed an amazing website for me which attracted lots of buyers.","uz":"Muvaffaqiyatimning bir qismi akamga bog'liq — u menga ko'plab xaridorlarni jalb qilgan ajoyib sayt yaratdi.","why":"Onlayn sotish (E). Aka saytni yasagan, lekin maslahat — onlayn sotish (C tuzoq).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.58,"e":10.17,"t":"You will hear five different craft workers giving advice to people who want to start a home-based business to sell the things they make."},{"k":"h","s":16.15,"e":16.15,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":18.42,"e":27.9,"t":"Most people who are interested in starting craft businesses enjoy making or doing something, whether it's making dolls, candles or even cooking."},{"s":28.34,"e":30.3,"t":"but it's not as easy as it might seem.\""},{"s":30.84,"e":38.49,"t":"Some think a good website and a few ads in the papers are all they need for their business to take off and provide a regular income."},{"s":39.1,"e":40.64,"t":"but there's much more to it than that"},{"s":41.08,"e":49.18,"t":"I make silver jewellery and you'll find my style has changed over time because I've kept doing research into the latest techniques."},{"s":49.72,"e":56.16,"t":"There's nothing worse than thinking you know it all. However much you advertise, your business will slow down."},{"k":"h","s":59.61,"e":59.61,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":61.69,"e":66.4,"t":"There are such a demand for handmade goods because people are looking for the personal touch."},{"s":66.97,"e":75.71,"t":"One day I had the idea of covering some jars and bottles with cloth, then putting a thin coat of plaster on and painting designs on the surface."},{"s":76.54,"e":79.55,"t":"I sold them so quickly that I decided to start a business."},{"s":80.15,"e":89.12,"t":"There were bottles all over my house in different stages of development and I wished I'd given more thought to setting up an area where I'd do the work."},{"s":89.94,"e":96.16,"t":"I lost time and money because I ended up getting in such a mess. So beginners, take notice."},{"s":96.98,"e":102.17,"t":"I also sell online now, but most of my sales are from word of mouth recommendations."},{"k":"h","s":105.62,"e":105.62,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":107.7,"e":113.25,"t":"Doing something you like to do and getting paid for it is great and it doesn't have to be scary."},{"s":113.85,"e":124.32,"t":"By the time you actually start selling things though, it's essential to have a rough bookkeeping system in place and to have worked out the profits you expect and deducted your expenditure and possible losses."},{"s":124.92,"e":133.28,"t":"I started my own craft business two years ago, making baskets, filling them with things like fruit and nuts, and decorating them with silk flowers."},{"s":133.75,"e":140.67,"t":"I wrapped them as gifts and sold them to friends at first, but now I have lots of orders. I'm even thinking of employing a couple of people."},{"k":"h","s":143.96,"e":143.96,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":146.04,"e":153.02,"t":"When you're ready to launch your business, it pays to think carefully about how your prospective customers will hear about you."},{"s":153.85,"e":164.38,"t":"this little point in taking out ads in the national papers at this stage, but it may well pay to invest in a colourful brochure and posters, which can be left in shops in the area."},{"s":165.43,"e":169.79,"t":"That's how I started my business, which is designing and making greeting cards."},{"s":170.3,"e":179.2,"t":"Mind you, friends and acquaintances gave me contradictory advice and I ended up paying someone to design a website for me when I wasn't ready for it."},{"s":179.86,"e":185.02,"t":"Anyway, my business is thriving and now takes up five rooms in my house."},{"k":"h","s":188.47,"e":188.47,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":190.65,"e":194.75,"t":"I started making lamb shades and it just went from hobby to career."},{"s":195.48,"e":200.45,"t":"My home no longer offers enough space, so I may rent some extra rooms from a friend."},{"s":201.18,"e":205.41,"t":"It was good to start small though. I wouldn't have been able to cope with lots of work then."},{"s":206.1,"e":207.97,"t":"I really knew nothing about marketing."},{"s":208.41,"e":212.54,"t":"And if you're like me, don't worry, if your product sell, it'll sort itself out."},{"s":213.34,"e":219.87,"t":"I owe part of my success to my brother who designed an amazing website for me which attracted lots of buyers."},{"s":220.76,"e":225.79,"t":"It does mean you need to organise a way to post things securely, but it's all worthwhile doing."}]},{"n":36,"q":"You will hear five different writers talking about their first novels. What does each writer say?","qu":"Besh yozuvchi birinchi romanlari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"different writers talking about their first novels","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I learnt some of the skills of novel writing in a previous job.","u":"Roman yozish ko'nikmalarining bir qismini oldingi ishimda o'rgandim."},{"l":"B","t":"My earlier style of writing was not suitable for a novel.","u":"Avvalgi yozish uslubim romanga mos emas edi."},{"l":"C","t":"I was determined to write a novel that was true to life.","u":"Hayotga yaqin roman yozishga qat'iy qaror qilgandim."},{"l":"D","t":"I believe I should've been paid more to write this novel.","u":"Bu romanni yozganim uchun ko'proq haq olishim kerak edi."},{"l":"E","t":"This novel benefited from a course of study I attended.","u":"Bu romanga men qatnashgan kurs foyda berdi."},{"l":"F","t":"Being asked to write a novel came as a complete surprise to me.","u":"Roman yozishni so'rashgani men uchun mutlaqo kutilmagan bo'ldi."}],"dur":226.5,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":13.14,"en":51.2,"ev":"I don't think I could have written it if I hadn't decided to take a degree in creative writing a few years ago though.","uz":"Bir necha yil oldin ijodiy yozish bo'yicha o'qishga qaror qilmaganimda, buni yoza olmasdim.","why":"O'qigan kursi foyda bergan (E). Restoran — oilasining ishi (A emas).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":54.52,"en":90.62,"ev":"When I started writing a novel, I realised the way I'd written so far wasn't so good really, not for real fiction.","uz":"Roman yozishni boshlaganimda, shu paytgacha yozgan uslubim haqiqiy badiiy adabiyot uchun unchalik yaxshi emasligini angladim.","why":"Avvalgi uslubi romanga mos emas (B). Hayotga yaqin emas, aksincha to'qima qahramonlar (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":94.23,"en":137.73,"ev":"Within a week of starting it, I'd been offered a book deal by a publisher… I thought there must have been some mistake.","uz":"Blogni boshlaganimdan bir hafta o'tmay nashriyot kitob shartnomasini taklif qildi… Biror xato bo'lsa kerak deb o'yladim.","why":"Kutilmagan taklif (F). Ko'p pul — \"ko'proq olishim kerak edi\" emas (D tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":141.43,"en":179.84,"ev":"The inspiration for my novel came from… my disappointment at how unrealistic and far-fetched they were… Tell it like it was.","uz":"Romanim ilhomi… ularning qanchalik g'ayritabiiy va to'qima ekanidan hafsalam pir bo'lganidan kelgan… Qanday bo'lsa, shunday aytish.","why":"Hayotga yaqin roman yozishga qat'iyat (C).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":183.42,"en":224.0,"ev":"Journalism wasn't a bad place to acquire useful skills. It taught me to be clear and edit myself, not to write too much.","uz":"Jurnalistika foydali ko'nikmalar orttirish uchun yomon joy emasdi. U menga aniq yozishni, o'zimni tahrir qilishni va ortiqcha yozmaslikni o'rgatdi.","why":"Oldingi ishida o'rgangan (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":3.96,"e":7.84,"t":"You'll hear five different writers talking about their first novels."},{"k":"h","s":13.14,"e":13.14,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.67,"e":18.85,"t":"I'd never done any writing before, though I was a keen reader."},{"s":19.45,"e":22.85,"t":"This novel was inspired by my own childhood experiences."},{"s":23.42,"e":28.38,"t":"I got to meet a lot of people as a child because my parents owned a large successful restaurant."},{"s":29.08,"e":34.62,"t":"I don't think I could have written it if I hadn't decided to take a degree in creative writing a few years ago though."},{"s":35.32,"e":39.52,"t":"It was a way of being serious about writing and it gave me a lot of confidence."},{"s":40.28,"e":45.92,"t":"I began work on the novel halfway through the second year and completed it after graduating."},{"s":46.36,"e":48.54,"t":"It was very, very hard work."},{"s":49.43,"e":51.2,"t":"all really being worthwhile."},{"k":"h","s":54.52,"e":54.52,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":56.95,"e":64.64,"t":"I'm only 22 years old and I've been writing since I was 13, mainly short stories which were published in team magazines."},{"s":65.18,"e":78.11,"t":"When I started writing a novel, I realised the way I'd written so far wasn't so good really, not for real fiction, so I knew I had to look at my favourite writers. You learn a lot by seeing how they do what they do."},{"s":78.78,"e":81.28,"t":"I knew very well what I wanted to write about though."},{"s":82.2,"e":85.21,"t":"I'm bored with books where everyone is a bit like someone you know."},{"s":85.66,"e":90.62,"t":"I wanted to write about people who only exist in fiction. That's what readers find attractive."},{"k":"h","s":94.23,"e":94.23,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":96.5,"e":99.61,"t":"My novel began life as a blog on my website."},{"s":100.28,"e":104.48,"t":"Within a week of starting it, I'd been offered a book deal by a publisher."},{"s":105.11,"e":115.68,"t":"I remember sitting and looking at this offer on my computer screen. The sum was several times bigger than my annual librarian salary and I thought there must have been some mistake."},{"s":117.18,"e":124.48,"t":"And the novel is a fictional version of my blog and it centres on a university librarian, his partner and their sons."},{"s":125.5,"e":127.52,"t":"writing it wasn't particularly hard because"},{"s":127.96,"e":131.42,"t":"Basically, I was being asked to keep to the same style."},{"s":132.15,"e":134.11,"t":"and I'm now adapting it for the screen."},{"s":135.06,"e":137.73,"t":"I'd always wanted a job that I could really enjoy."},{"k":"h","s":141.43,"e":141.43,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":143.54,"e":155.29,"t":"I used to watch a lot of TV, and I admit that the inspiration for my novel came from the dramas I watched, or rather from my disappointment at how unrealistic and far-fetched they were."},{"s":155.99,"e":160.83,"t":"It was very rarely that any of them attempted to get under the skin of the characters."},{"s":161.34,"e":164.61,"t":"So that's what I aim to do. Tell it like it was."},{"s":165.37,"e":179.84,"t":"It wasn't easy, and when people say how wonderful it must be to be recognised in the street and to be asked to sign autographs, I tell them about the long hours in front of the computer and about forgetting what it means to have a free weekend."},{"k":"h","s":183.42,"e":183.42,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":185.98,"e":191.58,"t":"I used to be a journalist on a national paper and I began work on my novel in 2001."},{"s":192.02,"e":196.48,"t":"It's a historical novel, and I spent months researching the history of the period."},{"s":197.18,"e":199.39,"t":"It's set in India in the 1920s."},{"s":200.22,"e":202.53,"t":"I then spent two years writing it."},{"s":203.42,"e":211.39,"t":"Journalism wasn't a bad place to acquire useful skills. It taught me to be clear and edit myself not to write too much."},{"s":212.34,"e":224.0,"t":"My parents couldn't believe it when they heard my name on the news. I hadn't told them anything because they never thought very highly of anything I'd written previously, and I didn't want to start having any doubts myself."}]},{"n":38,"q":"You hear five people talking about cycling. What did each person feel?","qu":"Besh kishi velosport haqida gapiradi. Har biri nimani his qilgan?","topic":"people talking about cycling","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I was glad I took adequate precautions.","u":"Yetarli ehtiyot choralarini ko'rganimdan xursand bo'ldim."},{"l":"B","t":"I feel let down because I did not get the support I should have got.","u":"Kerakli yordamni olmaganim uchun o'zimni aldangandek his qilaman."},{"l":"C","t":"I have a lot to learn about this event.","u":"Bu musobaqa haqida hali ko'p narsa o'rganishim kerak."},{"l":"D","t":"I was disappointed, though I had done everything I could.","u":"Qo'limdan kelganini qilgan bo'lsam ham, hafsalam pir bo'ldi."},{"l":"E","t":"My equipment breaking down robbed me of the success I had worked for.","u":"Jihozim buzilib, mehnat qilgan muvaffaqiyatimdan mahrum bo'ldim."},{"l":"F","t":"I lost because I was given poor advice.","u":"Yomon maslahat berishgani uchun yutqazdim."},{"l":"G","t":"I underestimated how demanding the event could be.","u":"Musobaqa qanchalik og'ir bo'lishini yetarlicha baholamadim."},{"l":"H","t":"My fellow competitors behaved very badly.","u":"Raqiblarim o'zini juda yomon tutdi."}],"dur":454.6,"items":[{"a":"D","ps":12.34,"en":53.15,"ev":"There must have been an accident earlier for me to meet a traffic jam on such a small country road… I know it was not my fault, but still it really is annoying.","uz":"Bunday kichik qishloq yo'lida tirbandlikka duch kelganimga qaraganda, oldinroq avariya bo'lgan bo'lsa kerak… Bilaman, aybim yo'q, lekin baribir juda alam qiladi.","why":"Qo'lidan kelganini qilgan, lekin omadsizlik — D. Velosiped yaxshi ishlagan (E emas).","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":55.51,"en":92.38,"ev":"I thought I was well prepared, but I was only halfway through it when my legs began to seize up. I soon realised that I hadn't done enough mountain training.","uz":"Yaxshi tayyorlanganman deb o'ylagandim, lekin yarim yo'lda oyoqlarim qotib qola boshladi. Tog'da yetarli mashq qilmaganimni tushundim.","why":"Poyga qanchalik og'irligini kam baholagan (G).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":93.78,"en":132.19,"ev":"I was wearing all the protective clothing so I wasn't hurt.","uz":"Barcha himoya kiyimlarini kiygan edim, shuning uchun jarohat olmadim.","why":"Yetarli ehtiyot choralari (A).","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":133.78,"en":178.27,"ev":"If the support team would have been doing their job properly, this should not have been a bad issue. It took too long to get to me.","uz":"Yordam guruhi ishini to'g'ri qilganida, bu katta muammo bo'lmasdi. Ular menga juda kech yetib kelishdi.","why":"Kerakli yordam bo'lmagan (B). G'ildirak muammosi — lekin aybdor yordam guruhi (E tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":180.31,"en":228.73,"ev":"That's when I heard a crunching sound. And then the gears just jammed… I never expected the bike to let me down.","uz":"Aynan o'shanda qarsillagan ovoz eshitdim. Keyin uzatmalar tiqilib qoldi… Velosiped meni pand berishini kutmagandim.","why":"Jihoz buzilib, muvaffaqiyatdan mahrum bo'lgan (E). Murabbiy maslahati yaxshi edi (F emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.87,"e":6.94,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about a particular subject."},{"k":"h","s":12.34,"e":12.34,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":15.06,"e":17.63,"t":"I had a good lead coming up to the last hill climb."},{"s":18.07,"e":25.12,"t":"I thought I had the race in the bag. I was feeling great. The bike was performing well after all the repairs it had this season."},{"s":25.88,"e":30.78,"t":"There must have been an accident earlier for me to meet a traffic jam on such a small country road."},{"s":31.38,"e":38.43,"t":"Normally I would have just sped past the slow moving traffic if the road had only been a little bit wider."},{"s":39.32,"e":41.15,"t":"teammates still congratulated me."},{"s":41.75,"e":44.06,"t":"to that point I'd had a good race."},{"s":44.82,"e":53.15,"t":"I know it was not my fault, but still it really is annoying. I'm so competitive. That sort of thing can be really hard to take."},{"k":"h","s":55.51,"e":55.51,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":57.88,"e":60.64,"t":"I had been planning to take part in this race all year."},{"s":61.18,"e":66.59,"t":"I thought I was well prepared, but I was only halfway through it when my legs began to seize up."},{"s":67.06,"e":77.25,"t":"I soon realized that I hadn't done enough mountain training. In my normal environment, I would have been fine. But it was the steep climbs in this race that I wasn't used to."},{"s":77.72,"e":84.96,"t":"My muscles just began to tighten up and I realized that if I pushed myself any harder, I'd probably tear a muscle."},{"s":85.46,"e":92.38,"t":"Yes, it can be disappointing, but you have to learn from these experiences and it will make me a better cyclist in the long run."},{"k":"h","s":93.78,"e":93.78,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":95.8,"e":98.97,"t":"This is the first time I've been off-road mountain biking."},{"s":100.12,"e":114.05,"t":"The track was quite difficult and I fell off a couple of times. I was wearing all the protective clothing so I wasn't hurt. The most painful thing was cycling down the bumpy tracks. I tried riding standing up but that gave me a backache."},{"s":114.55,"e":118.4,"t":"When I fell the second time, it was while cycling along a thin track"},{"s":119.1,"e":124.25,"t":"The bike just slipped from under me and I tumbled down a bank into a large puddle of mud."},{"s":124.92,"e":132.19,"t":"I got a bit dirty but nothing was broken and I managed to make it to the end of the course very tired and in desperate need of a bath."},{"k":"h","s":133.78,"e":133.78,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":136.18,"e":141.25,"t":"I am a keen competitor and I like to enter as many cycle races as I can in any one year."},{"s":141.78,"e":146.08,"t":"I was really looking forward to last week's race because a large part of it is in the hills."},{"s":146.62,"e":150.88,"t":"One of my main strengths is uphill cycling, so I really fancied my chances."},{"s":151.67,"e":158.11,"t":"Everything was going fine, I was in a good position and I just started to climb when I had a problem with my front wheel."},{"s":158.68,"e":163.13,"t":"If the support team would have been doing their job properly, this should not have been a bad issue."},{"s":163.86,"e":168.45,"t":"It took too long to get to me, and then they fiddled about for far too long adjusting my front wheel."},{"s":169.05,"e":171.84,"t":"When I did finally get going again, it was all too late."},{"s":172.38,"e":174.33,"t":"I ended up being one of the last to finish."},{"s":175.0,"e":176.29,"t":"This was disappointing for me."},{"s":176.86,"e":178.27,"t":"I thought it was going to be my"},{"k":"h","s":180.31,"e":180.31,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":182.58,"e":187.93,"t":"I'd spent a lot of time training this year, not just on the bike but a lot of hours in the gym."},{"s":188.63,"e":193.47,"t":"After I strained a muscle in training, my trainer told me to take it a little easier."},{"s":194.04,"e":196.83,"t":"He didn't want me to burn out before I'd started racing."},{"s":197.72,"e":201.44,"t":"In the end we got the balance right and I went into the race feeling great."},{"s":202.46,"e":213.37,"t":"This was one of the toughest races of the season. You're pushed to your limit in races like this. The training was paying off though. I was feeling good and I was well placed in the leading group."},{"s":214.07,"e":217.95,"t":"That's when I heard a crunching sound. And then the gears just jammed."},{"s":218.58,"e":222.21,"t":"I jumped off and tried to fix it, but the race was over for me."},{"s":223.16,"e":228.73,"t":"was in a bad state. I was so angry and disappointed. I never expected the bike to let me down."}]},{"n":39,"q":"You hear five people speaking about their relationships with their motorbikes. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi mototsikllari bilan bog'liqligi haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people speaking about their relationships with their motorbikes","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"Learning to ride a motorbike gave me a good living.","u":"Mototsikl haydashni o'rganish menga yaxshi daromad berdi."},{"l":"B","t":"Don't get on a bike without having classes.","u":"Dars olmasdan mototsiklga minmang."},{"l":"C","t":"My bike was too big for me.","u":"Mototsiklim menga juda katta edi."},{"l":"D","t":"My bike helps me relax.","u":"Mototsiklim dam olishimga yordam beradi."},{"l":"E","t":"My bike means the world to me.","u":"Mototsiklim men uchun hamma narsa."},{"l":"F","t":"A bike stands for something more than just a set of wheels.","u":"Mototsikl shunchaki g'ildiraklardan ko'ra ko'proq narsani anglatadi."},{"l":"G","t":"My bike gave me some fond memories.","u":"Mototsiklim menga yoqimli xotiralar berdi."},{"l":"H","t":"I miss my first bike.","u":"Birinchi mototsiklimni sog'inaman."}],"dur":478.6,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":10.9,"en":45.89,"ev":"If you want to ride a motorbike in the UK, you'll have to take a short course first… the police recommend that you go on an advanced motorcycle handling course. They are excellent and could save your life one day.","uz":"Buyuk Britaniyada mototsikl haydamoqchi bo'lsangiz, avval qisqa kursdan o'tishingiz kerak… politsiya ilg'or boshqaruv kursiga borishni tavsiya qiladi. Ular a'lo va bir kun hayotingizni saqlab qolishi mumkin.","why":"Darssiz minmang — B.","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":47.42,"en":82.3,"ev":"When I'm on the bike it's just me and the machine… it's a great way to relieve stress and blow the cobwebs off at the end of the day.","uz":"Mototsiklda bo'lganimda faqat men va mashina… kun oxirida stressni chiqarib, boshni yangilashning ajoyib usuli.","why":"Dam olishga yordam beradi (D).","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":83.0,"en":128.48,"ev":"My first partner was my mum… We were a good team and enjoyed racing together.","uz":"Birinchi sherigim onam edi… Biz yaxshi jamoa edik va birga poygada qatnashishdan zavq olardik.","why":"Yoqimli xotiralar (G). Onasi birinchi motoni sotib olgan — H emas (sog'inish aytilmaydi).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":129.46,"en":168.48,"ev":"A motorbike is more than a vehicle to get you from A to B. A biker is like a knight on horseback.","uz":"Mototsikl sizni A dan B ga olib boradigan transportdan ko'proq narsa. Motochi — ot mingan ritsarga o'xshaydi.","why":"Shunchaki g'ildiraklardan ko'proq narsani anglatadi (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":169.56,"en":240.57,"ev":"I was lucky to have had a career as a test rider with a company called BSA… I'd answered a newspaper advertisement for a test rider and was thrilled when I got the job.","uz":"BSA kompaniyasida sinov haydovchisi bo'lib ishlash baxtiga muyassar bo'ldim… Gazetadagi e'longa javob berib, ishga olinganimda juda xursand bo'ldim.","why":"Mototsikl unga kasb va daromad bergan (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.97,"e":7.04,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about a particular subject."},{"k":"h","s":10.9,"e":10.9,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":13.59,"e":16.61,"t":"people get into motorcycling for different reasons."},{"s":17.05,"e":36.54,"t":"For me it was my family. I was around bikes from an early age. If you want to ride a motorbike in the UK, you'll have to take a short course first. Even if you've passed your test and have been driving for years, the police recommend that you go on an advanced motorcycle handling course. They are excellent and could save your life one day."},{"s":37.24,"e":45.89,"t":"The course shows you how to avoid accidents, how to drive on motorways and how to drive safely at high speeds, plus loads of other things."},{"k":"h","s":47.42,"e":47.42,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":50.01,"e":53.37,"t":"I suppose you don't get many moms in full biker leathers."},{"s":53.88,"e":61.79,"t":"I get a lot of thumbs up from other women drivers. It gives me plenty of street cred being a leather clad woman on a big motorbike."},{"s":62.3,"e":72.96,"t":"I don't do it for the look though, it's more for the freedom. It's actually a very convenient way of travelling around the city. Riding a bike is a lot different to driving a car, which I prefer."},{"s":73.43,"e":82.3,"t":"When I'm on the bike it's just me and the machine. I know it sounds a bit macho but it's a great way to relieve stress and blow the cobwebs off at the end of the day."},{"k":"h","s":83.0,"e":83.0,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":85.5,"e":97.28,"t":"Motorbike and sidecar racing isn't a very popular sport, but I love it. It's all about speed and balance. It's a lot harder racing when you've got a sidecar attached to your motorbike."},{"s":98.01,"e":101.73,"t":"There has to be a good understanding between both rider and passenger."},{"s":102.39,"e":106.81,"t":"My first partner was my mum, which caused the other riders to tease me a bit."},{"s":107.42,"e":118.69,"t":"Everybody knew her in the racing world because she was a real character and used to race bikes when she was younger. My mum bought me my first bike. We were a good team and enjoyed racing together."},{"s":119.35,"e":121.79,"t":"I don't know what our friends and families really thought."},{"s":122.36,"e":128.48,"t":"Probably, like most people, they saw it as dangerous. And the last thing a mother should be encouraging her son to do."},{"k":"h","s":129.46,"e":129.46,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":132.6,"e":147.74,"t":"The image of a motorcyclist is iconic in society. It represents freedom and rebellion and not just the freedom of the open road, but the biker is often seen to be on the edge of the law, free from moral constraints and free from having to be respectable."},{"s":148.31,"e":154.43,"t":"It's the ultimate freedom, a fusion of man and machine, cutting through traffic leaving everyone behind."},{"s":155.0,"e":157.95,"t":"The only trouble is that it happens to be quite dangerous."},{"s":158.55,"e":168.48,"t":"A motorbike is more than a vehicle to get you from A to B. A biker is like a knight on horseback in a world which is a little different and a little dangerous from everyone else's."},{"k":"h","s":169.56,"e":169.56,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":172.38,"e":179.77,"t":"I've always been passionate about motorbikes and was lucky to have had a career as a test rider with a company called BSA."},{"s":180.34,"e":185.89,"t":"They were one of the best British motorcycle manufacturers, but they closed down in 1978."},{"s":186.39,"e":188.57,"t":"It was a very sad moment in time for me."},{"s":189.02,"e":197.6,"t":"Their name BSA stood for British Small Arms, which is a strange name for a motorcycle manufacturer, but they made other things as well."},{"s":198.2,"e":204.06,"t":"When I joined BSA in Birmingham in 1955, British bikes were the best in the world."},{"s":204.6,"e":209.98,"t":"I'd answered a newspaper advertisement for a test rider and was thrilled when I got the job."},{"s":210.42,"e":215.42,"t":"I was only 18 and motorbike crazy as I had been riding since the age of 11."},{"s":215.96,"e":226.05,"t":"Being a test rider was great because I got to take part in all sorts of motorbike riding like speedway, races, hill climbing and reliability trials."},{"s":226.84,"e":233.5,"t":"When the company closed down, I did some exhibition writing with my brother, and we called our show \"The Partners of Dare\"."},{"s":234.07,"e":240.57,"t":"There were good times and even though I am getting a bit old now, I still go out for a ride every Sunday on my BSA Goldstar."}]},{"n":40,"q":"You hear some people talking about the hotel they stayed in. What does each speaker say about their hotel?","qu":"Odamlar turgan mehmonxonalari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about the hotel they stayed in","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"We liked it because they were set up to keep the kids happy.","u":"Bolalarni xursand qilishga moslashgani uchun yoqdi."},{"l":"B","t":"They rented bikes which was good.","u":"Velosiped ijaraga berishardi, bu yaxshi edi."},{"l":"C","t":"The management were very informed about outdoor activities.","u":"Ma'muriyat ochiq havodagi mashg'ulotlar haqida juda yaxshi xabardor edi."},{"l":"D","t":"It was too noisy.","u":"Juda shovqinli edi."},{"l":"E","t":"They had a lot of space and great deals for the kids.","u":"Joy ko'p va bolalar uchun ajoyib chegirmalar bor edi."},{"l":"F","t":"The facilities for the kids were disappointing.","u":"Bolalar uchun sharoitlar hafsalani pir qildi."},{"l":"G","t":"Only good for very young children, but the service was great.","u":"Faqat juda kichik bolalar uchun yaxshi, lekin xizmat a'lo edi."},{"l":"H","t":"I was not impressed with the food.","u":"Ovqat menga unchalik yoqmadi."}],"dur":430.0,"items":[{"a":"A","ps":10.46,"en":42.69,"ev":"The staff are great and there's lots of stuff for the kids to do. If the kids are happy then we are happy.","uz":"Xodimlar a'lo va bolalar uchun mashg'ulotlar ko'p. Bolalar xursand bo'lsa, biz ham xursandmiz.","why":"Bolalarni xursand qilishga moslashgan (A).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":44.5,"en":99.1,"ev":"The staff and owners are all great fun. They're very outdoorsy type people. They're into mountain biking themselves and know all the good routes.","uz":"Xodimlar va egalari juda quvnoq. Ular tabiatni sevadigan odamlar: o'zlari tog' velosipedida yurishadi va barcha yaxshi yo'nalishlarni bilishadi.","why":"Ochiq havodagi mashg'ulotlardan xabardor ma'muriyat (C). Velosiped bepul edi — ijaraga emas (B tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":100.22,"en":135.55,"ev":"The rooms are big and have four proper beds. Children under 10 go free.","uz":"Xonalar katta, to'rtta haqiqiy karavot bor. 10 yoshgacha bolalar bepul.","why":"Joy ko'p va bolalarga chegirma (E).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":137.21,"en":178.49,"ev":"I did feel that there could have been a few more things for the kids to do… there was just one old swing which was a bit disappointing.","uz":"Bolalar uchun ko'proq mashg'ulot bo'lishi mumkin edi deb o'yladim… faqat bitta eski arg'imchoq bor edi, bu biroz hafsalani pir qildi.","why":"Bolalar uchun sharoit qoniqarsiz (F).","hl":null},{"a":"G","ps":179.32,"en":217.09,"ev":"It would not be that good for older children, but for us it is fine… the staff could not do enough for you.","uz":"Kattaroq bolalar uchun unchalik yaxshi emas, lekin bizga mos… xodimlar hamma narsani qilishga tayyor edi.","why":"Faqat kichik bolalar uchun, xizmat a'lo (G).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.74,"e":6.59,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about a particular subject."},{"k":"h","s":10.46,"e":10.46,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":11.7,"e":18.94,"t":"We like staying in this hotel because it is cheap and child-friendly. The rooms are a little small and basic, but they're fine."},{"s":19.42,"e":25.41,"t":"The staff are great and there's lots of stuff for the kids to do. If the kids are happy then we are happy."},{"s":26.14,"e":30.37,"t":"You can book the kids in for an early child's meal and eat later yourself."},{"s":30.97,"e":34.27,"t":"There's a large garden with a treehouse and a playground."},{"s":34.81,"e":42.69,"t":"If the weather isn't good, there's a playroom inside and a ballpark which the kids love. We definitely come here again. 2."},{"k":"h","s":44.5,"e":44.5,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":44.5,"e":47.1,"t":"This hotel is really geared towards family holidays."},{"s":47.58,"e":53.66,"t":"It is not the cheapest, but you can get a small suite, a bedroom with a separate sitting room for a reasonable price."},{"s":54.17,"e":62.08,"t":"It's good to be able to put the kids to bed in their own room. Then we can stay up a little later and use the sofa bed to sleep on. It's very comfortable."},{"s":63.03,"e":66.46,"t":"There is a heated outdoor swimming pool and the kids are in it all the time."},{"s":66.9,"e":72.16,"t":"The hotel also had free mountain bikes which was also great as we loved cycling as a family."},{"s":73.11,"e":75.07,"t":"The staff and owners are all great fun."},{"s":75.8,"e":81.34,"t":"They're very outdoorsy type people. They're into mountain biking themselves and know all the good routes."},{"s":82.1,"e":88.29,"t":"They also have a tennis court. I'm not keen on tennis but my partner is. He always meets someone to play with."},{"s":88.76,"e":90.3,"t":"It's a very friendly place."},{"s":90.9,"e":96.03,"t":"We stay half bored, the food is very good and there's plenty of vegetarian options to choose from."},{"s":96.63,"e":99.1,"t":"Families with young children have their own dining room."},{"k":"h","s":100.22,"e":100.22,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":101.78,"e":110.46,"t":"Last year we stayed in a hotel which wasn't very child friendly. So this year I booked somewhere with lots of things to keep the kids entertained."},{"s":111.1,"e":116.16,"t":"place is perfect because there's a large adventure playground and they have family rooms."},{"s":116.6,"e":119.1,"t":"The rooms are big and have 4 proper beds."},{"s":119.58,"e":121.44,"t":"children under 10 go free."},{"s":122.52,"e":124.57,"t":"plenty of other activities nearby."},{"s":125.02,"e":128.13,"t":"There's horse riding mini golf paddle."},{"s":128.76,"e":129.82,"t":"public swimming pool."},{"s":130.52,"e":135.55,"t":"It's a really big pool with slides and a wave machine. The kids had a fabulous time."},{"k":"h","s":137.21,"e":137.21,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":138.74,"e":142.69,"t":"Family sweet was good. You had two decent sized rooms."},{"s":143.48,"e":147.07,"t":"but I did feel that they could have been a few more things for the kids to do."},{"s":147.8,"e":150.62,"t":"A few board games for the kids to play, maybe."},{"s":151.22,"e":156.7,"t":"The outside garden was good, but there was just one old swing which was a bit disappointing."},{"s":157.46,"e":160.48,"t":"The saving grace was the outdoor heated pool."},{"s":160.98,"e":163.55,"t":"which is where the kids spent the entire holiday."},{"s":164.18,"e":169.66,"t":"Unfortunately, children under the age of 10 were not allowed in the dining room after 9pm."},{"s":170.3,"e":178.49,"t":"So you had to eat at separate times, the kids having their meals first and then after putting them down to bed, you could go down and have yours."},{"k":"h","s":179.32,"e":179.32,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":180.95,"e":183.52,"t":"This is a really nice family run hotel."},{"s":184.25,"e":189.95,"t":"The kids love our room, it's really cheery with books, teddy bears and some wooden toys."},{"s":190.87,"e":194.53,"t":"It would not be that good for older children, but for us it is fine."},{"s":195.19,"e":197.5,"t":"We can put our kids in bed at 8pm."},{"s":198.01,"e":199.29,"t":"and then come down to dine"},{"s":200.02,"e":203.87,"t":"There are no kids in the lounge and dining room after 7.30pm."},{"s":204.76,"e":207.23,"t":"This seems a little early if you had older children."},{"s":208.18,"e":210.78,"t":"The children's dining time is at 6pm."},{"s":211.51,"e":217.09,"t":"We had a super stay and were made to feel very welcome and the staff could not do enough for you."}]},{"n":41,"q":"You will hear a couple who have recently moved home talking about items that they use in their flat. Which item are they talking about?","qu":"Yaqinda ko'chib o'tgan er-xotin kvartiradagi buyumlar haqida gapiradi. Qaysi buyum haqida gap ketyapti?","topic":"couple who have recently moved home talking about items that they use in their f","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"a pair of pillows","u":"bir juft yostiq"},{"l":"B","t":"a CD","u":"CD disk"},{"l":"C","t":"a sleeping bag","u":"uxlash xaltasi"},{"l":"D","t":"a dishwasher","u":"idish yuvish mashinasi"},{"l":"E","t":"scissors","u":"qaychi"},{"l":"F","t":"laptop","u":"noutbuk"}],"dur":268.7,"items":[{"a":"B","ps":2.39,"en":54.14,"ev":"I know it's been on again and again on the radio, but I want to own it… I still get a thrill having the hard copy in my hand.","uz":"Bilaman, u radioda qayta-qayta yangraydi, lekin o'zimniki bo'lishini xohlayman… qo'limda fizik nusxasi bo'lishi hali ham hayajonlantiradi.","why":"Radio, qo'shiq, \"hard copy\" — CD (B).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":64.5,"en":134.08,"ev":"It's so much quicker than doing everything by hand… I'll stack it all inside now. So we have to choose a programme for the wash.","uz":"Hammasini qo'lda qilishdan ancha tez… Endi hammasini ichiga teraman. Yuvish dasturini tanlashimiz kerak.","why":"Idishlar, yuvish dasturi — idish yuvish mashinasi (D).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":144.22,"en":201.89,"ev":"I wanted some filled with real feathers… You just sink into them… I think I'm ready to lay my head down.","uz":"Haqiqiy pat bilan to'ldirilganlarini xohlardim… Ularga cho'kib ketasiz… Boshimni qo'yishga tayyorman shekilli.","why":"Bosh qo'yiladigan, juft — yostiqlar (A). Uxlash xaltasi emas (C tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":212.02,"en":265.76,"ev":"We must have loads of pairs… They've got to be sharp enough for the carpet… Wow, they're sharp.","uz":"Bizda bir talay juft bo'lsa kerak… Gilamni kesadigan darajada o'tkir bo'lishi kerak… Voy, o'tkir ekan.","why":"\"Pairs… sharp… sewing\" — qaychi (E).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":2.39,"e":2.39,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":3.9,"e":22.78,"t":"This is my current favourite. It's like a soundtrack to my life now. Ah, so you've bought it at last. I thought you might. Yes, I know it's been on again and again on the radio, but I want it to own it. You really should get into sharing. It's so much easier. I suppose so, but I still get a thrill having the hard copy in my hand."},{"s":35.29,"e":54.14,"t":"This is my current favourite. It's like a soundtrack to my life now. Ah, so you've bought it at last. I thought you might. Yes, I know it's been on again and again on the radio, but I want it to own it. You really should get into sharing. It's so much easier. I suppose so, but I still get a thrill having the hard copy in my hand."},{"k":"h","s":64.5,"e":64.5,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":65.98,"e":79.2,"t":"I'm so pleased we got this. It's so much quicker than doing everything by hand. True, though it's more expensive and I'm not sure it's environmentally friendly. It's better though. Everything comes out really clean and shiny."},{"s":79.67,"e":86.85,"t":"But I still wouldn't put our finest crockery in. Okay, I've rinsed everything. I'll stack it all inside now."},{"s":87.29,"e":90.4,"t":"So we have to choose a program for the wash. What do you think?"},{"s":90.84,"e":91.84,"t":"This one will do."},{"s":92.34,"e":93.85,"t":"It's only 15 minutes."},{"s":106.17,"e":124.7,"t":"I'm so pleased we got this. It's so much quicker than doing everything by hand. True, though it's more expensive and I'm not sure it's environmentally friendly. It's better though. Everything comes out really clean and shiny, but I still wouldn't put our finest crockery in. Okay, I've rinsed everything."},{"s":125.14,"e":127.04,"t":"I'll stack it all inside now."},{"s":127.48,"e":130.59,"t":"So we have to choose a program for the wash. What do you think?"},{"s":131.06,"e":132.03,"t":"This one will do."},{"s":132.57,"e":134.08,"t":"It's only 15 minutes."},{"k":"h","s":144.22,"e":144.22,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":145.85,"e":161.25,"t":"Why ever do we need new ones? Well, I'm really sold on natural materials now. I wanted some filled with real feathers. The old ones were comfortable enough, I thought. You just try these and you'll feel the difference. You just sink into them and they smell crispy clean."},{"s":161.69,"e":162.17,"t":"Okay."},{"s":162.68,"e":166.21,"t":"I think I'm ready to lay my head down. It's been a long day."},{"s":166.84,"e":167.61,"t":"What do you think"},{"s":180.15,"e":196.45,"t":"Why ever do we need new ones? Well, I'm really sold on natural materials now. I wanted some filled with real feathers. The old ones were comfortable enough, I thought. You just try these and you'll feel the difference. You just sink into them and they smell crispy clean. Okay."},{"s":196.92,"e":200.48,"t":"I think I'm ready to lay my head down. It's been a long day."},{"s":201.11,"e":201.89,"t":"What do you think"},{"k":"h","s":212.02,"e":212.02,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":213.53,"e":224.61,"t":"We must have loads of pairs, but however hard I search, I can never find them. Look in the drawer over there. There'll be some amongst my sewing materials. Are they suitable for the job, though?"},{"s":225.14,"e":227.29,"t":"They've got to be sharp enough for the carpet."},{"s":228.06,"e":231.07,"t":"Ah, maybe not. Use the ones in the toolbox then. Got them."},{"s":231.64,"e":233.25,"t":"Wow, the shop!"},{"s":246.14,"e":257.21,"t":"We must have loads of pairs, but however hard I search, I can never find them. Look in the drawer over there. There'll be some amongst my sewing materials. Are they suitable for the job, though?"},{"s":257.75,"e":259.93,"t":"They've got to be sharp enough for the carpet."},{"s":260.66,"e":263.68,"t":"Ah, maybe not. Use the ones in the toolbox then. Got them."},{"s":264.28,"e":265.76,"t":"Wow, they're sharp."}]},{"n":42,"q":"You hear five people talking about why they took up sport. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi nima uchun sport bilan shug'ullana boshlagani haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about why they took up sport","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I was persuaded to do it by other people.","u":"Boshqalar meni bunga ko'ndirishdi."},{"l":"B","t":"I needed to set myself a new challenge.","u":"O'zimga yangi sinov qo'yishim kerak edi."},{"l":"C","t":"I did it to raise money for charity.","u":"Xayriya uchun pul yig'ish maqsadida qildim."},{"l":"D","t":"I wanted to give my family a surprise.","u":"Oilamni hayratda qoldirmoqchi edim."},{"l":"E","t":"I wanted to find a way to relax.","u":"Dam olish yo'lini topmoqchi edim."},{"l":"F","t":"I wanted to prove to someone that I could do it.","u":"Kimgadir buni uddalay olishimni isbotlamoqchi edim."}],"dur":235.0,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":13.66,"en":54.3,"ev":"I had no choice but to do it though because the whole point was to get people to give donations to a medical research organisation.","uz":"Lekin buni qilishdan boshqa ilojim yo'q edi, chunki butun maqsad — odamlarni tibbiy tadqiqot tashkilotiga xayriya qilishga undash edi.","why":"Xayriya uchun pul yig'ish (C).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":57.78,"en":102.05,"ev":"Not because I'd changed my mind about wanting to swim, just so that I could see the expressions of amazement on my kids' faces.","uz":"Suzishni xohlab qolganim uchun emas, shunchaki bolalarimning yuzidagi hayratni ko'rish uchun.","why":"Oilasini hayratda qoldirish (D). Basseyn yonida dam olishni afzal ko'radi — E emas.","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":105.24,"en":144.22,"ev":"In fact, I had to be talked into doing it by my friends. They… kept on at me until I agreed to give it a go.","uz":"Aslida meni bunga do'stlarim ko'ndirishdi. Ular… rozi bo'lgunimcha tinmay qistashdi.","why":"Boshqalar ko'ndirgan (A).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":147.9,"en":190.56,"ev":"My main motive for taking up scuba diving… is because my boyfriend Tony said I wouldn't be able to do it… I was determined to show Tony that he was wrong.","uz":"Akvalang bilan sho'ng'ishni boshlashimning asosiy sababi — yigitim Toni buni uddalay olmaysan degani… Toniga uning noto'g'ri ekanini ko'rsatishga qaror qildim.","why":"Kimgadir isbotlash (F). Yangi sinov emas, aynan isbot.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":194.14,"en":231.23,"ev":"I wanted something to help me unwind after a stressful day at work.","uz":"Ishdagi asabiy kundan keyin bo'shashishga yordam beradigan narsa xohlardim.","why":"Dam olish yo'li (E).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.68,"e":8.86,"t":"You will hear five short extracts in which people say why they took up a sport."},{"k":"h","s":13.66,"e":13.66,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":17.4,"e":20.8,"t":"My first parachute jump was the scariest thing I'd ever done."},{"s":21.59,"e":25.34,"t":"Nothing prepares you for falling out of a plane at 180 km/h."},{"s":26.1,"e":28.86,"t":"After all, you can't turn back if you change your mind, can you"},{"s":29.66,"e":31.58,"t":"When it came to actually jumping..."},{"s":32.02,"e":33.25,"t":"I got very nervous."},{"s":34.36,"e":40.67,"t":"I had no choice but to do it though because the whole point was to get people to give donations to a medical research organisation."},{"s":41.78,"e":44.35,"t":"If I hadn't jumped, I wouldn't have got any money for them"},{"s":45.78,"e":54.3,"t":"Once back on the ground, I realised I'd loved it. And that was the beginning of my big hobby, much to the amazement of my friends and family."},{"k":"h","s":57.78,"e":57.78,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":60.79,"e":69.02,"t":"I grew up surrounded by water. You could see the Atlantic from my bedroom window and yet I'd never learnt to swim."},{"s":70.68,"e":75.2,"t":"I just never fancied it, even though my parents and brother swam like fish."},{"s":76.31,"e":84.8,"t":"I finally signed up for a five week beginners course at the age of 35. Not because I'd changed my mind about wanting to swim."},{"s":85.91,"e":94.05,"t":"just so that I could see the expressions of amazement on my kids' faces. It was worth suffering those awful lessons just for that."},{"s":94.87,"e":102.05,"t":"But I must admit that even now I'd much rather relax at the poolside and watch them splashing about."},{"k":"h","s":105.24,"e":105.24,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":108.18,"e":110.4,"t":"I took up skiing while I was living abroad."},{"s":111.42,"e":113.53,"t":"absolutely loved it from the word go."},{"s":114.04,"e":119.04,"t":"the scenery, of course, the sense of speed and complete focus on the task."},{"s":119.61,"e":121.53,"t":"It's fantastic exercise to"},{"s":122.42,"e":124.51,"t":"I hadn't expected to enjoy it though."},{"s":124.95,"e":128.41,"t":"In fact, I had to be talked into doing it by my friends."},{"s":129.02,"e":134.43,"t":"They'd all skied since they were very small and kept on at me until I agreed to give it a go."},{"s":135.16,"e":139.01,"t":"I'm much older now and obviously not as fit as I used to be."},{"s":139.54,"e":144.22,"t":"But if I could find the money, I'd like to take the kids and see if I can still do it."},{"k":"h","s":147.9,"e":147.9,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":150.94,"e":158.65,"t":"I'm not really into risky sports but I enjoyed snorkelling and quite fancied getting a closer look at exotic fish."},{"s":159.45,"e":167.71,"t":"My main motive for taking up scuba diving though, to be honest, is because my boyfriend Tony said I wouldn't be able to do it."},{"s":168.63,"e":173.53,"t":"I tend to panic you see and in scuba diving you have to remain totally calm."},{"s":173.98,"e":175.97,"t":"or things can get very dangerous."},{"s":176.79,"e":182.72,"t":"It took me ages to gain the confidence to do it, but I was determined to show Tony that he was wrong."},{"s":183.32,"e":190.56,"t":"So I persevered and I've now passed all my exams and we're off on a diving holiday together soon."},{"k":"h","s":194.14,"e":194.14,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":197.3,"e":198.81,"t":"I've always been into football."},{"s":199.26,"e":201.95,"t":"All my friends were, it was something we could all share."},{"s":203.0,"e":207.87,"t":"Apart from a few kickabouts in the garden, it tended to be very much a spectator sport."},{"s":208.66,"e":215.93,"t":"We'd watch much of the day on the TV, play computer games like FIFA, and go to Liverpool home matches when we could afford it."},{"s":217.08,"e":221.76,"t":"Funnily enough, it was only quite recently that I started playing it on a regular basis."},{"s":222.23,"e":226.69,"t":"And that was because I wanted something to help me unwind after a stressful day at work."},{"s":227.67,"e":231.23,"t":"brilliant because it means I have to think about something other than my job."}]},{"n":43,"q":"You hear five people talking about their clothes. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi kiyimlari haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about their clothes","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"I can't afford new clothes.","u":"Yangi kiyimga pulim yetmaydi."},{"l":"B","t":"I buy good-quality clothes.","u":"Sifatli kiyim sotib olaman."},{"l":"C","t":"I don't care what I wear.","u":"Nima kiyishim menga farqi yo'q."},{"l":"D","t":"I choose clothes that are easy to look after.","u":"Parvarishi oson kiyimlarni tanlayman."},{"l":"E","t":"I wear fashionable clothes.","u":"Zamonaviy kiyimlar kiyaman."},{"l":"F","t":"It's important that my clothes are clean.","u":"Kiyimlarim toza bo'lishi muhim."},{"l":"G","t":"I dress to look smart.","u":"Ozoda (bejirim) ko'rinish uchun kiyinaman."},{"l":"H","t":"My priority is to be comfortable.","u":"Men uchun eng muhimi — qulaylik."}],"dur":216.5,"items":[{"a":"G","ps":5.05,"en":41.25,"ev":"The first impression my clients get of me is fairly crucial, so I spend time looking for clothes that are business-like.","uz":"Mijozlarimda men haqimda paydo bo'ladigan birinchi taassurot juda muhim, shuning uchun ishbilarmonlarga xos kiyim izlashga vaqt sarflayman.","why":"Ozoda, rasmiy ko'rinish (G). Qimmat kiyim olmaydi — B emas.","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":45.11,"en":79.17,"ev":"There's no point in dressing up in smart clothes anyway… what matters is feeling relaxed and not having to worry about what you look like.","uz":"Har holda chiroyli kiyinishning ma'nosi yo'q… muhimi — o'zingni erkin his qilish va qanday ko'rinishingdan tashvishlanmaslik.","why":"Qulaylik ustuvor (H). Brendli krossovka — moda emas, sport kiyimi.","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":82.49,"en":131.87,"ev":"At the moment either very short or very long skirts are cool… I wouldn't dream of wearing anything sort of frumpy or like my mum wears.","uz":"Hozir juda qisqa yoki juda uzun yubkalar urfda… Onam kiyadigan eskicha kiyimni kiyishni xayolimga ham keltirmayman.","why":"Zamonaviy kiyim (E).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":135.26,"en":170.97,"ev":"I don't think about clothes very much… I'll wear anything as long as it's warm and not too scruffy. I'm certainly not trying to impress anyone.","uz":"Kiyim haqida ko'p o'ylamayman… Issiq va juda yirtiq bo'lmasa, nima bo'lsa ham kiyaveraman. Hech kimni hayratda qoldirmoqchi emasman.","why":"Nima kiyishiga befarq (C). Pulga qodir emas demaydi — A emas.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":174.62,"en":211.17,"ev":"I do tend to spend quite a lot on my clothes but then I can wear them over and over again and they don't drop to pieces. It's an investment.","uz":"Kiyimlarimga ancha pul sarflayman, lekin ularni qayta-qayta kiyaman va ular tez yirtilmaydi. Bu sarmoya.","why":"Sifatli kiyim (B). Amaliylik ham bor, lekin asosiysi — sifat.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":5.05,"e":5.05,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":8.09,"e":16.0,"t":"During the week when I'm at work I tend to wear fitted jackets, high heels, straight skirts, you know, quite stylish clothes."},{"s":16.7,"e":22.49,"t":"The first impression my clients get of me is fairly crucial, so I spend time looking for clothes that are business-like."},{"s":23.29,"e":27.49,"t":"I can't afford to spend too much on them though. I don't buy expensive clothes."},{"s":28.22,"e":35.65,"t":"It's got to the point where I don't feel right in casual clothes so even at the weekends I'll still wear the same kind of thing but..."},{"s":36.31,"e":41.25,"t":"swap the jacket and heels for a sweater and flat shoes. Um, pumps."},{"k":"h","s":45.11,"e":45.11,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":47.77,"e":50.05,"t":"I always wear the same things when I'm not at school."},{"s":50.78,"e":55.77,"t":"Tracksuit bottoms, a fleece or a t-shirt and designer trainers."},{"s":56.28,"e":57.41,"t":"Nearly all my friends do."},{"s":58.1,"e":63.68,"t":"I've also got three different football kits. Man United, England and Barcelona."},{"s":64.38,"e":65.09,"t":"in the summer."},{"s":65.62,"e":70.33,"t":"I sometimes wear shorts instead of tracksuit bottoms, but it's always sports stuff."},{"s":70.94,"e":74.53,"t":"There's no point in dressing up in smart clothes anyway. They just get dirty."},{"s":75.13,"e":79.17,"t":"what matters is feeling relaxed and not having to worry about what you look like."},{"k":"h","s":82.49,"e":82.49,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":85.46,"e":89.25,"t":"Well, I've always had a fairly clear idea of how I want to look."},{"s":89.78,"e":96.32,"t":"I want to be a designer when I leave school and I'm always flicking through magazines to pick up ideas."},{"s":97.18,"e":117.98,"t":"At the moment either very short or very long skirts are cool, worn with trainers or wedges, nothing in between and low waisted trousers. Strong patterns and crop tops in bright colours. Even colours that clash like lime green and pink are popular too."},{"s":118.9,"e":123.58,"t":"I wouldn't dream of wearing anything sort of frumpy or like my mum wears."},{"s":124.12,"e":131.87,"t":"I even try to adapt my school uniform a bit to personalise it so I might wear patterned or striped tights with it."},{"k":"h","s":135.26,"e":135.26,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":138.3,"e":140.54,"t":"I don't think about clothes very much."},{"s":141.34,"e":143.58,"t":"I suppose I wear what I've always worn."},{"s":144.63,"e":148.86,"t":"a shirt and tie with trousers and maybe a sweater."},{"s":150.3,"e":152.51,"t":"I don't spend much money on clothes so..."},{"s":153.14,"e":155.29,"t":"Most of them are a few years old."},{"s":156.47,"e":158.62,"t":"sometimes go into charity shops."},{"s":159.51,"e":161.89,"t":"and my son gives me things he's fed up with."},{"s":163.38,"e":164.48,"t":"I'll wear anything"},{"s":164.98,"e":167.39,"t":"as long as it's warm and not too scruffy."},{"s":168.5,"e":170.97,"t":"I'm certainly not trying to impress anyone."},{"k":"h","s":174.62,"e":174.62,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":177.82,"e":182.33,"t":"I like clothes, but I'm not a fashion victim and I don't dress up."},{"s":182.84,"e":188.89,"t":"Now I've got kids, my clothes have to be practical, so no high heels and tight skirts these days."},{"s":189.56,"e":195.93,"t":"If I said that, I don't want to end up living in tracksuits or jeans and baggy jumpers all the time, like some mums."},{"s":196.7,"e":201.6,"t":"I go for casual but well cut clothes in natural fabrics like silk or cotton."},{"s":202.74,"e":209.5,"t":"I do tend to spend quite a lot on my clothes but then I can wear them over and over again and they don't drop to pieces."},{"s":209.94,"e":211.17,"t":"It's an investment."}]},{"n":44,"q":"You hear five people talking about their favourite transport. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi sevimli transporti haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about their favourite transport","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"It is a safe way to travel.","u":"Bu xavfsiz yurish usuli."},{"l":"B","t":"I found driving my car too stressful.","u":"Mashina haydash men uchun juda asabiy edi."},{"l":"C","t":"I wanted to avoid being in large crowds.","u":"Katta olomondan qochmoqchi edim."},{"l":"D","t":"It's a reliable form of transport.","u":"Bu ishonchli transport turi."},{"l":"E","t":"I like surprising the people I work with.","u":"Hamkasblarimni hayratda qoldirishni yaxshi ko'raman."},{"l":"F","t":"It helps me to get more work done.","u":"Ko'proq ish bajarishimga yordam beradi."},{"l":"G","t":"I'm helping to keep the environment clean.","u":"Atrof-muhitni toza saqlashga hissa qo'shyapman."},{"l":"H","t":"I bought it to save money.","u":"Pulni tejash uchun sotib oldim."}],"dur":233.6,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":7.51,"en":49.12,"ev":"It has shrunk London for me and means I can fit in more business meetings than I used to before.","uz":"U Londonni men uchun kichraytirdi — endi avvalgidan ko'proq ish uchrashuvlariga ulguraman.","why":"Ko'proq ish bajarishga yordam (F). Ba'zan o't olmaydi — ishonchli emas (D tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":52.25,"en":101.41,"ev":"I started cycling to work around the time of the terrorist attacks on the underground… I'd always hated being squashed in with all these other people during the rush hour.","uz":"Metrodagi teraktlar paytida ishga velosipedda borishni boshladim… Tig'iz soatlarda odamlar orasida siqilib qolishni doim yomon ko'rardim.","why":"Olomondan qochish (C). Arzon sotib olgan — H tuzoq.","hl":null},{"a":"H","ps":105.3,"en":145.28,"ev":"It all began 20 years ago when I was a student and I was looking for something cheaper to run than a car. Now I use it every day for the same reason.","uz":"Hammasi 20 yil oldin, talabaligimda mashinadan arzonroq ishlaydigan transport izlaganimda boshlangan. Hozir ham shu sabab bilan har kuni ishlataman.","why":"Pul tejash (H).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":148.57,"en":187.58,"ev":"People do often look really astonished when I turn up to important meetings on my scooter, which is great. It's good to challenge people's expectations.","uz":"Muhim uchrashuvlarga skuterda kelganimda odamlar ko'pincha hayratlanadi — bu zo'r. Odamlarning kutganini buzish yaxshi.","why":"Hamkasblarni hayratga solish (E).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":190.9,"en":231.68,"ev":"You always know how long the journey's going to take, whereas you can't depend on public transport.","uz":"Yo'l qancha vaqt olishini doim bilasiz, jamoat transportiga esa ishonib bo'lmaydi.","why":"Ishonchli transport (D). Xavfsiz emasligini his qiladi — A emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":7.51,"e":7.51,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":10.46,"e":14.3,"t":"About four years ago, during a tube strike, I was in a taxi."},{"s":14.74,"e":22.91,"t":"I was running late for a meeting because, as usual at rush hour, all the roads were jammed. Suddenly, I saw this scooter in the window of a showroom."},{"s":23.38,"e":25.31,"t":"And that's when I had my flash of inspiration."},{"s":26.07,"e":31.23,"t":"I jumped out of the cab, did all the paperwork in 15 minutes and still got to my meeting on time."},{"s":32.34,"e":38.65,"t":"The bike can't go above 50km/h, but it doesn't seem that slow because you can overtake lines of cars."},{"s":39.19,"e":49.12,"t":"I must admit it sometimes doesn't start, which is a pain, but when it does go it has shrunk London for me and means I can fit in more business meetings than I used to before."},{"k":"h","s":52.25,"e":52.25,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":55.29,"e":64.45,"t":"I love my bike. It's quite comfortable with lots of gears. I bought it second hand from a colleague so it was quite cheap as well."},{"s":65.18,"e":70.72,"t":"I started cycling to work around the time of the terrorist attacks on the underground."},{"s":71.26,"e":80.61,"t":"Like lots of other people I suddenly got very scared and anyway I'd always hated being squashed in with all these other people during the rush hour."},{"s":81.21,"e":84.48,"t":"It's so much nicer being outside in the fresh air."},{"s":85.14,"e":86.91,"t":"Apart from when it's freezing of course."},{"s":87.35,"e":95.42,"t":"And motorists are quite considerate to cyclists these days, although I wear a yellow jacket to be on the safe side."},{"s":96.09,"e":101.41,"t":"The only problem is all the pollution from the traffic. Perhaps I should wear a mask."},{"k":"h","s":105.3,"e":105.3,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":108.28,"e":112.03,"t":"If I drove a car, people would probably try to contact me on my mobile."},{"s":112.5,"e":120.32,"t":"Riding a bike gives me a breathing space to think about things without being interrupted for once, which is great when you have a demanding job like mine."},{"s":120.82,"e":123.49,"t":"I find I arrive at places in a much better mood."},{"s":124.15,"e":127.93,"t":"I've got a Kawasaki motorbike and I'm a passionate enthusiast."},{"s":128.44,"e":134.11,"t":"It all began 20 years ago when I was a student and I was looking for something cheaper to run than a car."},{"s":134.71,"e":136.93,"t":"Now I use it every day for the same reason."},{"s":137.5,"e":145.28,"t":"When it's windy or pouring down with rain, it's not very pleasant, but I still go out on it, although my family never thought I would stick with it."},{"k":"h","s":148.57,"e":148.57,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":151.61,"e":164.7,"t":"I'm aware that many colleagues and clients think that lawyers should drive flash cars rather than have a bike, but the great thing about a bike is there's always somewhere to leave it and you don't have to worry about getting a parking ticket."},{"s":165.37,"e":170.46,"t":"Mind you, I've had a couple of bikes stolen the last few years, despite having chained them up."},{"s":170.97,"e":179.81,"t":"People do often look really astonished when I turn up to important meetings on my scooter, which is great. It's good to challenge people's expectations."},{"s":180.28,"e":187.58,"t":"Some probably look down on this method of transport, but I don't care. The opinions of others don't matter to me in the least."},{"k":"h","s":190.9,"e":190.9,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":194.07,"e":200.73,"t":"I began cycling again because I wanted to get fit, but jogging bores me and I don't like going to the gym."},{"s":201.53,"e":205.89,"t":"I'm wary of the major roads just from lack of experience."},{"s":206.33,"e":216.19,"t":"Cars seem to go so fast, and you feel very vulnerable on a bike. But I think this will pass eventually, and I've not had an accident yet, thank goodness."},{"s":216.98,"e":220.67,"t":"I'm really glad I took it up again, because it's so convenient."},{"s":221.11,"e":231.68,"t":"You always know how long the journey's going to take, whereas you can't depend on public transport. And also hopping on a bus or tube is so expensive these days."}]},{"n":45,"q":"You hear four people. Where is each speaker?","qu":"To'rt kishini eshitasiz. Har biri qayerda turibdi?","topic":"people","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"at a wedding","u":"to'yda"},{"l":"B","t":"at a birthday party","u":"tug'ilgan kun ziyofatida"},{"l":"C","t":"at a leaving party","u":"xayrlashuv ziyofatida"},{"l":"D","t":"in a university lecture hall","u":"universitet ma'ruza zalida"},{"l":"E","t":"at a funeral","u":"dafn marosimida"},{"l":"F","t":"in a classroom","u":"sinfxonada"}],"dur":326.5,"items":[{"a":"F","ps":3.96,"en":73.53,"ev":"Okay, sit down and be quiet everyone. It's good to see you all back after the Christmas holiday… What you learn between now and June will affect which university you go to.","uz":"Xo'p, hamma o'tirib, jim bo'linglar. Rojdestvo ta'tilidan keyin hammangizni ko'rganimdan xursandman… Hozirdan iyungacha o'rganganlaringiz qaysi universitetga kirishingizga ta'sir qiladi.","why":"Maktab o'qituvchisi sinfda (F). Universitet — kelajak haqida, ma'ruza zali emas (D tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":76.57,"en":164.06,"ev":"So, it's with great pleasure that I ask you all to raise your glasses in a toast to Tom and Susie on the happiest day of their lives.","uz":"Shunday ekan, hammangizdan qadahlarni Tom va Syuzining hayotidagi eng baxtli kuni sharafiga ko'tarishingizni katta mamnuniyat bilan so'rayman.","why":"\"Happiest day of their lives\" — to'y (A). Universitet — o'tmish haqida.","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":166.97,"en":253.05,"ev":"Neil has been an important person in this company… You will all miss him.","uz":"Nil bu kompaniyada muhim shaxs bo'lgan… Hammangiz uni sog'inasiz.","why":"Ishdan ketayotgan hamkasb — xayrlashuv ziyofati (C).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":254.68,"en":319.52,"ev":"Thank you all for coming on this sad occasion. Diana would be so pleased to know that she had so many good friends.","uz":"Bu qayg'uli kunda kelganingiz uchun hammangizga rahmat. Diana shuncha yaxshi do'stlari borligini bilsa, juda xursand bo'lardi.","why":"\"Sad occasion\" — dafn marosimi (E).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":3.96,"e":3.96,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":9.14,"e":13.44,"t":"Okay, sit down and be quiet everyone."},{"s":13.98,"e":16.64,"t":"It's good to see you all back after the Christmas holiday."},{"s":17.18,"e":23.17,"t":"Now, I don't want to worry you on anything, but this is a really important part of the year."},{"s":24.06,"e":32.64,"t":"What you learn between now and June will affect which university you go to. And that may determine your entire future."},{"s":33.34,"e":37.31,"t":"So you're going to have to work really hard right from the start."},{"s":45.37,"e":49.34,"t":"Okay, sit down and be quiet everyone."},{"s":50.2,"e":59.36,"t":"It's good to see you all back after the Christmas holiday. Now, I don't want to worry you or anything, but this is a really important part of the year."},{"s":60.28,"e":68.86,"t":"What you learn between now and June will affect which university you go to. And that may determine your entire future."},{"s":69.56,"e":73.53,"t":"So you're going to have to work really hard right from the start."},{"k":"h","s":76.57,"e":76.57,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":79.42,"e":87.1,"t":"As you all know, Tom and I go back a long way, since we were students at university together in fact."},{"s":87.93,"e":89.98,"t":"We've had some great times together."},{"s":90.74,"e":94.62,"t":"Lots of adventures and experiences too."},{"s":95.48,"e":99.04,"t":"We've had our ups and downs now as well."},{"s":99.7,"e":102.65,"t":"But more ups than downs, I have to say."},{"s":107.74,"e":118.49,"t":"So, it's with great pleasure that I ask you all to raise your glasses in a toast to Tom and Susie on the happiest day of their lives."},{"s":124.76,"e":132.64,"t":"As you all know, Tom and I go back a long way, since we were students at university together in fact."},{"s":133.34,"e":149.31,"t":"We've had some great times together. Lots of adventures and experiences too. We've had our ups and downs now as well. But more ups than downs I have to say. Isn't that right Tom?"},{"s":153.14,"e":164.06,"t":"So, it's with great pleasure that I ask you all to raise your glasses in a toast to Tom and Susie on the happiest day of their lives."},{"k":"h","s":166.97,"e":166.97,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":171.8,"e":177.98,"t":"I'd just like to say a few words everyone."},{"s":178.46,"e":189.47,"t":"Neil has been an important person in this company. He has organized many excellent conferences and has run his department with enthusiasm and drive."},{"s":191.48,"e":200.61,"t":"We may not always have agreed with all his ideas and initiatives, but I'm sure you'll all agree when I say"},{"s":201.05,"e":202.75,"t":"You will all miss him."},{"s":203.77,"e":209.34,"t":"especially his colleagues in marketing who dealt with him on a day-to-day basis."},{"s":215.48,"e":220.29,"t":"I'd just like to say a few words everyone."},{"s":220.73,"e":221.31,"t":"F"},{"s":222.14,"e":233.09,"t":"Neil has been an important person in this company. He has organised many excellent conferences and has run his department with enthusiasm and drive."},{"s":235.13,"e":246.4,"t":"We may not always have agreed with all his ideas and initiatives, but I'm sure you'll all agree when I say we'll all miss him."},{"s":247.45,"e":253.05,"t":"especially his colleagues in marketing who dealt with him on a day-to-day basis."},{"k":"h","s":254.68,"e":254.68,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":256.47,"e":257.82,"t":"Ladies and gentlemen."},{"s":258.78,"e":261.5,"t":"Thank you all for coming on this sad occasion."},{"s":262.49,"e":270.33,"t":"Diana would be so pleased to know that she had so many good friends and indeed so many kind relatives."},{"s":271.45,"e":273.44,"t":"I'd like to say a special thank you."},{"s":273.94,"e":277.05,"t":"those who have made long journeys to be here."},{"s":277.75,"e":279.55,"t":"Our nephews from Australia."},{"s":280.09,"e":282.14,"t":"and our cousins from South Africa."},{"s":282.68,"e":285.47,"t":"who have made such an effort to be here today."},{"s":290.58,"e":291.84,"t":"Ladies and gentlemen."},{"s":292.86,"e":295.45,"t":"Thank you all for coming on this sad occasion."},{"s":296.6,"e":304.45,"t":"Diana would be so pleased to know that she had so many good friends and indeed so many kind relatives."},{"s":305.53,"e":307.52,"t":"I'd like to say a special thank you."},{"s":308.02,"e":311.17,"t":"those who have made long journeys to be here."},{"s":311.83,"e":313.63,"t":"Our nephews from Australia."},{"s":314.2,"e":316.25,"t":"and our cousins from South Africa."},{"s":316.76,"e":319.52,"t":"who have made such an effort to be here today."}]},{"n":46,"q":"You hear five people talking about why they use the Internet. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi internetdan nima uchun foydalanishi haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about why they use the Internet","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"as a source of free entertainment","u":"bepul ko'ngilochar manba sifatida"},{"l":"B","t":"as a way of saving money","u":"pul tejash usuli sifatida"},{"l":"C","t":"for watching TV programmes they missed","u":"o'tkazib yuborgan teleko'rsatuvlarni ko'rish uchun"},{"l":"D","t":"for downloading books","u":"kitob yuklab olish uchun"},{"l":"E","t":"for communicating with people","u":"odamlar bilan muloqot uchun"},{"l":"F","t":"for making online purchases","u":"onlayn xarid qilish uchun"},{"l":"G","t":"to help with studies","u":"o'qishga yordam uchun"},{"l":"H","t":"as a way of making new friends","u":"yangi do'stlar orttirish usuli sifatida"}],"dur":202.9,"items":[{"a":"G","ps":2.84,"en":37.28,"ev":"I find it really useful to help me with school work, especially when we're doing geography or history projects.","uz":"U menga maktab ishlarida, ayniqsa geografiya yoki tarix loyihalarida juda foydali.","why":"O'qishga yordam (G).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":40.89,"en":79.42,"ev":"I'm addicted to my computer mainly as a way of keeping in touch with people… I haven't made any new friends like that.","uz":"Kompyuterga asosan odamlar bilan aloqada bo'lish uchun bog'lanib qolganman… Bu orqali yangi do'st orttirmaganman.","why":"Muloqot (E). Yangi do'stlar — rad etilgan (H tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":82.81,"en":127.1,"ev":"But at the moment mostly for buying things… I buy all kinds of things from websites.","uz":"Lekin hozir asosan narsa sotib olish uchun… Saytlardan har xil narsalar xarid qilaman.","why":"Onlayn xarid (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":130.55,"en":167.81,"ev":"I can't afford to pay, but I don't download anything that you're supposed to pay for.","uz":"Pul to'lashga qurbim yetmaydi, lekin pullik narsalarni yuklab olmayman.","why":"Bepul ko'ngilochar manba — musiqa (A).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":171.7,"en":200.12,"ev":"At the moment mainly catching up with programmes I couldn't watch first time round for some reason.","uz":"Hozir asosan biror sababdan birinchi marta ko'ra olmagan ko'rsatuvlarimni tomosha qilish uchun.","why":"O'tkazib yuborilgan teleko'rsatuvlar (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":2.84,"e":2.84,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":5.62,"e":11.52,"t":"I find it really useful to help me with school work, especially when we're doing geography or history projects."},{"s":12.02,"e":26.85,"t":"I know people of my parents' generation used to spend hours in the school or the town library finding the information they needed. My dad said the information was almost always out of date. The internet is fantastic. I've always found what I'm looking for."},{"s":27.32,"e":31.13,"t":"The only problem is that sometimes there's just too much stuff to get through."},{"s":31.67,"e":37.28,"t":"One of my friends said she'd once spent five hours looking for information. You've just got to know when to stop."},{"k":"h","s":40.89,"e":40.89,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":44.02,"e":51.26,"t":"I'm addicted to my computer mainly as a way of keeping in touch with people. It's just so easy to talk to your friends."},{"s":51.74,"e":58.91,"t":"At the moment, I'm chatting to my older brother who's in Thailand. He's told me incredible stories about what he's getting up to."},{"s":59.51,"e":62.85,"t":"It's almost as good as the phone, and it doesn't cost anything."},{"s":63.64,"e":68.38,"t":"I've started talking to a few people I don't know, but I haven't made any new friends like that."},{"s":68.98,"e":74.37,"t":"I think it's a bit scary. The idea that you can get to know someone like this and then call them your friend."},{"s":74.94,"e":79.42,"t":"You don't really know anything about these people. I mean, everything they say could be lies."},{"k":"h","s":82.81,"e":82.81,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":86.04,"e":92.64,"t":"I use it for various things. You know, the obvious ones like emailing, getting the latest news."},{"s":93.08,"e":95.77,"t":"but at the moment mostly for buying things."},{"s":96.38,"e":100.0,"t":"The thing is, I really don't enjoy going shopping in town anymore."},{"s":100.44,"e":105.47,"t":"It takes me half an hour to get there on the bus and the shops are always really crowded."},{"s":106.39,"e":113.89,"t":"I buy all kinds of things from websites like last week I bought a DVD, a new pair of jeans and some make up."},{"s":114.33,"e":121.63,"t":"It's so quick and easy. You just click on what you want, put it in your basket, go to the checkout and pay with your card."},{"s":122.2,"e":124.29,"t":"And most things don't take long to arrive."},{"s":124.79,"e":127.1,"t":"I said I'd show my brother how to do it tomorrow."},{"k":"h","s":130.55,"e":130.55,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":133.53,"e":143.52,"t":"Music definitely. It has to be music. That's about all I use it for really, apart from occasionally checking the sports results. It's fantastic if you're into music of any kind."},{"s":143.96,"e":150.72,"t":"I go on some of the music sites and download all kinds of music files straight to my smartphone. It's so easy these days."},{"s":151.16,"e":165.53,"t":"can't afford to pay but I don't download anything that you're supposed to pay for. I know some people do. The music industry is trying to crack down on the illegal downloading. They say they're losing sales because people aren't buying CDs anymore or paying for downloads."},{"s":166.07,"e":167.81,"t":"I reckon the fight in a losing battle."},{"k":"h","s":171.7,"e":171.7,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":175.06,"e":200.12,"t":"I use it for all kinds of stuff but at the moment mainly catching up with programs I couldn't watch first time round for some reason. It's incredibly useful to be able to do that. Most of them you can still get for up to a week after their first broadcast. The quality is not quite as good on my laptop but at least you don't have to wait for ages until they repeat the broadcast. And of course you can pause programs and fast forward them so you can avoid the adverts."}]},{"n":47,"q":"You hear five people talking about cars. What does each speaker say?","qu":"Besh kishi avtomobillar haqida gapiradi.","topic":"people talking about cars","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"the car can be left at home from time to time","u":"mashinani vaqti-vaqti bilan uyda qoldirish mumkin"},{"l":"B","t":"driving can be an enjoyable pastime","u":"mashina haydash yoqimli mashg'ulot bo'lishi mumkin"},{"l":"C","t":"cars on certain roads can lead to pedestrian deaths","u":"ayrim yo'llardagi mashinalar piyodalar o'limiga sabab bo'lishi mumkin"},{"l":"D","t":"driving can have a negative impact on lifestyle","u":"mashina haydash turmush tarziga salbiy ta'sir qilishi mumkin"},{"l":"E","t":"using the car cuts down on the daily commuting time","u":"mashinadan foydalanish har kungi yo'l vaqtini qisqartiradi"},{"l":"F","t":"public transportation is a priority","u":"jamoat transporti ustuvor bo'lishi kerak"}],"dur":493.8,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":60.6,"en":104.41,"ev":"Often, rush hour traffic passes through major city and urban centres, causing accidents, some of which have been fatal.","uz":"Ko'pincha tig'iz soatdagi transport katta shahar markazlaridan o'tib, baxtsiz hodisalarga sabab bo'ladi, ba'zilari o'lim bilan tugagan.","why":"Piyodalar o'limiga olib kelishi (C).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":108.02,"en":146.53,"ev":"When I bought my house, I made sure that it was accessible to public transport and close to all the essential things I need.","uz":"Uy sotib olganimda, uning jamoat transportiga yaqin bo'lishi va kerakli joylar yaqinida bo'lishiga ishonch hosil qildim.","why":"Jamoat transporti ustuvor (F).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":150.04,"en":188.99,"ev":"I had to work last weekend, so I took the car, and I was at the office in less than 15 minutes.","uz":"O'tgan dam olish kuni ishlashimga to'g'ri keldi, mashinani oldim va 15 daqiqa ichida ofisda edim.","why":"Kitob kaliti E — mashina yo'l vaqtini qisqartiradi. Mazmunan \"you don't need to use it every time\" (A) ham yaqin, lekin kitob javobi E.","hl":null},{"a":"B","ps":193.11,"en":227.2,"ev":"I think at the weekends it's a pleasure to drive around Dublin city, especially on a Sunday morning.","uz":"Dam olish kunlari, ayniqsa yakshanba ertalab Dublin bo'ylab mashina haydash zavq beradi deb o'ylayman.","why":"Yoqimli mashg'ulot (B).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":230.62,"en":270.21,"ev":"Cars can make people lazy. They can contribute to an unhealthy lifestyle.","uz":"Mashinalar odamlarni dangasa qilishi mumkin. Ular nosog'lom turmush tarziga hissa qo'shishi mumkin.","why":"Turmush tarziga salbiy ta'sir (D).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.54,"e":7.74,"t":"You will hear five different speakers talking about cars."},{"s":8.73,"e":12.89,"t":"Select the correct answer from the list to match correctly with the speaker."},{"s":14.14,"e":16.89,"t":"You cannot make the same selection more than once."},{"s":17.82,"e":21.05,"t":"Please note that there is three extra letters in the list."},{"s":21.5,"e":23.26,"t":"which you do not need to use."},{"s":23.74,"e":27.81,"t":"You now have 30 seconds to look at the answer list on the screen."},{"k":"h","s":60.6,"e":60.6,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":60.6,"e":68.96,"t":"I hate cars. They are noisy, cause pollution, are expensive to maintain, and cause problems for cyclists."},{"s":69.5,"e":74.46,"t":"I think they should be banned from the city and town centres across the country."},{"s":75.26,"e":79.71,"t":"It's time the roads and paths were given back to the pedestrians."},{"s":80.22,"e":81.95,"t":"It's also quite dangerous."},{"s":82.42,"e":90.88,"t":"Often, rush hour traffic passes through major city and urban centres, causing accidents, some of which have been fatal."},{"s":91.61,"e":93.09,"t":"Is there anything we can do?"},{"s":93.78,"e":104.41,"t":"Well, I am not sure. The car industry is very powerful, employs thousands of people and it's very difficult to persuade people to leave their car at home."},{"k":"h","s":108.02,"e":108.02,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":108.02,"e":127.93,"t":"I am terrified of cars. I don't drive and I won't even get into a car. There have been very few times in my life when I have absolutely needed to use a car. I am very lucky though because I live very close to the local train station and it takes me 20 minutes to get into town."},{"s":128.5,"e":146.53,"t":"I also live in close proximity to a major shopping centre that supplies me with all my needs. In fact, because I hate cars so much, when I bought my house, I made sure that it was accessible to public transport and close to all the essential things I need."},{"k":"h","s":150.04,"e":150.04,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":150.04,"e":166.49,"t":"I would never think of driving my car to work. The road to my office is choked with traffic every morning, from Monday to Friday. In fairness though, I had to work last weekend, so I took the car, and I was at the office in less than 15 minutes."},{"s":167.0,"e":171.42,"t":"I got all my work done by noon and was home by 12.30."},{"s":172.06,"e":183.1,"t":"Obviously the car has its advantages, especially for the weekly visit to the shops, or a drive in the country, or for that long weekend trip to somewhere nice."},{"s":183.8,"e":188.99,"t":"I think it's important to have a car, but you don't need to use it every time you go out."},{"k":"h","s":193.11,"e":193.11,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":193.11,"e":204.7,"t":"couldn't exist without a car. It's a lifesaver for me. I need it for work as I am a district nurse. At the weekends I use it to take my sick mother out for a drive into town."},{"s":205.24,"e":217.53,"t":"She loves to get out, but she is not good at walking because of an accident she had a few years ago. I find cars are safer these days. Most people are civilized on the road and follow the rules."},{"s":217.98,"e":227.2,"t":"I think at the weekends it's a pleasure to drive around Dublin city, especially on a Sunday morning when a lot of people are having a well deserved rest."},{"k":"h","s":230.62,"e":230.62,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":230.62,"e":239.55,"t":"It's faster to walk down to my local shop on a Sunday morning to get the newspaper than drive down, although my neighbour would probably disagree."},{"s":240.02,"e":242.81,"t":"I don't think I have ever seen him walk anywhere."},{"s":243.45,"e":245.15,"t":"Cars can make people lazy."},{"s":245.59,"e":251.13,"t":"They can contribute to an unhealthy lifestyle and are not good if you are trying to lose weight."},{"s":251.8,"e":263.68,"t":"One of the joys about Sunday mornings for me is walking the dog along the promenade, dropping into my favourite cafe for a skinny latte and a slow read of the weekend newspapers."},{"s":264.41,"e":270.21,"t":"Walking gives you a chance to think things out in a fresh environment. Driving doesn't."}]},{"n":48,"q":"You will hear people speaking about apologizing for something. What is the reason for each speaker's apology?","qu":"Odamlar biror narsa uchun uzr so'rashadi. Har birining uzr so'rash sababi nima?","topic":"speaking about apologizing for something","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"disturbing someone","u":"kimnidir bezovta qilish"},{"l":"B","t":"cancelling a theatre booking","u":"teatrdagi buyurtmani bekor qilish"},{"l":"C","t":"leaving something behind","u":"biror narsani qoldirib ketish"},{"l":"D","t":"forgetting to write something down","u":"biror narsani yozib qo'yishni unutish"},{"l":"E","t":"arriving very late","u":"juda kech kelish"},{"l":"F","t":"dropping something","u":"biror narsani tushirib yuborish"}],"dur":346.5,"items":[{"a":"E","ps":20.57,"en":46.56,"ev":"When I got to the bus stop there was a simply enormous queue… It never occurred to me you'd miss the first act.","uz":"Bekatga yetganimda juda uzun navbat bor edi… Birinchi pardani o'tkazib yuborishingni xayolimga ham keltirmagandim.","why":"Juda kech kelgan (E). Teatr — lekin bron bekor qilinmagan (B tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"C","ps":50.33,"en":80.25,"ev":"When I went away on holiday I was in such a hurry at the last minute that I took the wrong diary with me… It just completely slipped my mind.","uz":"Ta'tilga ketayotganimda so'nggi daqiqada shunchalik shoshdimki, noto'g'ri kundalikni olib ketibman… Butunlay esimdan chiqibdi.","why":"Kerakli kundalikni qoldirib ketgan (C).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":84.02,"en":113.37,"ev":"I always make a note of everything… It must be the first time this has happened. I hate being in debt.","uz":"Men hamma narsani doim yozib qo'yaman… Bu birinchi marta bo'lsa kerak. Qarzdor bo'lishni yomon ko'raman.","why":"Qarzni yozib qo'yishni unutgan (D).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":117.08,"en":144.77,"ev":"It just seemed to slip out of my hands as I was filling it with water.","uz":"Suv to'ldirayotganimda u qo'limdan sirg'alib ketdi shekilli.","why":"Vazani tushirib yuborgan (F).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":148.31,"en":176.96,"ev":"I did try and creep in very quietly… I'm extremely sorry. You had a sleepless night.","uz":"Juda sekin kirishga harakat qildim… Juda afsusdaman. Tuni bilan uxlay olmading.","why":"Bezovta qilgan (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":2.65,"e":6.75,"t":"You will hear five different people apologizing about something."},{"k":"h","s":20.57,"e":20.57,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":23.77,"e":34.49,"t":"I'm awfully sorry. I left home in plenty of time and when I got to the bus stop there was a simply enormous queue. Apparently a bus had broken down earlier and some people had been waiting for up to an hour."},{"s":35.03,"e":38.72,"t":"I couldn't contact you so I thought you'd just go in and not wait for me."},{"s":39.26,"e":41.41,"t":"It never occurred to me you'd miss the first act."},{"s":42.07,"e":46.56,"t":"You should have left a message at the box office because I had to pick up my ticket from there anyway."},{"k":"h","s":50.33,"e":50.33,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":53.4,"e":61.85,"t":"Trouble is I'm using two diaries, one for a day-to-day business and the other one for anniversaries and people's birthdays and so on."},{"s":62.49,"e":74.69,"t":"You know I've never forgotten before, but when I went away on holiday I was in such a hurry at the last minute that I took the wrong diary with me and I'm really sorry. It just completely slipped my mind."},{"s":75.61,"e":80.25,"t":"Anyway, I'll make it up to you and we'll go out to a concert or something next week."},{"k":"h","s":84.02,"e":84.02,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":87.13,"e":88.45,"t":"I don't understand this."},{"s":88.98,"e":97.25,"t":"I always make a note of everything. You know, bills, how much I've spent, how much I can save. Every month without fail."},{"s":97.94,"e":102.75,"t":"And it's all recorded in the back of my large desk diary, which I look at every day."},{"s":103.96,"e":105.15,"t":"do apologize."},{"s":105.62,"e":109.34,"t":"It must be the first time this has happened. I hate being in debt."},{"s":109.88,"e":113.37,"t":"I'll go and get my checkbook this very minute and pay you back now."},{"k":"h","s":117.08,"e":117.08,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":120.09,"e":126.72,"t":"I know it was one of your favorites. I'm most terribly sorry. I'll try and find another one, which is exactly the same."},{"s":127.61,"e":133.09,"t":"I've no idea how it happened. It just seemed to slip out of my hands as I was filling it with water."},{"s":134.01,"e":137.37,"t":"And I bought you these flowers especially to go in that bars."},{"s":137.91,"e":140.03,"t":"And now all I've done is upset you."},{"s":141.34,"e":142.49,"t":"Please stop crying."},{"s":143.22,"e":144.77,"t":"I promise I'll get you another one."},{"k":"h","s":148.31,"e":148.31,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":152.18,"e":153.73,"t":"no idea it was so late."},{"s":154.39,"e":157.53,"t":"And in any case, I did try and creep in very quietly."},{"s":158.3,"e":160.73,"t":"I even took my boots off before opening the front door."},{"s":161.46,"e":162.81,"t":"I don't know what else I could"},{"s":163.54,"e":164.93,"t":"I didn't put on any lights."},{"s":165.98,"e":168.45,"t":"tiptoed up the stairs and went straight to bed."},{"s":169.3,"e":172.32,"t":"I'm extremely sorry. You had a sleepless night."},{"s":172.92,"e":176.96,"t":"But as I say, I did my best not to make the slightest noise."}]},{"n":49,"q":"You will hear people speaking about being the eldest child in a family. What is the best thing each speaker remembers?","qu":"Odamlar oiladagi to'ng'ich farzand bo'lish haqida gapiradi. Har biri eng yaxshi nimani eslaydi?","topic":"speaking about being the eldest child in a family","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"feeling certain of oneself","u":"o'ziga ishonch his qilish"},{"l":"B","t":"not arguing with parents","u":"ota-ona bilan bahslashmaslik"},{"l":"C","t":"having parental attention","u":"ota-onaning e'tiborida bo'lish"},{"l":"D","t":"learning to be supportive","u":"boshqalarni qo'llab-quvvatlashni o'rganish"},{"l":"E","t":"being bought new clothes","u":"yangi kiyim olib berilishi"},{"l":"F","t":"enjoying special advantages","u":"alohida imtiyozlardan bahramand bo'lish"}],"dur":404.2,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":21.62,"en":63.01,"ev":"For the first few years of my life, I had my parents all to myself… I think that experience was very special.","uz":"Hayotimning dastlabki yillarida ota-onam butunlay menga tegishli edi… Bu juda o'zgacha tajriba edi.","why":"Ota-ona e'tibori (C).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":66.78,"en":90.85,"ev":"Being the eldest, there was nothing my parents could hand on to me and say, \"Right, you don't need a new sweater.\"","uz":"To'ng'ich bo'lganim uchun ota-onam menga hech narsani \"Mana, senga yangi sviter kerak emas\" deb bera olmasdi.","why":"Doim yangi kiyim olib berilgan (E).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":94.49,"en":125.79,"ev":"I used to love those little privileges… When you were allowed to stay up late, the younger ones had to go to bed early.","uz":"O'sha kichik imtiyozlarni juda yaxshi ko'rardim… Menga kech yotishga ruxsat berilardi, kichiklar esa erta yotishi kerak edi.","why":"Alohida imtiyozlar (F).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":129.43,"en":166.11,"ev":"And this early role of taking care of others is probably one of the reasons why I… am a caring person, generally.","uz":"Boshqalarga g'amxo'rlik qilishdagi bu erta rolim, ehtimol, umuman g'amxo'r inson bo'lishimning sabablaridan biri.","why":"Qo'llab-quvvatlashni o'rganish (D).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":169.88,"en":203.52,"ev":"I developed a confidence in being able to look after myself.","uz":"O'zimga o'zim qaray olishimga ishonch paydo bo'ldi.","why":"O'ziga ishonch (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":6.2,"e":11.45,"t":"You'll hear five different people talking about being the eldest child in a family."},{"k":"h","s":21.62,"e":21.62,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":24.86,"e":28.48,"t":"To be honest, I don't remember being jealous of my brother and sister."},{"s":29.18,"e":31.36,"t":"I think I was expected to come first."},{"s":31.86,"e":41.18,"t":"And I must have been in my late teens, around 17 or 18, before it occurred to me that my parents had to divide their time amongst the three of us."},{"s":42.04,"e":46.46,"t":"And I suppose I felt more irritated rather than jealous."},{"s":47.22,"e":49.98,"t":"I remember arguments about having to 'wait my turn'."},{"s":50.81,"e":53.73,"t":"But my sister wasn't born until I was almost six."},{"s":54.2,"e":58.3,"t":"So for the first few years of my life, I had my parents all to myself and..."},{"s":58.84,"e":63.01,"t":"I think that experience was very special and I'm really glad I was born first."},{"k":"h","s":66.78,"e":66.78,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":69.78,"e":87.52,"t":"I know our parents tried to treat us all the same, but I remember my younger brother and sister complaining about having to wear my second-hand jeans or trainers. And of course, being the eldest, there was nothing my parents could hand on to me and say, \"Right, you don't need a new sweater or whatever. You can wear John's old one.\""},{"s":88.02,"e":90.85,"t":"In that respect, I think the eldest child's very lucky."},{"k":"h","s":94.49,"e":94.49,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":97.59,"e":100.22,"t":"I used to love those little privileges, you know."},{"s":100.95,"e":104.86,"t":"When you were allowed to stay up late, the younger ones had to go to bed early."},{"s":105.5,"e":109.69,"t":"or if my parents had friends around for a meal and I was allowed to join them."},{"s":110.97,"e":114.37,"t":"And looking back now, I imagine I must have been a horrible older brother."},{"s":115.26,"e":120.7,"t":"I don't think it ever occurred to me to ask my parents to let my sisters share in some of the little treats."},{"s":121.46,"e":123.33,"t":"was only too pleased to have them all to myself."},{"s":124.18,"e":125.79,"t":"have been a very selfish child."},{"k":"h","s":129.43,"e":129.43,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":132.76,"e":137.25,"t":"I clearly remember wanting to know if my parents liked me best."},{"s":137.94,"e":143.65,"t":"I used to look after my younger brother and sister and hope that my parents would be pleased with me."},{"s":144.41,"e":148.35,"t":"I think I hoped that they would favour me above the younger children."},{"s":149.3,"e":153.89,"t":"I enjoyed pleasing them and having that feeling of satisfaction."},{"s":154.62,"e":166.11,"t":"And this early role of taking care of others is probably one of the reasons why I enjoy taking responsibility for things that need doing and being a caring person, generally."},{"k":"h","s":169.88,"e":169.88,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":173.34,"e":179.52,"t":"I think my parents were so busy looking after my younger brothers and sisters that I was given quite a lot of freedom."},{"s":180.06,"e":186.17,"t":"So I became independent at a very early age and went off at weekends and did my own thing."},{"s":186.87,"e":198.11,"t":"I used to disappear for the whole day with my friends, cycling, camping, canoeing. And although I didn't realise it at the time, I developed a confidence in being able to look after myself."},{"s":199.16,"e":203.52,"t":"I wasn't the least bit worried about moving away from home and living by myself."}]},{"n":50,"q":"You will hear people speaking about jobs. What job does each speaker talk about?","qu":"Odamlar kasblar haqida gapiradi. Har biri qaysi kasb haqida?","topic":"speaking about jobs","opts":[{"l":"A","t":"singer","u":"qo'shiqchi"},{"l":"B","t":"disco owner","u":"diskoteka egasi"},{"l":"C","t":"farmer","u":"fermer"},{"l":"D","t":"teacher","u":"o'qituvchi"},{"l":"E","t":"artist","u":"rassom"},{"l":"F","t":"restaurant owner","u":"restoran egasi"}],"dur":409.1,"items":[{"a":"C","ps":16.12,"en":49.89,"ev":"If the weather was awful it could affect the crop so badly that of course your income suffered.","uz":"Agar ob-havo yomon bo'lsa, hosilga shunchalik ta'sir qilardiki, albatta daromad ham kamayardi.","why":"Hosil, ob-havo — fermer (C).","hl":null},{"a":"E","ps":53.91,"en":91.74,"ev":"Hoping your work will be noticed, that someone will see something that you've done hanging on a wall… dragging your stuff around various galleries.","uz":"Ishingiz e'tiborga tushishiga, devorda osilgan biror asaringizni kimdir ko'rishiga umid qilish… ishlaringizni galereyalarma-galereya olib yurish.","why":"Galereyalar, devordagi asar — rassom (E).","hl":null},{"a":"D","ps":95.58,"en":130.14,"ev":"I can understand why she's attracted to education and there always seem to be plenty of jobs going, there'd always be kids.","uz":"Nega uning ta'limga qiziqishini tushunaman, ish o'rinlari doim ko'p — bolalar har doim bo'ladi.","why":"Ta'lim, bolalar — o'qituvchi (D). Tibbiyot — ota-onaning orzusi (tuzoq).","hl":null},{"a":"A","ps":133.98,"en":162.17,"ev":"Constantly packing and unpacking, loading up all your gear and maybe staying every night in a different place… she's so good, and audiences love her.","uz":"Doim yuk yig'ish va yechish, jihozlarni ortish va har kecha boshqa joyda qolish… u juda zo'r, tomoshabinlar uni yaxshi ko'radi.","why":"Gastrollar, tomoshabinlar — qo'shiqchi (A).","hl":null},{"a":"F","ps":166.04,"en":203.81,"ev":"He's a big name. Hardly ever goes near a hot stove, although he's the brains behind some of the most imaginative dishes.","uz":"U mashhur odam. Issiq plitaga deyarli yaqinlashmaydi, lekin eng ajoyib taomlarning muallifi.","why":"Taomlar, xodimlar — restoran egasi (F).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"s":4.06,"e":7.58,"t":"You will hear five different people talking about jobs."},{"k":"h","s":16.12,"e":16.12,"t":"Speaker 1"},{"s":19.48,"e":23.39,"t":"What really impressed me about him was the incredibly long hours that he was prepared to work."},{"s":23.99,"e":28.7,"t":"And it wasn't as if he earned loads of money either. In fact, I think there were times when he had to struggle."},{"s":29.24,"e":30.81,"t":"particularly when the children were young."},{"s":31.58,"e":35.68,"t":"getting up very early in the morning, which in winter must have been pretty disagreeable."},{"s":36.34,"e":38.94,"t":"working quite late at night if there were any problems"},{"s":39.9,"e":44.29,"t":"And then if the weather was awful it could affect the crop so badly that of course your income suffered."},{"s":45.11,"e":49.89,"t":"may have spent three years at college, but they don't teach you what to do about controlling the weather, do they?"},{"k":"h","s":53.91,"e":53.91,"t":"Speaker 2"},{"s":57.08,"e":62.05,"t":"I can see the attraction of not working for an employer and in being your own boss."},{"s":62.71,"e":81.28,"t":"But I wouldn't fancy the insecurity, you know, waiting for the phone to ring, wondering if anyone's ever going to ask you to do anything ever again, and then hoping your work will be noticed, that someone will see something that you've done hanging on a wall and say, \"Oh, where did you get that?\" And so your name gets mentioned."},{"s":81.82,"e":91.74,"t":"Or even worse, dragging your stuff around various galleries, watching the owners look through it and finally say, \"No, sorry. Not quite what our customers like.\""},{"k":"h","s":95.58,"e":95.58,"t":"Speaker 3"},{"s":98.84,"e":103.17,"t":"I suppose years ago a university degree was a passport to almost any job but..."},{"s":103.77,"e":105.02,"t":"I'm not so sure now."},{"s":105.69,"e":109.69,"t":"Most employers want experience these days before you can get anything worthwhile."},{"s":111.51,"e":130.14,"t":"I can understand why she's attracted to education and there always seem to be plenty of jobs going, there'd always be kids. And although I wish she'd gone on to study medicine, it's much better paid. If that's what she wants to do, then who am I to say no? But it's going to be quite a tough life."},{"k":"h","s":133.98,"e":133.98,"t":"Speaker 4"},{"s":137.14,"e":145.85,"t":"I remember being quite envious of people like her. I had friends whose parents were in the business and got to travel all over the world. It seemed very glamorous."},{"s":146.84,"e":148.51,"t":"Guess it must get quite exhausting."},{"s":149.27,"e":155.26,"t":"Constantly packing and unpacking, loading up all your gear and maybe staying every night in a different place."},{"s":155.77,"e":158.88,"t":"If you want to get married and have a family it must be really difficult."},{"s":159.67,"e":162.17,"t":"But then she's so good, and audiences love her."},{"k":"h","s":166.04,"e":166.04,"t":"Speaker 5"},{"s":169.37,"e":173.31,"t":"It's a good life if you're successful, but then that applies to most things."},{"s":174.36,"e":182.43,"t":"I think it must be hard work building up the business in the early years. You've got to be willing to work all hours and do whatever's necessary."},{"s":183.19,"e":187.81,"t":"I know someone whose staff were always letting him down and never turning up on time."},{"s":188.54,"e":190.88,"t":"I think at one stage she almost gave up."},{"s":191.32,"e":193.63,"t":"He was doing everything single handed."},{"s":194.65,"e":203.81,"t":"It's very different now, of course. He's a big name. Hardly ever goes near a hot stove, although he's the brains behind some of the most imaginative dishes."}]}];
